ig.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THURSDAY PUZZLE — It’s very hard to be an objective judge of a puzzle when the theme affects you personally, so I’ll just admit that Ben Tausig’s puzzle struck me right in the heart. And it’s not just because it manages to pull off a really neat constructing trick called a Schrödinger theme (described below), but also because I have a young adult child who happens to be GENDER FLUID. And this concept of gender existing on a continuum instead of a binary (male or female only) is the theme of our crossword puzzle today.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/01/crosswords/01wordplay-surfer/01wordplay-surfer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/01/crosswords/01wordplay-surfer/01wordplay-surfer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/01/crosswords/01wordplay-surfer/01wordplay-surfer-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/01/crosswords/01wordplay-surfer/01wordplay-surfer-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/01/crosswords/01wordplay-surfer/01wordplay-surfer-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/01/crosswords/01wordplay-surfer/01wordplay-surfer-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, '