vibe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sure, the “Full House” meets “ALF” mash-up sequence from two episodes ago got the most ink. (Understandably!) But when it comes to painstaking recreations of outmoded aesthetics, the show’s slasher parody “The Careful Massacre of the Bourgeoisie” is clearly the retro Rosetta stone for “Mr. Robot.” While no one was murdered onscreen, this week’s episode carried over its predecessor’s horror-movie vibe, and then some. Flickering lights, dark hallways, doppelgängers, menacing knocks at the door, a generalized sense of impending doom: “eps2.7_init_5.fve” was about as creepy as you can get without a serial killer or supernatural entity stalking the cast.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/31/watching/31robot2/31robot2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/31/watching/31robot2/31robot2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/31/watching/31robot2/31robot2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/31/watching/31robot2/31robot2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/31/watching/31robot2/31robot2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/31/watching/31robot2/31robot2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'c