t nation out of a deepening fiscal crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRASÍLIA — Brazilians booed him as he presided over the opening of the Olympics in Rio. He has been accused of taking bribes. The economy he is supposed to rescue is on the cusp of a depression.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Impeachment Over, Brazil’s Next Challenge Is Its Flailing Economy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Impeachment Over, Brazil’s Next Challenge Is Its Flailing Economy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romero, Simon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Impeachment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brazilian Democratic Movement Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Temer, Michel (1940- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rousseff, Dilma', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bribery and Kickbacks', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Workers' Party (Brazil)", 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-01T09:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simon Romero', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Romero', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a6f0646-475b-5fa9-b41c-1d65ba63d5d7', 'word_count': 943, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a6f0646-475b-5fa9-b41c-1d65ba63d5d7'}, {'abstract': 'Nothing defines China’s hottest days more than the Beijing Bikini: grown men, without a hint of shame, rolling up shirts to expose often generous bellies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/02/world/what-in-the-world/china-summer-beijing-bikini.html', 'snippet': 'Nothing defines China’s hottest days more than the Beijing Bikini: grown men, without a hint of shame, rolling up shirts to expose often generous bellies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Summer on the streets of Chinese cities yields a panoply of exotic sights and sounds: old men loudly jousting over mah-jongg tiles, sidewalk barbecues grilling tough-to-identify animal parts, and the unmistakable growl of a clearing throat — that ends with an inevitable splat.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/01/world/wit-beijingbikini1/wit-beijingbikini1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/01/world/wit-beijingbikini1/wit-beijingbikini1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/01/world/wit-beijingbikini1/wit-beijingbikini1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/01/world/wit-beijingbikini1/wit-beijingbikini1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/01/world/wit-beijingbikini1/wit-beijingbikini1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/0