8f218c3f-3dae-5539-b069-7052beea2c6e'}, {'abstract': 'From the archives of The International Herald Tribune: Japan seeks peace with the U.S. in September 1941.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/09/01/1941-japan-seeks-peace-with-u-s/', 'snippet': 'From the archives of The International Herald Tribune: Japan seeks peace with the U.S. in September 1941.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKIO — As the European war enters its third year, Japan has abandoned hope of an early termination of the conflict. A feeling of having been let down by German promises of a quick conclusion was noticeable here today. The Japanese have become aware of the necessity of adopting ‘‘realistic’’ diplomacy instead of ‘‘idealistic.’’ The announcement that Japan is negotiating with the United States for a settlement of Far Eastern issues has created a problem for the government from the point of view of public peace and order. — New York Herald Tribune, Sept. 2, 1941', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1941: Japan Seeks Peace With U.S.', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-01T15:17:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dbe4237f-d775-5df8-b90d-c3a7251cac0c', 'word_count': 96, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dbe4237f-d775-5df8-b90d-c3a7251cac0c'}, {'abstract': 'From the archives of The International Herald Tribune: The U.S. Office of Education struggles with desegregation guidelines enforcement in September 1966.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/09/01/1966-desegregation-in-trouble/', 'snippet': 'From the archives of The International Herald Tribune: The U.S. Office of Education struggles with desegregation guidelines enforcement in September 1966.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MONTGOMERY — As public schools prepare to reopen, it is increasingly clear that the U.S. Office of Education has serious enforcement problems with desegregation guidelines throughout the Deep South. Resistance to the guidelines has been so strong in hard-core segregationist areas that in a great majority of cases the Education Office has accepted token compliance rather than invoke Title 6 of the 1964 Civil Rights Act and withdraw federal assistance. As a result, more than 96 percent of some 1,500,000 Negro pupils in Alabama, Georgia, Mississippi, Louisiana and South Carolina will be attending all-Negro schools as they return to classes. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Sept. 2, 1966', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1966: Desegregation in Trouble', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Segregation and Desegregation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'UNITED STATES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-01T15:18:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '