nce, for a Good Cause', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Denny', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'VH1 Save the Music Foundation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Festivals', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fire Island (NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sagaponack (NY)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hamptons (NY)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-01T20:41:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Denny Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Denny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85f76e12-afa4-5519-813d-eecda07b3bd1', 'word_count': 81, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85f76e12-afa4-5519-813d-eecda07b3bd1'}, {'abstract': 'Though a strong dollar and lower oil prices constrained August manufacturing, labor market strength could push the Fed closer to raising interest rates.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/02/business/economy/factory-activity-dips-but-economic-growth-seems-promising.html', 'snippet': 'Though a strong dollar and lower oil prices constrained August manufacturing, labor market strength could push the Fed closer to raising interest rates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON (Reuters) — Factory activity contracted in August for the first time in six months as new orders and production tumbled, the Institute for Supply Management said on Thursday, but a low level of layoffs continued to point to a pickup in economic growth in the third quarter.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Factory Activity Dips, but Economic Growth Seems Promising', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Activity Dips at Factories, but Signs Say Growth', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Institute for Supply Management', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Labor Department (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-01T20:49:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b5edb55-2ff6-5761-a792-c922df02be53', 'word_count': 409, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b5edb55-2ff6-5761-a792-c922df02be53'}, {'abstract': 'This film, directed by Luke Scott (whose father is Ridley Scott), focuses on a girl who is pale and fast, strong and hungry.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/02/movies/morgan-review.html', 'snippet': 'This film, directed by Luke Scott (whose father is Ridley Scott), focuses on a girl who is pale and fast, strong and hungry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'That “Morgan” is a movie about genetics is somehow appropriate, given that the origins of its director, Luke Scott, will be an inescapable component of any discussion of its merits. Unveiling a first feature seems stressful enough; but when your father is peeking over your shoulder as one of the producers, and he’s none other than Ridley Scott — who, with “Alien” and “Blade Runner,” gave us two of the most m