successors and books.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When it comes to jewels, there are Taylor-Burton rocks and discreet heirloom stones. With museum shows, it’s the same. “Hans Memling: Portraiture, Piety and a Reunited Altarpiece,” at the Morgan Library & Museum, is a minute but invaluable gem of some two dozen small paintings, drawings and books set in the Morgan’s Clare Eddy Thaw gallery, known as the Cube for its intimate size.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/02/arts/02MEMLING2/02MEMLING2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/02/arts/02MEMLING2/02MEMLING2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/02/arts/02MEMLING2/02MEMLING2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/02/arts/02MEMLING2/02MEMLING2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 417, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/02/arts/02MEMLING2/02MEMLING2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 417}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/02/arts/02MEMLING2/02MEMLING2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 711, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/02/arts/02MEMLING2/02MEMLING2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1041, 'width': 1499, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Hans Memling Show Is More Than the Sum of Its Divine Parts', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'More Than the Sum of Its Divine Parts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cotter, Holland', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Memling, Hans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Morgan Library & Museum', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-01T21:23:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holland Cotter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holland', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cotter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f931ef3d-4a9e-5960-9267-1183af693394', 'word_count': 1249, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f931ef3d-4a9e-5960-9267-1183af693394'}, {'abstract': '“Cartoon Memoirs,” at the Museum of the City of New York, exhibits the mind-to-hand connection in about 200 of Ms. Chast’s wacky creations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/02/arts/design/why-roz-chast-makes-fun-of-white-middle-class-new-yorkers.html', 'snippet': '“Cartoon Memoirs,” at the Museum of the City of New York, exhibits the mind-to-hand connection in about 200 of Ms. Chast’s wacky creations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A cartoon by the brilliant, widely beloved visual humorist Roz Chast has the title “Einsteins on the Beach” drawn above a family of three camped out on the shore: Dad, listening to the gurgling coming from his wristwatch, remarks, “Guess I shouldn’t have worn my Rolex.” Mom, sitting in a beach chair and observing a large, transparent bag of food on the blanket at her feet, reflects, “Maybe it’s time to move the sandwiches out of the sun.” Their young daughter, emptying a bag of snacks onto the sand, says, “I wonder if sea gulls like Cheez Doodles.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/02/arts/02ROZ/02ROZ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/02/arts/02ROZ/02ROZ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/02/arts/02ROZ/02ROZ-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/02/arts/02ROZ/02ROZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/02/arts/02ROZ/02ROZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/02/arts/02ROZ/02ROZ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/02/arts/02ROZ/02ROZ-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Roz Chast Makes Fun of White Middle-Class New Yorkers', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Making Fun of White Middle-Class New Yorkers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cartoons and Cartoonists', 'rank': 1, 'maj