r', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/02775c34-0171-56dc-bfb7-5503eee31f88', 'word_count': 3790, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02775c34-0171-56dc-bfb7-5503eee31f88'}, {'abstract': 'Six destinations that can be reached by ferry and foot.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/02/arts/design/no-subway-no-buses-no-uber-no-problem.html', 'snippet': 'Six destinations that can be reached by ferry and foot.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WE were trapped beneath the heat dome — the air like soup, the sun relentless — with no escape. But as my son, Spencer, and I set off by ferry toward Randalls Island in late July, something like relief swept over us. A faint breeze squeezed through an open window and then stiffened as the boat motored north on the East River. And if I closed my eyes and succumbed to the water’s rhythm, I was almost transported out of this urban toaster oven and onto a Caribbean island or maybe a Pacific atoll.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/02/arts/02FERRIES/02FERRIES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 421, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/02/arts/02FERRIES/02FERRIES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 421}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/02/arts/02FERRIES/02FERRIES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 718, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/02/arts/02FERRIES/02FERRIES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1436, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'cred