 'snippet': 'The organic version will be made up of seven ingredients, will come in lemon, strawberry and mixed berry flavors and will be sold in select markets this fall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gatorade, the brightly colored sports drink marketed by professional sports figures in advertising targeted at amateur athletes, is introducing an organic version.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/01/business/00xp-gatorade_web1/00xp-gatorade-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/01/business/00xp-gatorade_web1/00xp-gatorade-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/01/business/00xp-gatorade_web1/00xp-gatorade-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/01/business/00xp-gatorade_web1/00xp-gatorade-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/01/business/00xp-gatorade_web1/00xp-gatorade-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 710}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/01/business/00xp-gatorade_web1/00xp-gatorade-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 692, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/01/business/00xp-gatorade_web1/00xp-gatorade-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 692, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gatorade Shakes Up the Sport Drink by Going Organic', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Organic Version of Gatorade Is Coming This Fall', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gatorade Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Energy and Sports Drinks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pepsico Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organic Foods and Products', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-02T14:06:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Mele', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mele', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dbcfbc12-dd39-5d20-aad0-f4f91a9ea501', 'word_count': 775, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dbcfbc12-dd39-5d20-aad0-f4f91a9ea501'}, {'abstract': 'From the archives of The International Herald Tribune: The Bank of England suffers fraud in September 1891.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/09/02/1891-fraud-at-the-bank-of-england/', 'snippet': 'From the archives of The International Herald Tribune: The Bank of England suffers fraud in September 1891.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For some days persistent rumors have been in the air of a colossal fraud said to have been perpetrated on the Bank of England. On Monday the amount alleged to have been stolen was currently given as £250,000, and since then the sum has advanced by leaps and bounds, until today it was confidently asserted in the City that it amounted to half a million. These rumors have obtained a degree of credence in banking circles which calls for authoritative treatment. There is no truth whatever in the report, which, if well founded, would have startled the commercial world, and must have produced results disastrous to the largest interests. The Governor of the Bank of England states that there is absolutely no foundation for the rumors. The story, it appears, arose as follows: It will be remembered that in February last a counter robbery was effected at the Bank of Scotland. Certain of the securities then stolen have been within the last few days presented for payment in Paris, and in one of the Paris papers an announcement appeared confusing the Bank of Scotland with the Bank of England, and stating the amount of the frauds to have been £250,000. — The New York Herald, European Edition, Sept. 3, 1891 ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1891: Fraud at the Bank of England', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank of England', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-02T14:07:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5409f15d-5010-5227-bc54-3c92438101f5', 'word_count': 211, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5409f15d-5010-5227-bc54-3c92438101f5'}, {'abstract': 'From the archives of The International Herald Tribune: President Sukarno compares himself to Jesus Christ and Mohammed in September 1966.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/09/02/1966-sukarno-likens-self-to-christ/', 'snippet': 'From the archives of The International Herald Tribune: President Sukarno compares himself to Jesus Christ and Mohammed in September 1966.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DJAKARTA — Comparing himself to Mohammed and Christ, President Sukarno said today [Sept. 2] that he would go on speaking his mind. The president, who has been stripped of most of his powers, was replying to the criticism which has been leveled at him for his speeches contradicting stated government policy. ‘‘Mohammed also made speeches all the time,’’ he declared. Challenging those who criticized hero worship and the personality cult in Indonesia, Mr. Sukarno said it was necessary to worship something. He asked what would happen to Islam and Christianity without worship of Mohammed and Christ, then added; ‘‘I want Indonesia to have a hero the Indonesians can be proud of.’’ — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Sept. 3, 1966', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/03/blogs/03oldiht-1966-sukarno/03oldiht-1966-sukarno-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 444, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/03/blogs/03oldiht-1966-sukarno/03oldiht-1966-sukarno-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 444}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/03/blogs/03oldiht-1966-sukarno/03oldiht-1966-sukarno-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/03/blogs/03oldiht-1966-sukarno/03oldiht-1966-sukarno-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', '