://article/f54e1558-419b-59d5-8b06-7474297d34db'}, {'abstract': 'A by-no-means-exhaustive list of items we like.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/02/t-magazine/dr-gross-radiance-booster-apc-outdoor-voices-loewe-francis-lights-friends.html', 'snippet': 'A by-no-means-exhaustive list of items we like.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I am not, nor have I ever been, a Serum Person. Serums just always seemed to be a thing people liked to say they use in order to appear fancy and well groomed. That was until I tried Dr. Gross’s “Radiance Booster” — housed in a little orange bottle that, I was sure when I purchased it, would not make me more radiant. But as I’ve used the serum in my morning routine (either applying it before moisturizer or mixing it into my makeup), it has surprisingly delivered on its promise. I’ve been told how radiant I look — even though, no, I didn’t just come back from summer vacation. $68, drdennisgross.com. — ISABEL WILKINSON', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/02/t-magazine/02tmag-thingseditorslike-slide-MR5M/02tmag-thingseditorslike-slide-MR5M-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/02/t-magazine/02tmag-thingseditorslike-slide-MR5M/02tmag-thingseditorslike-slide-MR5M-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/02/t-magazine/02tmag-thingseditorslike-slide-MR5M/02tmag-thingseditorslike-slide-MR5M-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/02/t-magazine/02tmag-thingseditorslike-slide-MR5M/02tmag-thingseditorslike-slide-MR5M-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 204