r those who are sick.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/04/nyregion/the-sunday-routine-of-koshin-paley-ellison-monk-and-zen-teacher.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Paley Ellison of the New York Zen Center for Contemplative Care in Chelsea believes that it is a privilege to care for those who are sick.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2007, Koshin Paley Ellison and Robert Chodo Campbell founded the New York Zen Center for Contemplative Care, a nonprofit in Chelsea that offers meditation training and study programs for medical professionals and caregivers. Since then, they and their students have worked with over 80,000 people. Dr. Paley Ellison, co-editor of the new book “Awake at the Bedside: Contemplative Teachings on Palliative and End-of-Life Care,” lives on the Upper West Side with Mr. Campbell, who is also his husband, and two Maine coon cats.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/04/nyregion/04ROUTINE1sub/04ROUTINE1sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/04/nyregion/04ROUTINE1sub/04ROUTINE1sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/04/nyregion/04ROUTINE1sub/04ROUTINE1sub-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/04/nyregion/04ROUTINE1sub/04ROUTINE1sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 469, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/04/nyregion/04ROUTINE1sub/04ROUTINE1sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 469}}, {'rank': 0,