change Commission’s recent decision to throw in the towel in its civil case against Daniel H. Mudd, the chief executive of Fannie Mae in the go-go years immediately preceding the crisis, helps explain why.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why No Punishment for Financial Executives? Fannie Mae Is Case Study', 'kicker': 'Another View', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal National Mortgage Assn (Fannie Mae)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mudd, Daniel H', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-02T16:46:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Zaring', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zaring', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd755bf2-dafd-59e4-99c6-d77904868246', 'word_count': 754, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd755bf2-dafd-59e4-99c6-d77904868246'}, {'abstract': 'The Brooklyn Public Library has announced its first official cultural season, which also features Patti Smith and Medea Benjamin.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/03/books/jonathan-safran-foer-oliver-stone-javier-marias-brooklyn-public-library.html', 'snippet': 'The Brooklyn Public Library has announced its first official cultural season, which also features Patti Smith and Medea Benjamin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The days when Brooklyn meant “baseball, boredom and bad breath,” to quote a d