85-20ff-5894-8c10-2ce34e76744c', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/cada5085-20ff-5894-8c10-2ce34e76744c'}, {'abstract': 'Alibaba’s mobile-payment affiliate and a private-equity firm will buy part of Yum’s China unit for a good price, but the deal may also pay off for Yum.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/03/business/dealbook/yum-brands-in-china-adds-owners-with-skill-and-connections.html', 'snippet': 'Alibaba’s mobile-payment affiliate and a private-equity firm will buy part of Yum’s China unit for a good price, but the deal may also pay off for Yum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yum Brands has added some spice at a price. The company, which owns KFC and Pizza Hut, is selling part of its China business to Alibaba’s mobile-payments affiliate and a private-equity firm run by Fred Hu, the former chairman of Goldman Sachs China. They bring valuable technology skill and connections. It is a better deal than usual for so-called cornerstone investors, but may pay off for Yum’s coming spinoff.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yum Brands in China Adds Owners With Skill and Connections', 'kicker': 'Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Owners Add Skill and Connections Yum’s Menu in China', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fast Food Industry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ant Financial Services Group', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'China Investment Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kentucky Fried Chicken', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yum Brands Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ma, Jack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-02T21:03:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By K