, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-09-02T22:42:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b741dd7e-f80b-5495-9499-2b91f6263502', 'word_count': 37, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b741dd7e-f80b-5495-9499-2b91f6263502'}, {'abstract': 'When the results finally were announced, a curious set of returns from one province — the incumbent’s — gave him the slimmest of victories over me.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/05/opinion/save-gabon-from-election-fraud.html', 'snippet': 'When the results finally were announced, a curious set of returns from one province — the incumbent’s — gave him the slimmest of victories over me.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Saturday, Aug. 27, presidential elections were held in my country, Gabon, in West Africa, and I was the candidate who won by a substantial vote margin. Nearly a week later, I would have expected to be addressing the world as Gabon’s president-elect, ready and willing to work with the United States and all our international partners to fight terrorism, build our economies and improve the lives of our citizens through increased development and cooperation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Save Gabon From Election Fraud', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Save Gabon From Election Fraud', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gabon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 4,