rial': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/3474922c-86f2-5b70-b830-7e7444001a58', 'word_count': 921, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3474922c-86f2-5b70-b830-7e7444001a58'}, {'abstract': 'Conservative donors have seized on campus debates to push their belief in free markets, not in free speech.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/04/opinion/sunday/political-correctness-and-its-real-enemies.html', 'snippet': 'Conservative donors have seized on campus debates to push their belief in free markets, not in free speech.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW HAVEN — Last November, Scott C. Johnston, a 1982 Yale graduate, was attending a conference organized by the William F. Buckley Jr. Program at his alma mater when student protesters disrupted it. Soon after, he watched an online video of a black Yale student hurling imprecations at a professor who headed her residential college for failing “to create a place of comfort and home.”', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/04/opinion/sunday/04sleeper/04sleeper-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 409, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/04/opinion/sunday/04sleeper/04sleeper-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 409}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/04/opinion/sunday/04sleeper/04sleeper-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 698, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/04/opinion/sunday/04sleeper/04sleeper-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1396, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/04/opinion/sunday/04sleeper/04sleeper-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/04/opinion/sunday/04sleeper/04sleeper-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/04/opinion/sunday/04sleeper/04sleeper-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Political Correctness and Its Real Enemies', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'God and Brand at Yale', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sleeper, Jim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservatism (US Politics)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bradley, Lynde and Harry, Foundation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Buckley, William F Jr, Program', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Foundation for Individual Rights in Education', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Intercollegiate Studies Institute Inc', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yale University', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'God and Man at Yale (Book)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-03T18:30:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Sleeper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sleeper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/a66095e3-a81c-57d5-b2a2-a616ae72b6da', 'word_count': 912, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a66095e3-a81c-57d5-b2a2-a616ae72b6da'}, {'abstract': 'Do not ever say he was lucky that he did not feel pain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/04/opinion/sunday/how-to-tell-a-mother-her-child-is-dead.html', 'snippet': 'Do not ever say he was lucky that he did not feel pain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Philadelphia — First you get your coat. I don’t care if you don’t remember where you left it, you find it. If there was a lot of blood you ask someone to go quickly to the basement to get you a new set of scrubs. You put on your coat and you go into the bathroom. You look in the mirror and you say it. You use the mother’s name and you use her child’s name. You may not adjust this part in any way.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/04/opinion/sunday/04rosenberg/04rosenberg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/04/opinion/sunday/04rosenberg/04rosenberg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/04/opinion/sunday/04rosenberg/04rosenberg-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/04/opinion/sunday/04rosenberg/04rosenberg-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 550, 'width': 420, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/04/opinion/sunday/04rosenberg/04rosenberg-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 550, 'width': 420, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Tell a Mother Her Child Is Dead', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How to Tell a Mother Her Child Is Dead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emergency Medical Treatment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-03T18:30:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Naomi Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Naomi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/101d87af-8013-5cde-91ce-3a5fed5feeb4', 'word_count': 854, 'uri': 'nyt://article/101d87af-8013-5cde-91ce-3a5fed5feeb4'}, {'abstract': 'In many countries, the number of deaths during pregnancy or after childbirth has fallen sharply. The United States is a glaring exception.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/04/opinion/sunday/americas-shocking-maternal-deaths.html', 'snippet': 'In many countries, the number of deaths during pregnancy or after childbirth has fallen sharply. The United States is a glaring exception.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The rate at which women die during pregnancy or shortly after childbirth has fallen sharply in many nations as maternal care has improved. The United States — and particularly Texas — is a glaring exception.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail'