nging the coup plotters to justice.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/05/world/05SUMMIT/05SUMMIT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/05/world/05SUMMIT/05SUMMIT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/05/world/05SUMMIT/05SUMMIT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/05/world/05SUMMIT/05SUMMIT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 353, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/05/world/05SUMMIT/05SUMMIT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 353}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/05/world/05SUMMIT/05SUMMIT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 602, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/05/world/05SUMMIT/05SUMMIT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1204, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Before G-20, Obama Tries to Smooth Things Over With Turkey', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama Meets Erdogan in an Effort to Patch Up Differences With Turkey', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Landler, Mark', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Erdogan, Recep Tayyip', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kurds', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Group of Twenty', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-04T15:35:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c929a92-74ec-5122-82fa-93cbc1024d27', 'word_count': 520, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c929a92-74ec-5122-82fa-93cbc1024d27'}, {'abstract': 'The United States decision to lift an arms embargo has empowered the regime to intensify its political repressions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/05/opinion/letter-from-a-bahraini-jail.html', 'snippet': 'The United States decision to lift an arms embargo has empowered the regime to intensify its political repressions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RIFFA, Bahrain — I write this from a Bahraini jail cell where I have been detained, largely in isolation, since the beginning of summer. This is not new to me: I have been here before, from 2012 to 2014, in 2015, and now again, all because of my work as a human rights defender.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Letter From a Bahraini Jail', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Letter from a Bahraini jail', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bahrain'