olicy and defeated on the left as well.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/06/world/europe/merkel-vows-to-stay-on-course-despite-german-election-setback.html', 'snippet': 'The German leader’s party placed third in state elections, beaten on the right over her refugee policy and defeated on the left as well.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — A day after voters in Chancellor Angela Merkel’s political home state delivered what amounted to a strong rejection of her refugee policy, the German leader acknowledged on Monday that she was “very dissatisfied” with the result but insisted that she would stick with her chosen course.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Merkel Vows to Stay on Course Despite Party Setback', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Merkel Promises to Stay on Course Despite Setback in State Elections in Germany', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merkel, Angela', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Alternative for Germany', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Christian Democratic Union (Germany)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Christian Social Union (Germany)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and Africa Migrant Crisis', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-05T14:49:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alison Smale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0416104a-94fe-5dd7-ad02-5d6fcb05a774', 'word_count': 870, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0416104a-94fe-5dd7-ad02-5d6fcb05a774'}, {'abstract': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: China’s foreign population is outraged over the country’s tardiness to punish the Wusueh murders perpetrators in September 1891.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/09/05/1891-wusueh-outrages-in-china/', 'snippet': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: China’s foreign population is outraged over the country’s tardiness to punish the Wusueh murders perpetrators in September 1891.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — A Wuchang correspondent, writing on August 3 to the North China News, which has just been received here by mail, says the patience of the foreign population is well nigh exhausted by the tardiness of the Chinese officials in punishing the perpetrators of the Wusueh outrages. On the second batch of offenders, eight in number, who were convicted of murder, assault and pillage, sentences of penal servitude for life, banishment for life, or branding on the face or back were imposed. — The New York Herald, European Edition, Sept. 6, 1891', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1891: Wusueh Outrages in China', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-05T14:58:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_ma