vil rights movement in the South and helped embolden Congress to ban racial discrimination in voting — died on Aug. 30 in Selma. He was 81.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/06/us/06hoggle/06hoggle-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 492, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/06/us/06hoggle/06hoggle-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 492}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/06/us/06hoggle/06hoggle-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 839, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/06/us/06hoggle/06hoggle-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1678, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/06/us/06hoggle/06hoggle-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/06/us/06hoggle/06hoggle-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/06/us/06hoggle/06hoggle-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Namon Hoggle, 81, Accused in a Civil Rights Killing, Is Dead', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Namon O’Neal Hoggle, 81, Is Dead; Acquitted in a Civil Rights Killing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights Movement (1954-68)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reeb, James (1927-65)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Selma (Ala)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "Hoggle, Namon O'Neal (1934-2016)", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-05T22:08:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b1c592e-90f9-53f2-8a28-9c250789fd9a', 'word_count': 1218, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b1c592e-90f9-53f2-8a28-9c250789fd9a'}, {'abstract': 'In the 1980s, Korita regularly served over 140 miles per hour in an era when that was unheard of. And power, he says, is about more than size and strength.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/06/sports/tennis/eric-korita-power-serve-q-and-a.html', 'snippet': 'In the 1980s, Korita regularly served over 140 miles per hour in an era when that was unheard of. And power, he says, is about more than size and strength.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the 1980s, the most powerful serve in tennis belonged to Eric Korita. He never achieved the overall success of his big-serving predecessor Roscoe Tanner or successors like Mark Philippoussis or Ivo Karlovic. Korita’s highest world ranking was 30th in doubles and 46th in singles, but he regularly served faster than 140 miles per hour in an era when that was unheard of. Korita will be at the United States Open, giving a clinic on serving, for The New York Times on Facebook Live on Tuesday at 1 p.m. First, he shared some thoughts on his biggest weapon.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q. and A.: Eric Korita Shares the Keys to a Power Serve', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Korita, Eric (1963- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-05T22:11:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/211d7b77-15a2-5934-9b80-75280ce7a784', 'word_count': 592, 'uri': 'nyt://article/211d7b77-15a2-5934-9b80-75280ce7a784'}, {'abstract': 'New York Times reporters answered readers’ questions about the George Washington Bridge scandal in a live online discussion on Wednesday, Sept. 7, 2016.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2016/09/07/nyregion/bridgegate-christie-scandal-reader-question-and-answer.html', 'snippet': 'New York Times reporters answered readers’ questions about the George Washington Bridge scandal in a live online discussion on Wednesday, Sept. 7, 2016.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York Times reporters answered readers’ questions about the George Washington Bridge scandal in a live online discussion on Wednesday, Sept. 7, 2016.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/03/nyregion/BRIDGEGATEPROMO2/BRIDGEGATEPROMO1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/03/nyregion/BRIDGEGATEPROMO2/BRIDGEGATEPROMO1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 