 trips throughout Mexico.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Alex Webb first walked across the bridge from El Paso to Ciudad Juárez, Mexico, in 1975, he was a 23-year-old hotshot photographer. He had just become a nominee to the esteemed Magnum photo collective and was already noted for his alienated black-and-white images capturing the American social landscape.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Capturing Complexity and Color in Mexico', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Light and Heat of Mexicou2019s Sublime and Visceral Streets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Webb, Alex', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'APERTURE FOUNDATION', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-06T07:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Estrin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Estrin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f41a329a-b1f6-51f4-bdbd-d7a43e8d4fdc', 'word_count': 451, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f41a329a-b1f6-51f4-bdbd-d7a43e8d4fdc'}, {'abstract': 'Hillary Clinton and Donald J. Trump enter the final nine weeks of a U.S. presidential campaign that has defied the expectations of both the American electorate and international observers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/07/world/americas/united-states-trump-clinton.html', 'snippet': 'Hillary Clinton and Donald J. Trump enter the final nine weeks of a U.S. presidential campaign that has defied the expectations of both the American electorate and international 