 and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN HISTORICAL ASSN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-06T07:21:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ec74c6f-ca48-5362-80f1-f4a110da008e', 'word_count': 677, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ec74c6f-ca48-5362-80f1-f4a110da008e'}, {'abstract': 'For Republicans opposed to Trump, sitting out the election or supporting a third-party candidate are a coward’s game.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/06/opinion/save-the-republican-party-vote-for-clinton.html', 'snippet': 'For Republicans opposed to Trump, sitting out the election or supporting a third-party candidate are a coward’s game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every day, I run into Republican friends who can’t stomach a vote for Donald J. Trump but don’t know what to do. Vote for Hillary Clinton, who has trouble with the truth, wants to raise taxes and opposes free trade with Asia? Vote for the Libertarian candidate, Gary Johnson, an outlier who once ran a marijuana business and embraces isolationism? Or not vote at all, maintaining a certain purity but allowing others to decide the next president?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/03/opinion/06glassmanWeb/06glassmanWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/03/opinion/06glassmanWeb/06glassmanWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/03/opinion/06glassmanWeb/06glassmanWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/03/opinion/06glassmanWeb/06glassmanWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/03/opinion/06glassmanWeb/06glassmanWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/03/opinion/06glassmanWeb/06glassmanWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/03/opinion/06glassmanWeb/06glassmanWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Save the Republican Party: Vote for Clinton', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The G.O.P. Needs You: Vote Clinton', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Glassman, James K', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Third-Party Politics (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-06T07:21:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Campaign Stops', 'byline': {'original': 'By James K. Glassman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'K.', 'lastname': 'Glassman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/853fcfcf-a77f-5409-a0d7-aa545f368fbb', 'word_count': 832, 'uri': 'nyt://article/853fcfcf-a77f-5409-a0d7-aa545f368fbb'}, {'abstract': 'John MacKenzie was a model prisoner for more than 40 years, but after 10 denials of parole he realized the only way out was to kill himself.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/06/opinion/false-hope-and-a-needless-death-behind-bars.html', 'snippet': 'John MacKenzie was a model prisoner for more than 40 years, but after 10 denials of parole he realized the only way out was to kill himself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On July 26, John MacKenzie went before the parole board at the Fishkill Correctional Facility in Beacon, N.Y., and made the case, once again, for his freedom. He had been locked up since 1975 for shooting and killing a Long Island police officer, Matthew Giglio, during a bungled robbery attempt. His sentence was 25 years to life — the maximum under state law.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/06/opinion/06tue3web/06tue3web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/06/opinion/06tue3web/06tue3web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/06/opinion/06tue3web/06tue3web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/06/opinion/06tue3web/06tue3web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'sub