article/629cb2d1-32ee-5736-a9b5-5fe869bc41d4'}, {'abstract': 'The N.S.A. may have crucial evidence that could solve the mystery of the United Nations leader’s 1961 death.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/07/opinion/release-the-records-on-dag-hammarskjolds-death.html', 'snippet': 'The N.S.A. may have crucial evidence that could solve the mystery of the United Nations leader’s 1961 death.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Last month, the outgoing secretary general of the United Nations, Ban Ki-moon, published a memo following up the inquiry he instigated last year into the death, nearly 55 years ago, of one of his predecessors in the role, the Swedish diplomat Dag Hammarskjold. Hammarskjold perished, along with his entourage, just after midnight on Sept. 18, 1961, when his chartered airliner crashed near Ndola, in what was then Northern Rhodesia, now Zambia.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Release the Records on Dag Hammarskjold’s Death', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Release the Records on Dag Hammarskjold’s Death', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hammarskjold, Dag', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aviation Accidents, Safety and Disasters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-06T11:31:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Sedley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sedley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/6525c895-6059-50c9-8110-4340842ef194', 'word_count': 929, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6525c895-6059-50c9-8110-4340842ef194'}, {'abstract': 'Senator Sam Dastyari apologized 