-officer-is-fired-a-year-after-fatal-shooting-of-south-carolina-teenager.html', 'snippet': 'Lt. Mark Tiller had opened fire during a drug sting in Seneca, killing Zachary Hammond, an unarmed white teenager, in 2015.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A South Carolina police lieutenant who fatally shot a 19-year-old man during an attempted drug arrest in a Hardee’s parking lot last year has been fired from his job, the police chief said. The officer contended that he was acting in self-defense when the suspect drove a car toward him.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Police Officer Is Fired a Year After Fatal Shooting of South Carolina Teenager', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'South Carolina Officer Who Killed Teenager in a 2015 Drug Sting Is Fired', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hammond, Zachary (1996-2015)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tiller, Mark (1982- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Seneca (SC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State, The (Newspaper)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Michael (1996-2014)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ferguson (Mo)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-06T14:25:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/28e8a6e3-e621-5e04-9594-2608a47622aa', 'word_count': 624, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28e8a6e3-e621-5e04-9594-2608a47622aa'}, {'abstract': 'Britain and the United States have stonewalled requests by Ban Ki-moon to divulge information on the plane crash that killed his predecessor in 1961.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/07/world/europe/dag-hammarskjold-death-ban-ki-moon.html', 'snippet': 'Britain and the United States have stonewalled requests by Ban Ki-moon to divulge information on the plane crash that killed his predecessor in 1961.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — A few days from now, the anniversary of one of the most enduring international mysteries will slide by, hardly likely to be marked by those in Britain and the United States accused of withholding the secret clues to its resolution.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/07/world/07Letter-web1/07Letter-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 388, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/07/world/07Letter-web1/07Letter-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 388}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/07/world/07Letter-web1/07Letter-web1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 663, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/07/world/07Letter-web1/07Letter-web1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1325, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/07/world/07Letter-web1/07Letter-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/07/world/07Letter-web1/07Letter-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/07/world/07Letter-web1/07Letter-web1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'U.N. Chief Presses to Unlock Mystery of Dag Hammarskjold’s Death', 'kicker': 'Letter From Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hammarskjold, Dag', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ban Ki-moon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aviation Accidents, Safety and Disasters', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-06T14:53:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Cowell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01c34884-dd52-5da9-9857-2d01d1f1942f', 'word_count': 677, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01c34884-dd52-5da9-9857-2d01d1f1942f'}, {'abstract': 'Peña and Murphy are willing to do whatever is necessary to get Escobar, no matter the damage to their integrity or their souls.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/04/arts/television/narcos-season-2-episode-5-recap.html', 'snippet': 'Peña and Murphy are willing to do whatever is necessary to get Escobar, no matter the damage to their integrity or their souls.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s an absurd sequence in “The Enemies of My Enemy” that can at least be salvaged as metaphor. With Col. Horacio Carrillo, the leader of Search Bloc, out of the picture, the official operation to capture or kill Pablo Escobar has not only lost the tip of its spear, but it also barely has a stick left for poking. The D.E.A. agents continue to gather information and surveillance, but protocol keeps them chained to their desks, compiling folders of classified information without anyone to act on the intelligence. And yet, remarkably, there’s a shot of Peña entering Carrillo’s office and delivering the documents anyway, like an old habit he hasn’t thought to break. Enter Murphy’s voice-over narration, lamenting that the hunt for Escobar had been reduced to “a growing stack of unread files on a dead man’s desk.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/02/watching/02narcos5/02narcos5-thumbStandard-v9.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/02/watching/02narcos5/02narcos5-thumbStandard-v9.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/02/watching/02narcos5/02narcos5-thumbLarge-v9.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/02/watching/02narcos5/02narcos5-articleLarge-v7.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/02/watching/02narcos5/02narcos5-articleLarge-v7.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': Non