t a ‘Brecession'” So says Business Insider, now that good UK PMI surveys have caused Credit Suisse and Morgan Stanley to back off their forecasts of a Brexit-induced recession.", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thinking About Brexit, Fast and Slow', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-09-07T02:07:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd1b366b-47b7-5d4e-a3e9-b1ab4d465e3a', 'word_count': 199, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd1b366b-47b7-5d4e-a3e9-b1ab4d465e3a'}, {'abstract': 'A South Carolina native, who liked to call herself a “culinary griot,” she was heard on NPR for three decades. She also was an author, an actress and a singer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/07/arts/vertamae-smart-grosvenor-dies-at-79-celebrated-gullah-food-and-culture-on-npr.html', 'snippet': 'A South Carolina native, who liked to call herself a “culinary griot,” she was heard on NPR for three decades. She also was an author, an actress and a singer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Vertamae Smart-Grosvenor, who in a life of varied artistic careers, most notably as a commentator on NPR, was best known for extolling the virtues of the Gullah food and culture of her native South Carolina, died on Saturday in the Bronx. She was 79.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/07/arts/07grosvenor-obit/07grosvenor-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail