 'lead_paragraph': 'First there were the reports in Greenville County, S.C., of creepy clowns offering children money to come into the woods. There was also the mysterious late-night sighting of a clown waving under a streetlight.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/07/us/07xp-clowns/07xp-clowns-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/07/us/07xp-clowns/07xp-clowns-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/07/us/07xp-clowns/07xp-clowns-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/07/us/07xp-clowns/07xp-clowns-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/07/us/07xp-clowns/07xp-clowns-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/07/us/07xp-clowns/07xp-clowns-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/07/us/07xp-clowns/07xp-clowns-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Creepy Clown Reports Continue, and Clowns Are Not Happy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Clowns', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Winston-Salem (NC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-07T14:54:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Mele', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mele', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/868cbe65-afc6-55e6-be0e-01460bd8e530', 'word_count': 785, 'uri': 'nyt://article/868cbe65-afc6-55e6-be0e-01460bd8e530'}, {'abstract': 'Work inspired by Kazuo Ohno and Tatsumi Hijikata will be presented on Sept. 16 and 17.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/11/arts/dance/recalling-butoh-pioneers-at-japan-society.html', 'snippet': 'Work inspired by Kazuo Ohno and Tatsumi Hijikata will be presented on Sept. 16 and 17.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One day, the Japanese dancer Takao Kawaguchi had a vision. “It suddenly popped into my head: I want to become Kazuo Ohno,” he recalled. Ohno, who died in 2010 at 103, was internationally celebrated as a founder of the emotionally intense dance form known as Butoh. Mr. Kawaguchi never saw Ohno perform, although Ohno danced past the age of 100, presenting solos in which he played both female and male roles. Mr. Kawaguchi eventually took vintage films of two of Ohno’s most famous solos, “My Mother” and “Admiring La Argentina,” which honors a great Spanish dancer, and duplicated them phrase by phrase with his own body.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/arts/11GUIDE7/11GUIDE7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1098, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/11/arts/11GUIDE7/11GUIDE7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1098}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/arts/11GUIDE7/11GUIDE7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 560, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/arts/11GUIDE7/11GUIDE7-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1120, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/arts/11GUIDE7/11GUIDE7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/11/arts/11GUIDE7/11GUIDE7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/arts/11GUIDE7/11GUIDE7-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Recalling Butoh Pioneers, at Japan Society', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dance; Two Salutes to Butoh Pioneers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kawaguchi, Takao', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'About Kazuo Ohno (Dance)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Japan Society', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Big Dance Theater', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parson, Annie B', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lazar, Paul', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-07T14:54:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Anderson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Anderson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1acd4826-ecad-5312-989c-a2e5f0cfda8f', 'word_count': 156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1acd4826-ecad-5312-989c-a2e5f0cfda8f'}, {'abstract': 'With her fragile yet commanding voice and barbed lyrics, this singer-songwriter from Richmond, Va., will hold forth at the Bowery Ballroom.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/11/arts/music/lucy-dacus-hopscotching-from-wounded-to-wounding.html', 'snippet': 'With her fragile yet commanding voice and barbed lyrics, this singer-songwriter from Richmond, Va., will hold forth at the Bowery Ballroom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lucy Dacus, a 21-year-old singer and songwriter based in Richmond, Va., makes indie rock sound urgent again by never rushing toward catharsis. On her precocious debut album, “No Burden” (recently reissued by Matador after a smaller independent release earlier this year), even the fuzzy, full-band stomps build like the ballads: Release comes only when Ms. Dacus has laid the foundation for emotional wreckage. With a fragile yet commanding voice and barbed lyrics that move between wounded and wounding, Ms. Dacus shares a skeptical wit with Will Toledo, her fellow Matador signee and current tour mate, who performs as Car Seat Headrest. Ms. Dacus, though, has teeth sharpened by the realities of being a woman. “Daddy told you to stay indoors,” she sings on “Troublemaker Doppelgänger.” “And I can understand how a girl gets bored/too old to play and too young to mess around.” (Thursday, Sept. 15, and Friday at the Bowery Ballroom; boweryballroom.com.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 