e': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d06a90ee-d7f6-5a74-bf25-375fdf3527e4', 'word_count': 164, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d06a90ee-d7f6-5a74-bf25-375fdf3527e4'}, {'abstract': 'A free concert will be held in a venue that used to look out on the twin towers, and a faculty recital kicks off a season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/11/arts/music/a-sept-11-memorial-at-bargemusic-and-a-juilliard-faculty-show.html', 'snippet': 'A free concert will be held in a venue that used to look out on the twin towers, and a faculty recital kicks off a season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bargemusic, the popular floating concert hall docked near the Brooklyn Bridge, is an especially poignant place for a Sept. 11 memorial. The twin towers used to be visible through the picture windows behind the small stage in this intimate space. This year’s free memorial program presents the violinist Mark Peskanov; the pianist and composer David Bottoms; the String Orchestra of Brooklyn; and others in works by Bach, Barber, Beethoven and more. (Sunday, Sept. 11, at 4 p.m., Fulton Ferry Landing, Brooklyn, 800-838-3006; bargemusic.org.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/arts/11GUIDE8/11GUIDE8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/11/arts/11GUIDE8/11GUIDE8-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 768}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/arts/11GUIDE8/11GUIDE8-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 801, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/arts/