': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d5f3e9c-3f8b-521f-8b7d-de08b82ce552', 'word_count': 652, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d5f3e9c-3f8b-521f-8b7d-de08b82ce552'}, {'abstract': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: Hundreds are roped in during a boxing event in London in September 1916.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/09/07/1916-hundreds-of-slackers-roped-in/', 'snippet': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: Hundreds are roped in during a boxing event in London in September 1916.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The boxing entertainment at the Ring, Blackfriars road, on Tuesday afternoon [Sept. 5] came to an abrupt conclusion. Three thousand persons were present, and the well-ordered and scientific pummelling was in full swing when a force of military and police, acting under the orders of the recruiting authorities, took possession of the building. Of the thousands who thronged the hall the majority were young men, sturdy, athletic and well trained. They tried to bolt, but all the exits were strongly guarded. A number gained the roof and tried to escape through the skylights. A few jumped into the street — in every case into the arms of a policeman. About 300 men were escorted to Southwark Police Station to give a satisfactory account of themselves, and wounded soldiers in the street cheered loudly. — The New York Herald, European Edition, Sept. 8, 1916', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/08/blogs/08oldiht-1916-menoflondon/08oldiht-1916-menoflondon-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 645, 'width': 527, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/08/blogs/08oldiht-1916-menoflondon/08oldiht-1916-menoflondon-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 645, 'width': 527, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/08/blogs/08oldiht-1916-menoflondon/08oldiht-1916-menoflondon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/08/blogs/08oldiht-1916-menoflondon/08oldiht-1916-menoflondon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/08/blogs/08oldiht-1916-menoflondon/08oldiht-1916-menoflondon-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1916: Hundreds of Slackers Roped In', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boxing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-07T15:33:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9293523-639d-5a00-9b72-e8de4c1863a7', 'word_count': 145, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9293523-639d-5a00-9b72-e8de4c1863a7'}, {'abstract': 'Once a 15-acre swath of gritty streets, parking lots and vacant buildings, North Shaw is the latest residential, retail and creative hub in the district.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/11/travel/five-places-to-go-in-washington-dc.html', 'snippet': 'Once a 15-acre swath of gritty streets, parking lots and vacant buildings, North Shaw is the latest residential, retail and creative hub in the district.', 'lead_paragraph': 'North Shaw is popping as a vibrant urban landscape with new shops and restaurants and more in mid-construction. Formerly a 15-acre swath known for gritty streets, parking lots, vacant buildings and chain-link fences, it’s the latest residential, retail and creative hub in the nation’s capital. On warm nights now, crowds pack the outdoor tables of tasteful restaurants on the wide sidewalks near the intersection of Florida Avenue and Eighth Street Northwest; street murals by local artists brighten building facades; and posters promote sumo wrestling and free henna tattoos.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/travel/11SURFACING6SUB/11SURFACING6SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/11/travel/11SURFACING6SUB/11SURFACING6SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/travel/11SURFACING6SUB/11SURFACING6SUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/travel/11SURFACING6SUB/11SURFACING6SUB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1535, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/travel/11SURFACING6SUB/11SURFACING6SUB-thumbStandard.jpg