nesday morning warning journalists to avoid offering up their own political opinions through Twitter, Facebook or other social media. The standards editor, Phil Corbett, says no particular incident prompted the note.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Leave the Editorializing to Our Colleagues on the Opinion Side’', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-07T16:29:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Public Editor', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Spayd', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spayd', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b52eff5-df07-57bf-9fbf-ff6a7522de2c', 'word_count': 308, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b52eff5-df07-57bf-9fbf-ff6a7522de2c'}, {'abstract': 'No, it’s not “The Notebook.” It’s real life. And it’s terrifying and wonderful all at once.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/09/fashion/mens-style/how-a-man-falls-in-love.html', 'snippet': 'No, it’s not “The Notebook.” It’s real life. And it’s terrifying and wonderful all at once.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In those miserable, wonderful days when love is new, when your heart pounds and your breath comes short and sharp, the only thing that matters is your beloved. News of the outside world comes as a rumor. Daily life is a melodrama, a musical, a rom-com, an epic.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/09/fashion/09MALEANIMAL1/09MALEANIMAL1-articleLa