aph': 'GALISTEO, N.M. — Squirrels had chewed through the internet cables, and cell service is never very good this far from Santa Fe, half an hour out on the sparsely inhabited high desert. So the artist Bruce Nauman had few distractions, which is the way he has liked it for more than 30 years, since moving to rural New Mexico from Los Angeles, away from an art world that has coveted him with an ardor he seems to need to hold at arm’s length.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/arts/11NAUMAN/11NAUMAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 675, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/11/arts/11NAUMAN/11NAUMAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 675}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/arts/11NAUMAN/11NAUMAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 911, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/arts/11NAUMAN/11NAUMAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1079, 'width': 959, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/arts/11NAUMAN/11NAUMAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/11/arts/11NAUMAN/11NAUMAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/arts/11NAUMAN/11NAUMAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headlin