ning Joe,” Mr. Johnson, the Libertarian Party candidate, indicated that he really was not aware of the Syrian city engulfed in civil war.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/09/us/politics/gary-johnson-aleppo.html', 'snippet': 'On “Morning Joe,” Mr. Johnson, the Libertarian Party candidate, indicated that he really was not aware of the Syrian city engulfed in civil war.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gary Johnson, the former New Mexico governor and Libertarian Party presidential nominee, revealed a surprising lack of foreign policy knowledge on Thursday that could rock his insurgent candidacy when he could not answer a basic question about the crisis in Aleppo, Syria.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘What Is Aleppo?’ Gary Johnson Asks, in an Interview Stumble', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘What Is Aleppo?’ Libertarian Presidential Candidate Asks in an Interview Stumble', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Gary E', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALEPPO (SYRIA)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Libertarian Party (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MSNBC', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-08T13:07:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Rappeport', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rappeport', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/178ae94b-023b-54a1-bf16-0c08307ea0f5', 'word_count': 665, 'uri': 'nyt://article/178ae94b-023b-54a1-bf16-0c08307ea0f5'}, {'abstract': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: The Egyptian Supreme Court sentences communists in Cairo in September 1966.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/09/08/1966-cairo-sentences-communists/', 'snippet': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: The Egyptian Supreme Court sentences communists in Cairo in September 1966.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — The Supreme State Security Court today sentenced eight pro-Peking communists to prison terms ranging from life to five years at hard labor on charges of plotting to overthrow the government and establish an ‘‘Egyptian People’s Republic.’’ The court sentenced the general secretary of the Egyptian Communist Party, Mustafa Agha, to life imprisonment with hard labor and also ordered the dissolution of the party and confiscation of its funds. Three defendants were acquitted, including army Col. Hamed Mustafa Daoud. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Sept. 9, 1966', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1966: Cairo Sentences Communists', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Communism (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Supreme Courts (State)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cairo (Egypt)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-08T13:08:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of