onference on Thursday on an airport tarmac in New York, one night after a presidential forum on national security issues.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/09/us/politics/hillary-clinton-highlights.html', 'snippet': 'Hillary Clinton took questions at a news conference on Thursday on an airport tarmac in New York, one night after a presidential forum on national security issues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hillary Clinton took questions at a news conference on an airport tarmac in New York on Thursday, one night after a presidential forum on national security issues.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Highlights of Hillary Clinton’s News Conference', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-08T13:47:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Flegenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flegenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3e31699-83d6-5e50-825d-2a3c833ad779', 'word_count': 351, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3e31699-83d6-5e50-825d-2a3c833ad779'}, {'abstract': 'Putin won’t trust anyone — except the people whose literal job is keeping him safe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/09/opinion/how-do-you-get-to-be-a-governor-in-vladimir-putins-russia.html', 'snippet': 'Putin won’t trust anyone — except the people whose literal job is keeping him safe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW According to Aleksei Diumin, it happened late one night, far from Moscow. He was standing guard at a presidential palace where Vladimir V. Putin was sleeping. A bear approached. “He and I looked each other in the eyes,” Mr. Diumin told a Russian newspaper. Then the bear backed away slightly. “I opened the door and emptied my gun’s entire clip at his feet.” The bear retreated. Russia’s president was safe.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/08/opinion/08kashin/08kashin-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 535, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/08/opinion/08kashin/08kashin-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 535}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/08/opinion/08kashin/08kashin-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 914, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/08/opinion/08kashin/08kashin-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1827, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/08/opinion/08kashin/08kashin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/08/opinion/08kashin/08kashin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/08/opinion/08kashin/08kashin-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Do You Get to Be a Governor in Vladimir Putin’s Russia?', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Becoming a governor in Putin’s Russia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-08T13:55:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Oleg Kashin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Oleg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kashin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/a080cfbb-9e13-5186-8a63-af45a04d9437', 'word_count': 849, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a080cfbb-9e13-5186-8a63-af45a04d9437'}, {'abstract': 'Tebow, 29, a former Heisman Trophy winner and N.F.L. quarterback, is now listed as an outfielder and expected to report to the Mets’ instructional league on Sept. 19.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/09/sports/baseball/tim-tebow-mets.html', 'snippet': 'Tebow, 29, a former Heisman Trophy winner and N.F.L. quarterback, is now listed as an outfielder and expected to report to the Mets’ instructional league on Sept. 19.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When word trickled out last month that Tim Tebow hoped to embark on a professional baseball career, Mets General Manager Sandy Alderson wanted in on the joke.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/09/sports/09tebow-web/09tebow-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 421, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/09/sports/09tebow-web/09tebow-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 421}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/09/sports/09tebow-web/09tebow-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/09/sports/09tebow-web/09tebow-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1208, 'width': 1721, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/09/sports/09tebow-web/09tebow-web-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/09/sports/09tebow-web/09tebow-web-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/09/sports/09tebow-web/09tebow-web-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tim Tebow Signs Minor League Deal With Mets', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'All Kidding Aside, Alderson and Mets Sign Tebow to Minor League Deal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tebow, Tim', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Witz, Billy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Baseball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minor Leagues', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-08T13:58:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Billy Witz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Billy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Witz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d738fa0-c999-52c9-be03-614f976be9a5', 'word_count': 980, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d738fa0-c999-52c9-be03-614f976be9a5'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Black will bring his red-hot temper to the Marquis Theater in a new show, “Black to the Future.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/11/theater/lewis-black-broadway.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Black will bring his red-hot temper to the Marquis Theater in a new show, “Black to the Future.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lewis Black is probably best known for his comedic rants on “The Daily Show,” which he has done during the tenure of all three of its hosts, dating back to Craig Kilborn. But Mr. Black also has a long history in the theater, both writing (including a short work produced at Ensemble Studio Theater) and performing (in New York as well as at the Williamstown Theater Festival, where he has appeared many times). While his trademark fury is the same, he presents a richer and more varied performance live, one that shows off his many shades of red-hot anger. His new show, “Black to the Future,” arrives on Broadway on Monday, Sept. 12, and considering the impending election, he should have plenty to vent about. (Marquis Theater; 877-250-2929, marquistheatre.com.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/arts/11GUIDE3/11GUIDE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/11/arts/11GUIDE3/11GUIDE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/arts/11GUIDE3/11GUIDE3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xl