 {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lehmann Maupin Gallery', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Paris Opera Ballet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-08T18:55:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Art', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Wilkinson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilkinson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40007c79-6c36-5d2d-99cc-d8bf71f9c1fe', 'word_count': 340, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40007c79-6c36-5d2d-99cc-d8bf71f9c1fe'}, {'abstract': 'It would have made sense for Jaguar Land Rover to borrow the architecture from the Evoque or Range Rover Sport, but the F-Pace is all Jag.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/09/automobiles/autoreviews/video-review-the-f-pace-crossover-keeps-its-jaguar-dna.html', 'snippet': 'It would have made sense for Jaguar Land Rover to borrow the architecture from the Evoque or Range Rover Sport, but the F-Pace is all Jag.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jaguar has produced beautiful sedans, coupes and convertibles over the years. The F-Pace is the first crossover from the formidable team of Jaguar’s design director, Ian Callum. Its largely aluminum skin is a fetching compilation of curves that somehow manages to evoke the F-Type coupe, a machine with no prayer of carrying a family.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/02/automobiles/autoreviews/driven-jaguar-f-pace/driven-jaguar-f-pace-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 347, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/02/automobiles/