riginal': 'By Tom Voelk', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Voelk', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6409b42c-6bdb-5ea6-92a2-e85095c62455', 'word_count': 713, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6409b42c-6bdb-5ea6-92a2-e85095c62455'}, {'abstract': 'Shane Gabier said PJ Harvey “is the closest thing I have to an idol or hero.” Here’s how to get the look she inspired for the brand’s spring 2017 show.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/08/t-magazine/fashion/creatures-of-the-wind-red-lip-fashion-week-beauty.html', 'snippet': 'Shane Gabier said PJ Harvey “is the closest thing I have to an idol or hero.” Here’s how to get the look she inspired for the brand’s spring 2017 show.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I love a really hard, drawn-on lip,” the makeup artist Mark Carrasquillo said this morning, backstage at Creatures of the Wind. For the brand’s spring/summer 2017 show, he created a fiery red shade that paid tribute to the rebellious ’90s spirit of the indie-rock musician PJ Harvey — his technique mirroring what you might actually do if you only had five minutes to prep in a van before a show. He quickly defined the mouth with the Nars Velvet Lip Pencil in Dragon Girl — a bright red that, he says, “every girl I know wears” — then tapped on Nars Coeur Battante fuchsia blush (a limited-edition shade that’s in tight circulation; try blush in Exhibit A for a close match), creating a matte effect that’s “a little sicker and more rock and roll.” Of the two-step application, Carrasquillo said, “It’s an old-school trick that I learned back in the ’80s when they didn’t have matte lipstick. You had to powder the lip to get that texture.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/08/t-magazine/fashion/08tmag-bbr-01/08tmag-bbr-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 899, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/08/t-magazine/fashion/08tmag-bbr-01/08tmag-bbr-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 899}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/08/t-magazine/fashion/08tmag-bbr-01/08tmag-bbr-01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 684, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/08/t-magazine/fashion/08tmag-bbr-01/08tmag-bbr-01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1367, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/08/t-magazine/fashion/08tmag-bbr-01/08tmag-bbr-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/08/t-magazine/fashion/08tmag-bbr-01/08tmag-bbr-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/08/t-magazine/fashion/08tmag-bbr-01/08tmag-bbr-01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Indie Rocker Behind Creatures of the Wind’s Fiery Red Lip', 'kicker': 'Backstage Beauty Report', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cosmetics and Toiletries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Creatures of the Wind (Fashion Label)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-08T18:56:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 