': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/09/movies/for-the-love-of-spock-review.html', 'snippet': 'Adam Nimoy’s documentary about his father nimbly straddles biography and “Star Trek” valentine, but also recounts the fraught but devoted ties between father and son.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the outset of his documentary “For the Love of Spock,” the director Adam Nimoy (son of Leonard Nimoy) imparts its origins. He intended to examine his father’s “Star Trek” character, Mr. Spock, and his place in culture for that franchise’s 50th anniversary. But in February 2015, Leonard Nimoy died, and the project became more of a tribute to his life. This film nimbly straddles biography and “Trek” valentine (Adam is a longtime television director), but also recounts the fraught if ultimately devoted ties between Adam and Leonard.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/09/arts/09FORLOVESPOCK/09FORLOVESPOCK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 353, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/09/arts/09FORLOVESPOCK/09FORLOVESPOCK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 353}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/09/arts/09FORLOVESPOCK/09FORLOVESPOCK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 602, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/09/arts/09FORLOVESPOCK/09FORLOVESPOCK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1199, 'width': 2039, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/09/arts/09FORLOVESPOCK/09FORLOVESPOCK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 