pe': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Comedy Listings for Sept. 9-15', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Listings: Comedy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-08T22:06:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/a13ffc4d-4e76-5ed3-ba22-f3b1882c8f7a', 'word_count': 689, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a13ffc4d-4e76-5ed3-ba22-f3b1882c8f7a'}, {'abstract': 'A modern ghost story haunted by the Holocaust, this film by the Polish director Marcin Wrona reconceptualizes the Jewish mythology of the dybbuk.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/09/movies/demon-review.html', 'snippet': 'A modern ghost story haunted by the Holocaust, this film by the Polish director Marcin Wrona reconceptualizes the Jewish mythology of the dybbuk.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Demon,” a modern ghost story haunted by the Holocaust, opens with an arrival and closes with a departure. These scenes, each set on a raft gliding on a deceptively tranquil country river, bookend a movie that raises light shivers by tapping into historical memory and employing some satisfying, bluntly old-fashioned screen magic. The movie’s visual style, narrative ellipses and weighty subject make it ready-made for the art house even if its mystical flourishes — an otherworldly claw, an undead bride — are the sort of woo-woo pleasures more often scared up in genre stories.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/09/arts/09DEMONALT/09DEMONALT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 341, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/09/arts/09DEMONALT/09DEMONALT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 341}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/09/arts/09DEMONALT/09DEMONALT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 583, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/09/arts/09DEMONALT/09DEMONALT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1165, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/09/arts/09DEMONALT/09DEMONALT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/09/arts/09DEMONALT/09DEMONALT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/09/arts/09DEMONALT/09DEMONALT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: In ‘Demon,’ Wedding Jitters From the Uninvited Dead', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wedding Jitters Caused by the Uninvited Dead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Demon (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wrona, Marcin (1973-2015)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maslona, Pawel (1983- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-08T22:07:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/75a3e204-f8b5-50cc-9dcb-e8e34ea5455a', 'word_count': 795, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75a3e204-f8b5-50cc-9dcb-e8e34ea5455a'}, {'abstract': 'This debut feature depicts a 15-year-old in a tough neighborhood who buys the shoes of his dreams — and the desperation he feels when they are taken from him.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/09/movies/kicks-review.html', 'snippet': 'This debut feature depicts a 15-year-old in a tough neighborhood who buys the shoes of his dreams — and the desperation he feels when they are taken from him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Teenage life in the East Bay neighborhood of Richmond, the setting of Justin Tipping’s promising debut feature film, “Kicks,” is so rough that it’s little wonder that the movie’s 15-year-old protagonist, Brandon (Jahking Guillory), fantasizes that he is watched over by an imaginary spaceman. Because Brandon is small for his age and has delicate features, he is a natural target for bullies. Lacking the macho swagger of his peers, he is not a romantic magnet for the girls who throw themselves at his friends. He dwells in an anxious limbo where the harsh realities of big-city life coincide with a childlike longing for a magical escape.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/09/arts/09KICKS/09KICKS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/09/arts/09KICKS/09KICKS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/09/arts/09KICKS/09KICKS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/09/arts/09KICKS/09KICKS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/09/arts/09KICKS/09KICKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/09/arts/09KICKS/09KICKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/09/arts/09KICKS/09KICKS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: In ‘Kicks,’ the Promise (and Perils) of Those Air Jordans', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A City Boy, Only as Tough as His Shoes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Kicks (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tipping, Justin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Guillory, Jahking', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-08T22:11:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/91d5f7ff-ab0c-59af-9769-055c0dc0a9cb', 'word_count': 569, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91d5f7ff-ab0c-59af-9769-055c0dc0a9cb'}, {'abstract': 'New books recommended by the editors of The New York Times Book Review this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/11/books/review/9-great-books-to-start-off-september.html', 'snippet': 'New books recommended by the editors of The New York Times Book Review this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The fall book season is finally upon us, and I don’t know about you, but I couldn’t possibly escape the summer heat or election onslaught fast enough. And luckily, the books out now provide their own welcome respite. This week, we at the Book Review are particularly excited about three new works of fiction, five excellent new nonfiction books and . . . a play.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/books/review/11edchoice-one/11edchoice-one-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 292, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/11/books/review/11edchoice-one/11edchoice-one-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 292}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/books/review/11edchoice-one/11edchoice-one-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 924, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/books/review/11edchoice-one/11edchoice-one-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 924, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/books/review/11edchoice-one/11edchoice-one-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/11/books/review/