igner Amanda Phelan’s work for the past year, from the time that Phelan — a fellow RISD alum — launched her eponymous women’s wear brand. “Her clothing is about the texture, and creating something unexpected but with a sophisticated silhouette, which I can relate to,” Yau says. “It’s refreshing, after everyone has become so obsessed with basics.” Earlier this summer, she emailed Phelan about CLOSER by WWAKE, her line of sculptural accessories that she had sidelined after her finer, jewel-encrusted pieces took off in 2013.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/08/t-magazine/08tmag-wwake/08tmag-wwake-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/08/t-magazine/08tmag-wwake/08tmag-wwake-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/08/t-magazine/08tmag-wwake/08tmag-wwake-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/08/t-magazine/08tmag-wwake/08tmag-wwake-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/08/t-magazine/08tmag-wwake/08tmag-wwake-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/08/t-magazine/08tmag-wwake/08tmag-wwake-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/08/t-magazine/08tmag-wwa