mbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/09/business/10MONEY/10MONEY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/09/business/10MONEY/10MONEY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/09/business/10MONEY/10MONEY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Should a Cubs Fan Pay to Realize a Lifelong Dream?', 'kicker': 'Your Money', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hard Numbers Intrude Where Cubs Fans Dream', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Cubs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lieber, Ron', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Series', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ticket Scalping', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'StubHub', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wrigley Field (Chicago)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-09T11:58:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Lieber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lieber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01596c68-49e3-5e25-a16a-dceb71aac249', 'word_count': 1483, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01596c68-49e3-5e25-a16a-dceb71aac249'}, {'abstract': 'Appalachian voters know perfectly well the candidate is dangerous. But they’re desperate for change.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/11/opinion/sunday/we-need-somebody-spectacular-views-from-trump-country.html', 'snippet': 'Appalachian voters know perfectly well the candidate is dangerous. But they’re desperate for change.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paris, Ky. — After Bill Bissett, the president of the Kentucky Coal Association, told me that “President Obama cares more about Paris, France, than he does about Paris, Kentucky” — a sentiment that seems broadly shared around here — I decided to check out this little town with a big name set amid the verdant undulations of picket-fenced Kentucky horse country. Soon enough I ran into Cindy Hedges, whose boot store stands on Main Street and whose hours, as described by a sign on the door, are: “If I’m here, I’m here. If I ain’t, I ain’t.”', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/opinion/sunday/11RogerCohen-web2/11RogerCohen-web2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/11/opinion/sunday/11RogerCohen-web2/11RogerCohen-web2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/opinion/sunday/11RogerCohen-web2/11RogerCohen-web2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/opinion/sunday/11RogerCohen-web2/11RogerCohen-web2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/opinion/sunday/11RogerCohen-web2/11RogerCohen-web2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/11/opinion/sunday/11RogerCohen-web2/11RogerCohen-web2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/opinion/sunday/11RogerCohen-web2/11RogerCohen-web2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'We Need ‘Somebody Spectacular’: Views From Trump Country', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'We Need ‘Somebody Spectacular’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kentucky', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cohen, Roger', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coal', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mines and Mining', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Bill', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-09T12:00:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roger Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roger', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a6d22d6-8f12-5bf8-a3f0-686f1def515e', 'word_count': 2513, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a6d22d6-8f12-5bf8-a3f0-686f1def515e'}, {'abstract': 'What once seemed shocking may now be seen as normal, and what seemed pernicious — the male gaze — can sometimes turn out to just be someone looking and trying to see.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/09/t-magazine/gazing-while-male.html', 'snippet': 'What once seemed shocking may now be seen as normal, and what seemed pernicious — the male gaze — can sometimes turn out to just be someone looking and trying to see.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the ’60s, the artist Tom Wesselmann was as famous as his contemporaries Andy Warhol, Roy Lichtenstein, James Rosenquist and Robert Indiana. His work then fell from favor in part because some critics took umbrage at what they felt was his objectification of the female form. Indeed, Wesselmann’s work incorporates big, bright Pop iconography of lady parts, like breasts and lips and suntanned bikini lines.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '64', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/09/t-magazine/09tmag-edletter/09tmag-edletter-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/09/t-magazine/09tmag-edletter/09tmag-edletter-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/09/t-magazine/09tmag-edletter/09tmag-ed