tedly, seemed more pulled together than the crowd might have suggested.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/09/fashion/adam-selman-spring-2017-review.html', 'snippet': 'The audience was a wild mix of pop and art-house types. The collection, unexpectedly, seemed more pulled together than the crowd might have suggested.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s a raucousness to Adam Selman’s shows that feels vital. The crowds are the types who go wild. In the house on Thursday night, the Cobrasnake (alias the photographer Mark Hunter) was snapping away as if 2006 had never left us. The art-house types (there’s Casey Spooner) mixed with the Top 40 types (there’s the sultry R&B popette Tinashe). Mr. Selman, with his Castro-clone mustache and Texas Baptist manners, brings them all to the party.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just Another Night at the Adam Selman Funhouse', 'kicker': 'Fashion Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Selman, Adam D (1982- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Fashion Week', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-09T14:59:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew Schneier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schneier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3f9eca6-e17b-579b-8b87-9bb5ee86e8e5', 'word_count': 361, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3f9eca6-e17b-579b-8b87-9bb5ee86e8e5'}, {'abstract': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: A fuel leak delays the liftoff of Gemini-11 in September 1966.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/09/09/1966-gemini-11-leak-delays-flight/', 'snippet': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: A fuel leak delays the liftoff of Gemini-11 in September 1966.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cape Kennedy, Fla — Gemini-11’s space flight was postponed for 24 hours early today [Sept. 9] when a fuel tank in a launch rocket developed a pinhole leak a few hours before liftoff. Space officials said the leak in the Titan-2 rocket which was to have launched astronauts Charles Conrad and Richard Gordon on a three-day flight was small but necessitated the defueling of the rocket. Technicians later repaired the hole, which was in a spot-weld about halfway up the 109-foot rocket. After checks, officials rescheduled the flight for tomorrow [Sept. 10] morning. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/10/blogs/10oldiht-1966-gemini11/10oldiht-1966-gemini11-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 481, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/10/blogs/10oldiht-1966-gemini11/10oldiht-1966-gemini11-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 481, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/10/blogs/10oldiht-1966-gemini11/10oldiht-1966-gemini11-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/10/blogs/10oldiht-1966-gemini11/10oldiht-1966-gemini11-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/10/blogs/10oldiht-1966-gemini11/10oldiht-1966-gemini11-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 