t': 'Tom Wolfe, whose new book about the evolution of language is No. 14 on the hardcover nonfiction list, says picking fights is “a lot better than not being noticed at all.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/18/books/review/tom-wolfe-inside-the-list.html', 'snippet': 'Tom Wolfe, whose new book about the evolution of language is No. 14 on the hardcover nonfiction list, says picking fights is “a lot better than not being noticed at all.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Everybody’s Talking: In some ways, it makes perfect sense that Tom Wolfe would write a book about the evolution of language. Over the past half-century, after all, Wolfe’s own work has contributed mightily to the evolution of a certain kind of language — or the evolution of a style, anyway: the neon-lit, whiz-bang exploding cigar of a sentence, bristling with exclamation points and packed tighter than a spring-loaded snake in a can of peanuts. As a founder of New Journalism in the 1960s and the author of sprawling social novels beginning with “The Bonfire of the Vanities,” in 1987, Wolfe has cast a big shadow on generations of American writers. But it turns out mere influence isn’t what he has in mind with “The Kingdom of Speech,” new on the hardcover nonfiction list at No.\u202f14. Instead, Wolfe trains his sights on biological evolution — specifically, Darwin’s theory of natural selection — and what he sees as its inadequacy to account for the existence of human language. Along the way, he also attacks the neo-Darwinian linguist Noam Chomsky, who has advanced the idea of language as an innate evolutionary trait.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/books/review/11inside-list-wolfe/11inside-list-wolfe-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 586, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/11/books/review/11inside-list-wolfe/11inside-list-wolfe-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 586}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/books/review/11inside-list-wolfe/11inside-list-wolfe-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 819, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/books/review/11inside-list-wolfe/11inside-list-wolfe-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 819, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/books/review/11inside-list-wolfe/11inside-list-wolfe-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/11/books/review/11inside-list-wolfe/11inside-list-wolfe-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/books/review/11inside-list-wolfe/11inside-list-wolfe-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Story Behind This Week’s Best Sellers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Inside the List', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wolfe, Tom', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-09T15:13:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gregory Cowles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gregory', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowles', 'qualifier': None