9-a6c8-e4fdb68c1470'}, {'abstract': 'Michael Redpath, a lieutenant in the Fire Department, spent six months documenting the cleanup at the World Trade Center site after the Sept. 11 attacks. Then a hurricane found his negatives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/11/nyregion/images-of-ground-zero-transformed-by-sandys-waters.html', 'snippet': 'Michael Redpath, a lieutenant in the Fire Department, spent six months documenting the cleanup at the World Trade Center site after the Sept. 11 attacks. Then a hurricane found his negatives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Michael Redpath had just started surfing near his home in Breezy Point, on the Rockaway Peninsula, when he looked up and saw smoke billowing up from Lower Manhattan. That was the end of his surfing that day, 15 years ago. A lieutenant in the Fire Department now, he was a firefighter in Ladder Company 169 then. By the time he got to the World Trade Center, both towers were down, and the area looked “like a nuclear winter,” he said, with “totally empty streets, white dust covering everything.” The next day he learned how many of his compatriots died.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Images of Ground Zero, Transformed by Sandy’s Waters', 'kicker': 'Album | Michael Redpath', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ground Zero, Deluged', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Trade Center (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Redpath, Michael A (1963- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rockaway Peninsula (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-09T16:53:59+0000', 'docu