ussia annexed from Ukraine in 2014.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/10/world/europe/war-games-show-off-russias-tightening-grip-on-crimea.html', 'snippet': 'A huge show of power, including 12,000 troops, simulated an invasion and counterattack on the Crimean peninsula, which Russia annexed from Ukraine in 2014.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — Large landing ships approached the shores of Crimea on Friday, simulating an invasion of the peninsula that was annexed by Moscow from Ukraine in 2014. Tanks and armored vehicles lumbered out of the ships, only to be met by the superior forces of the defenders, equipped with heavy artillery.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'War Games Show Off Russia’s Tightening Grip on Crimea', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Crimea (Ukraine)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-10T05:01:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ivan Nechepurenko', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ivan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nechepurenko', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/124ea30e-11b2-557d-88c7-57eca075897c', 'word_count': 639, 'uri': 'nyt://article/124ea30e-11b2-557d-88c7-57eca075897c'}, {'abstract': 'To mark the 15th anniversary of 9/11, the NYPD held its first memorial parade. The procession commemorated the 23 officers who died on 9/11 and the 99 who died