on/10MONSE01/10MONSE01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/10/fashion/10MONSE01/10MONSE01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Monse Draws Attention, and Not Just for the Clothes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Monse (Fashion Label)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oscar de la Renta LLC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-10T13:37:44+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Style', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/7f534794-ef5e-5f90-b3a5-0dfca18c83be', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/7f534794-ef5e-5f90-b3a5-0dfca18c83be'}, {'abstract': 'Laura Kim and Fernando Garcia, newly appointed as creative directors of Oscar de la Renta, showed their own label.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/10/fashion/monse-new-york-fashion-show-oscar-de-la-renta.html', 'snippet': 'Laura Kim and Fernando Garcia, newly appointed as creative directors of Oscar de la Renta, showed their own label.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One week ago, the news broke that Laura Kim and Fernando Garcia, the designers of Monse, would be going back to Oscar de la Renta — where they had spent 12 and 6 years, respectively — as its next creative directors. The timing was not ideal. Ms. Kim and Mr. Garcia’s own label was barely a year old, and the preparations for its New York Fashion Week show, only its third, were well underway. But news will out.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Amid Much Buzz, Monse Shows Its Spring Collection', 'kicker': 'Short Take', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garcia, Fernando (Designer)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim, Laura (Designer)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Monse (Fashion Label)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Fashion Week', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oscar de la Renta LLC', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-10T13:37:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew Schneier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schneier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/737b1d2c-f23a-5ae0-89db-d5a4ee584c00', 'word_count': 301, 'uri': 'nyt://article/737b1d2c-f23a-5ae0-89db-d5a4ee584c00'}, {'abstract': 'Nests near air vents, safety in low-rise buildings and accommodating disabilities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/11/realestate/when-birds-nest-in-bad-places.html', 'snippet': 'Nests near air vents, safety in low-rise buildings and accommodating disabilities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I live in a condominium with beautiful landscaping, trees —  and lots of birds. The air-conditioning and heating units in the apartments are vented outdoors through louvers built into the building’s brick facade. Birds nest in the spaces between the louvers and the cooling-and-heating units, leaving behind droppings and nesting material. It is messy and a health hazard, but does not damage the appliances. The board says condo owners are responsible for cleaning and removing the nests. But shouldn’t this be the board’s responsibility, since the nests are in the facade and not in the appliances?', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/realestate/11ask/11ask-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 458, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/11/realestate/11ask/11ask-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 458}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/realestate/11ask/11ask-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 782, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/realestate/11ask/11ask-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1500, 'width': 1964, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/realestate/11ask/11ask-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/11/realestate/11ask/11ask-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/realestate/11ask/11ask-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When Birds Nest in Bad Places', 'kicker': 'Ask Real Estate', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Birds Take Up Residence at a Condo', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buildings (Structures)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject',