ount': 1400, 'uri': 'nyt://article/345b4f76-d526-5489-b7f2-ebc7307cf530'}, {'abstract': 'For the Republican nominee, there’s no difference between ratings and worth.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/11/opinion/sunday/donald-trumps-ideology-of-applause.html', 'snippet': 'For the Republican nominee, there’s no difference between ratings and worth.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Americans are such sticklers. Such poops. Sure, some of Vladimir Putin’s political opponents wind up in jail, while some of the journalists he dislikes end up in the morgue. Yes, his government is apparently committing cybercrimes to meddle in our election. And there was that small matter of invading and annexing one of Russia’s neighbors.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/sunday-review/11Bruni/11Bruni-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 662, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/11/sunday-review/11Bruni/11Bruni-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 662}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/sunday-review/11Bruni/11Bruni-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 929, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/sunday-review/11Bruni/11Bruni-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1857, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/sunday-review/11Bruni/11Bruni-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/11/sunday-review/11Bruni/11Bruni-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/sunday-review/11Bruni/11Bruni-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Donald Trump’s Ideology of Applause', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Donald Trump’s Ideology of Applause', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-10T18:30:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Frank Bruni', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Frank', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bruni', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f142f6c-3f4f-5e90-b2b7-084d571dcfbf', 'word_count': 1109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f142f6c-3f4f-5e90-b2b7-084d571dcfbf'}, {'abstract': 'Move slowly through the World Trade Center memorial plaza. Watch the names that flow by. Absorb the vast emptiness, the enormity of our loss, the passage of years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/11/opinion/sunday/a-walk-around-the-void-of-9-11.html', 'snippet': 'Move slowly through the World Trade Center memorial plaza. Watch the names that flow by. Absorb the vast emptiness, the enormity of our loss, the passage of years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Walk onto the plaza in Lower Manhattan and you hear the memorial before you see it — a whooshing through the oak trees. You soon realize it’s not the wind, but water. At the footprint of each tower, north and south, a vast square emptiness is bound by four walls of falling water, the pool below pouring into a smaller central void that flows out of sight. The memorial is black upon black, but the water casts reflections. Sunlight and mist make fragmentary rainbows that flicker as clouds go by.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/opinion/sunday/11sun1/11sun1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/11/opinion/sunday/11sun1/11sun1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 599}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/opinion/sunday/11sun1/11sun1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1023, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/opinion/sunday/11sun1/11sun1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2046, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/opinion/sunday/11sun1/11sun1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/11/opinion/sunday/11sun1/11sun1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/opinion/sunday/11sun1/11sun1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLar