he archives of the International Herald Tribune: East Germans clash through the Berlin wall in a bulldozer in September 1966.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/09/11/1966-east-germans-bulldoze-way-to-freedom/', 'snippet': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: East Germans clash through the Berlin wall in a bulldozer in September 1966.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — Two East German couples and a child crashed through Communist barbed wire in a steel-plated bulldozer today [Sept. 11] and escaped into West Berlin. East German border guards riddled the bulldozer with sub-machine-gun bullets but it got through a trench and three barbed-wire barriers into West Berlin’s Spandau district. Steel plates placed around the bulldozer’s cabin saved the five refugees – two pregnant women, their husbands and a four year-old boy. Two bullets grazed the heads of one man and woman. They were treated for flesh wounds at a West Berlin hospital and then released.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/12/blogs/12oldiht-1966-eastgermans1/12oldiht-1966-eastgermans1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 449, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/12/blogs/12oldiht-1966-eastgermans1/12oldiht-1966-eastgermans1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 449}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/12/blogs/12oldiht-1966-eastgermans1/12oldiht-1966-eastgermans1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 767, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/12/blogs/12oldiht-1966-eastgermans1/12oldiht-1966-eastgermans1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1117, 'width': 1491, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_n