y as three major oil terminals, military and civilian officials said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Militia Seizes Libyan Oil Terminals in Challenge to Government', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Militia Seizes Libyan Oil Ports in Challenge to Government', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hifter, Khalifa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jathran, Ibrahim', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ports', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-12T00:30:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Suliman Ali Zway and Declan Walsh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Suliman', 'middlename': 'Ali', 'lastname': 'Zway', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Declan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Walsh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c6dfcc4-0a46-529a-9554-d0e2f8c1649f', 'word_count': 492, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c6dfcc4-0a46-529a-9554-d0e2f8c1649f'}, {'abstract': 'Fashion week doesn’t pause for the weekend — and neither do the parties.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/11/fashion/alexander-wang-naomi-campbell-karlie-kloss-new-york-fashion-week-parties.html', 'snippet': 'Fashion week doesn’t pause for the weekend — and neither do the parties.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Saturday night, Doutzen Kroes hosted the #KnotOnMyPlanet benefit for the Elephant Crisis Fund; Madonna and Nicki Minaj were among the celebrity guests at Alexander Wang; and Blood Orange performed for Re/Done jeans.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Alexander Wang, Naomi Campbell and Karlie Kloss Party on Saturday Night of Fashion Week', 'kicker': 'Scene City', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Re/Done (Fashion Label)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Minaj, Nicki', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wang, Alexander (1983- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Campbell, Naomi', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Fashion Week', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-12T00:31:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Valeriya Safronova', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Valeriya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Safronova', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf3cc1e7-4e23-5291-a502-787ce3e29931', 'word_count': 33, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf3cc1e7-4e23-5291-a502-787ce3e29931'}, {'abstract': 'The makeup artist Tom Pecheux created a “sweaty, sexy, naughty” look — and at least one model didn’t want to take it off after the show.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/11/t-magazine/fashion/altuzarra-beauty-glitter-new-york-fashion-week.html', 'snippet': 'The makeup artist Tom Pecheux created a “sweaty, sexy, naughty” look — and at least one model didn’t want to take it off after the show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Backstage at the Altuzarra spring/summer 2017 show this afternoon, the makeup artist Tom Pecheux was his usual chic, irreverent self. Smiling, he described the beautifully dewy look he created as “sweaty, sexy, naughty,” with a bit of a wink to reporters. The effect, he explained, picked up on the energetic, playful vibes of Joseph Altuzarra’s collection and channels the women who emerge from a pool or shower and “throw on their clothes and they just go.” For the high-shine look, he swept Butter Elixir botanical oil over the skin, patted on creamy foundation, and dusted MAC Mineralize SkinFinish in Perfectly Lit across the upper cheeks and nose in a wavelike formation for a natural glow. On the eyes, Pecheux applied black eyeliner smudged in with MAC Neon Studio Eye Gloss, a fleshy tone that warms up the black eyeliner so “it’s not so aggressive” and doesn’t look too pristine (“perfection is boring,” he said, with Parisian insouciance). But the glamorous twist? Pecheux lightly dappled MAC Glitter in Reflects Bronze over the models’ faces — the fine particles floating through the air before they gently landed on the skin to produce a subtle shimmer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/t-magazine/fashion/11tmag-bbr-03/11tmag-bbr-03-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 904, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/11/t-magazine/fashion/11tmag-bbr-03/11tmag-bbr-03-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 904}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/t-magazine/fashion/11tmag-bbr-03/11tmag-bbr-03-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 680, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/t-magazine/fashion/11tmag-bbr-03/11tmag-bbr-03-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1360, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/t-magazine/fashion/11tmag-bbr-03/11tmag-bbr-03-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/11/t-magazine/fashion/11tmag-bbr-03/11tmag-bbr-03-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/t-magazine/fashion/11tmag-bbr-03/11tmag-bbr-03-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At Altuzarra, a Party-Ready Touch of Glitter', 'kicker': 'Backstage Beauty Report', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Fashion Week', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Altuzarra, Joseph', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beauty (Concept)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-12T00:32:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Fashion & Beauty', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kari Molvar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kari', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Molvar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17d17130-9ef0-53bc-9080-3d6b7a014fe4', 'word_count': 247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17d17130-9ef0-53bc-9080-3d6b7a014fe4'}, {'abstract': 'Fairfield and Bridgeport sit side by side and spend more per student than the national average, but the quality of the education they offer is worlds apart.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/12/nyregion/in-connecticut-a-wealth-gap-divides-neighboring-schools.html', 'snippet': 'Fairfield and Bridgeport sit side by side and spend more per student than the national average, but the quality of the education they offer is worlds apart.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The two Connecticut school districts sit side by side along Long Island Sound. Both spend more than the national average on their students. They prepare their pupils for the same statewide tests. Their teachers, like virtually all the teachers in the state, earn the same high marks on evaluations.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/12/nyregion/12funding1/12funding1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/12/nyregion/12funding1/12funding1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/12/nyregion/12funding1/12funding1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/12/nyregion/12funding1/12funding1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/12/nyregion/12funding1/12funding1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/12/nyregion/12funding1/12funding1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/12/nyregion/12funding1/12funding1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge