nal anthem is not Jeff Fisher-approved.” Fisher is the head coach of the Los Angeles Rams, who, in an episode of the reality football show “Hard Knocks,” told his team that standing for the anthem was sacrosanct: “It’s an opportunity to realize how lucky you are.” Yet here was Kaepernick, sitting down.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/12/magazine/18firstwords1/18firstwords1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/12/magazine/18firstwords1/18firstwords1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/12/magazine/18firstwords1/18firstwords1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/12/magazine/18firstwords1/18firstwords1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1772, 'width': 1772, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/12/magazine/18firstwords1/18firstwords1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/12/magazine/18firstwords1/18firstwords1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/12/magazine/18firstwords1/18firstwords1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Colin Kaepernick and the Question of Who Gets to Be Called a ‘Patriot’', 'kicker': 'First Words', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stand and Deliver', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morris, Wesley', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Leslie (1967- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaepernick, Colin', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'English Language', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco 49ers', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Anthems', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-12T09:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Wesley Morris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Wesley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d799e3a-aa8f-5afe-8fef-e31c1708faf6', 'word_count': 1300, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d799e3a-aa8f-5afe-8fef-e31c1708faf6'}, {'abstract': 'John Belle, who died at 84, conveyed a genial joy in bringing back to life the masterworks of his predecessors, including Grand Central Terminal and the Enid A. Haupt Conservatory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/13/nyregion/john-belle-restoring-new-york-city-landmarks.html', 'snippet': 'John Belle, who died at 84, conveyed a