ename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b9472fc-45d6-5407-9277-6641edc3f142', 'word_count': 96, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b9472fc-45d6-5407-9277-6641edc3f142'}, {'abstract': 'Tunisian olive oils are now worth savoring thanks to tighter restrictions on labeling and production.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/14/dining/extra-virgin-olive-oil-tunisia.html', 'snippet': 'Tunisian olive oils are now worth savoring thanks to tighter restrictions on labeling and production.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tunisia was the featured country at this summer’s Fancy Food Show in New York, and almost half of that country’s exhibits were promoting extra-virgin olive oil. The industry, which has existed since Roman times, has shifted to a higher-end product for export to Europe and America. Although Tunisia’s extra-virgin olive oil is still sent in bulk to Europe for anonymous blending, production rules and labeling certifications for extra virgin and organic have been tightened. Now 100 percent of what’s in a bottle labeled Tunisian is indeed from Tunisia. Some oils tend to be lighter, sweeter and less peppery than their European counterparts. For example, Terra Delyssa Extra Virgin Olive Oil is typically mild and fruity with a hint of bitterness in the aftertaste (try it in a salad dressing), and Olivi Chemlali de Djerba Extra Virgin Olive Oil is lighter and even more delicate. Les Moulins de Mahjoub, an organic extra-virgin oil, is deeper in color, more viscous and herbal, with a nice green olive bite. It would add a sleek finish to grilled fish and vegetables: Terra Delyssa, $8.99 for 34 ounces, worldmarket.com; Olivi, $14.90 for 8.45 ounces, from amazon.com; Les Moulins de Mahjoub, $19.99 for 12.5 ounces, from amazon.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/14/dining/14BURNER-OIL-WEB/14BURNER-OIL-WEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 771, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/14/dining/14BURNER-OIL-WEB/14BURNER-OIL-WEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 771}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/14/dining/14BURNER-OIL-WEB/14BURNER-OIL-WEB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 798, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/14/dining/14BURNER-OIL-WEB/14BURNER-OIL-WEB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1563, 'width': 1217, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/14/dining/14BURNER-OIL-WEB/14BURNER-OIL-WEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/14/dining/14BURNER-OIL-WEB/14BURNER-OIL-WEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/14/dining/14BURNER-OIL-WEB/14BURNER-OIL-WEB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Olive Oil Revolution in Tunisia', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Drizzle: An Olive Oil  Revolution in Tunisia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olive Oil', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tunisia', 'rank': 