'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/13/world/13Letter-web/13Letter-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/13/world/13Letter-web/13Letter-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/13/world/13Letter-web/13Letter-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Airbnb, a Silicon Valley Titan, Breaks Ranks in Admitting Its Power', 'kicker': 'Letter From America', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Airbnb', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Uber Technologies Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-12T15:07:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anand Giridharadas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anand', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Giridharadas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/922e55ef-6481-5dcc-8178-5e53d05eba10', 'word_count': 662, 'uri': 'nyt://article/922e55ef-6481-5dcc-8178-5e53d05eba10'}, {'abstract': 'The designers Fanny Singer and Mariah Nielson unveil the selections in their new label, Permanent Collections.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/12/t-magazine/design/fanny-singer-mariah-nielson-design-permanent-collection.html', 'snippet': 'The designers Fanny Singer and Mariah Nielson unveil the selections in their new label, Permanent Collections.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In culling pieces for their new label, Permanent Collection, Fanny Singer and Mariah Nielson relied on principles of museum acquisition: They sought “what is most elemental and classic,” says Singer, and took care to avoid “even short-term obsolescence.” Inspired by their own possessions, the things “we’d had the longest, that felt most relevant no matter what,” their first collection includes porcelain teacups cast from originals by Nielson’s father, the sculptor J.B. Blunk (her mother is the organic textiles pioneer Christine Nielson), and a pair of Attal leather slides like the ones a family friend once gave Singer, whose mother is Alice Waters. Nielson and Singer, both Northern California natives, met in a London bakery while wearing matching navy blue jackets, both vintage of indeterminate origin, and hit on the idea for the project.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '66', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/12/t-magazine/12tmag-perm1/12tmag-perm1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/12/t-magazine/12tmag-perm1/12tmag-perm1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/12/t-magazine/12tmag-perm1/12tmag-perm1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/12/t-magazine/12tmag-perm1/12tmag-perm1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'th