], 'pub_date': '2016-09-12T15:22:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/480d04e6-0e58-50d9-8963-70be77740ce3', 'word_count': 736, 'uri': 'nyt://article/480d04e6-0e58-50d9-8963-70be77740ce3'}, {'abstract': 'Along with Vista Equity Partners, Thoma Bravo is one of the few specialists who focus solely on taking over aging tech companies and then turning them around.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/13/business/dealbook/thoma-bravo-raises-7-6-billion-fund-to-pursue-more-tech-deals.html', 'snippet': 'Along with Vista Equity Partners, Thoma Bravo is one of the few specialists who focus solely on taking over aging tech companies and then turning them around.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — At a busy time for technology takeovers, one of the main private equity specialists in the field is raising its biggest-ever fund to pursue more deals.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thoma Bravo Raises $7.6 Billion Fund to Pursue More Tech Deals', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Thoma Bravo', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Blue Coat Systems Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-12T15:34:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/92727e4b-e7ab-57a4-9bc2-656593c7a802', 'word_count': 455, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92727e4b-e7ab-57a4-9bc2-656593c7a802'}, {'abstract': '“The 24-Hour Wine Expert” by Jancis Robinson breaks down the basics of wine appreciation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/14/dining/the-24-hour-wine-expert-jancis-robinson-book.html', 'snippet': '“The 24-Hour Wine Expert” by Jancis Robinson breaks down the basics of wine appreciation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jancis Robinson, a British wine writer renowned for her many big, glossy tomes, has come up with a compact, breezy, one-shot wine seminar for novices. In 112 no-nonsense pages, she covers all the basics for understanding, selecting, appreciating, serving and storing wine. She dismisses pretension in favor of the practical. If carignan or claret are still vinous mysteries to you, look here for answers: “The 24-Hour Wine Expert” by Jancis Robinson (Abrams Image, $12.95).', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/14/dining/14BURNER-WINE-WEB/14BURNER-WINE-WEB-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 763, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/14/dining/14BURNER-WINE-WEB/14BURNER-WINE-WEB-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 763}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/14/dining/14BURNER-WINE-WEB/14BURNER-WINE-WEB-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 806, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url