ashion Week schedule in a blaze of color. Sander Lak, its designer, declared — heretically, given that he had just taken up residence in New York — that very few women actually look good in black. He advocated fearlessly for neon yellow and orange, lilac and magenta.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sies Marjan Still Swears Off Black', 'kicker': 'Short Take', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Fashion Week', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sies Marjan (Fashion Label)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-12T18:02:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew Schneier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schneier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4704c55a-6406-5ea0-b047-bdf21b1885a6', 'word_count': 436, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4704c55a-6406-5ea0-b047-bdf21b1885a6'}, {'abstract': 'The case of a mother who killed herself and her four children has ignited concerns about the grim realities rural families face amid rampant inequality.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/13/world/asia/mothers-killing-of-children-in-rural-china-spurs-debate-about-inequality.html', 'snippet': 'The case of a mother who killed herself and her four children has ignited concerns about the grim realities rural families face amid rampant inequality.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — The young mother lived in obscurity in a wobbly house at the end of a dusty road. She did not speak much with strangers, spending her days tending to rows of wheat, peas and potatoes.', 'print_section': 'A', 'pr