uren', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2dc4518c-c424-5425-9503-c6b8b8187a94', 'word_count': 1144, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2dc4518c-c424-5425-9503-c6b8b8187a94'}, {'abstract': 'For the designer’s spring/summer 2017 show, the makeup artist Francelle Daly created a graphic look that played on the idea of negative space.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/12/t-magazine/fashion/phillip-lim-eyeliner-beauty-fashion-week.html', 'snippet': 'For the designer’s spring/summer 2017 show, the makeup artist Francelle Daly created a graphic look that played on the idea of negative space.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The designer Phillip Lim is a passionate collector of art (furniture made by cabinetmakers is a particular interest). So it made sense that the makeup look at his spring/summer 2017 show took an artist-driven approach. Backstage, the makeup artist Francelle Daly slicked on graphic eyeliner, then removed the edges for a conceptual play on negative space. “It’s about modernizing the way we wear eyeliner,” she explained of her technique — which stood out for not only its impactful quality, but also for its ease of application. Daly simply outlined the eyes, “saturating” the upper and lower lash lines in Nars Eyeliner Stylo in Carpates, then traced Nars Kohliner Minorque along the inner waterline. Then, for the fun part: Daly dipped her Q-tip in a water cleanser and “chopped” off the inner and outer corners of her lines, customizing the shape to each models’ eyes. “Maybe it’s a little smaller at the bottom, maybe it’s a little bigger on top, just to make sure you don’t overpower the eye, or look like a raccoon,” she noted. Daly also recommends stepping back and looking in the mirror to ensure your liner is somewhat symmetrical on both eyes. But don’t agonize over it: “It’s all about what works best for you when doing your makeup, and being your own artist.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/12/t-magazine/12tmag-bbr-01/12tmag-bbr-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/12/t-magazine/12tmag-bbr-01/12tmag-bbr-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/12/t-magazine/12tmag-bbr-01/12tmag-bbr-01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/12/t-magazine/12tmag-bbr-01/12tmag-bbr-01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/12/t-magazine/12tmag-bbr-01/12tmag-bbr-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/12/t-magazine/12tmag-bbr-01/12tmag-bbr-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/12/t-magazine/12tmag-bbr-01/12tmag-bbr-01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At 3.1 Phillip Lim, Eyeliner Meets Architecture', 'kicker': 'Backstage Beauty Report', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cosmetics and Toiletries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Fa