d3dd-50ef-9943-d817ae6865fc', 'word_count': 244, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64455e72-d3dd-50ef-9943-d817ae6865fc'}, {'abstract': 'The author of “Hidden Figures” on black excellence, visibility in STEM fields and why imagination is paramount to social progress.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/18/magazine/margot-lee-shetterly-wants-to-tell-more-black-stories.html', 'snippet': 'The author of “Hidden Figures” on black excellence, visibility in STEM fields and why imagination is paramount to social progress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Your new book, “Hidden Figures,” is the story of the black female mathematicians at NASA who helped put Americans on the moon. Why haven’t we heard about this before? Where I grew up, in Hampton, Va., we knew the story, and we thought it was pretty normal. They were people who were doing this exceptional job when you look back on it, but at the time, they were just ordinary people who loved their work. It was kind of nice to grow up in a place where that achieved such a degree of normalcy that people weren’t talking about it all the time.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '88', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/magazine/18talk/18talk-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 948, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/18/magazine/18talk/18talk-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 948}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/magazine/18talk/18talk-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 649, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/magazine/18talk/18talk-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1262, 'width': 799, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'super