e work of Trix and Robert Haussmann is virtually unknown in the U.S.?', 'lead_paragraph': 'How is it that the brilliantly subversive work of Trix and Robert Haussmann is virtually unknown in the U.S.?', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '126', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'These Architects, Working Into Their 80s, Should Be Famous', 'kicker': 'By Design', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Should Be Famous', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hass, Nancy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Milan (Italy)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Memphis Group', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-13T12:01:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Design & Interiors', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nancy Hass', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nancy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hass', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e7f015a-389e-55ab-bc78-61c99a22134b', 'word_count': 803, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e7f015a-389e-55ab-bc78-61c99a22134b'}, {'abstract': 'The Polish-born designer Matylda Krzykowski will soon bring her knack for sniffing out talent to Chelsea.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/12/t-magazine/design/matylda-krzykowski-designer-chamber.html', 'snippet': 'The Polish-born designer Matylda Krzykowski will soon bring her knack for sniffing out talent to Chelsea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Matylda Krzykowski, the Polish-born designer, curator and co-founder of the contemporary-design space Depot Basel, in Switzerland, will lend her knack for sniffing out talent to Chamber, the Chelsea gallery and boutique, next month. Inspired by the artist Richard Hamilton’s iconic collage “Just what is it that makes today’s homes so different, so appealing?” — a comment on postwar consumer culture — she’s selected objects that are “between sculpture and your living environment,” including a surrealist lamp from the Austrian duo Mischer’traxler and a pair of trompe l’oeil wooden boxes by the Swiss designers Trix and Robert Haussmann. “It’s about shifting our perception of things that we know,” Krzykowski says. \xad', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '62', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/12/t-magazine/find-slide-WBGG/find-slide-WBGG-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/12/t-magazine/find-slide-WBGG/find-slide-WBGG-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/12/t-magazine/find-slide-WBGG/find-slide-WBGG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/12/t-magazine/find-slide-WBGG/find-slide-WBGG-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/12/t-magazine/find-slide-WBGG/find-slide-WBGG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/12/t-magazine/find-slide-WBGG/find-slide-WBGG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbL