': 'Maison Margiela (Fashion Label)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Polo Ralph Lauren Corp', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Handbags and Purses', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-13T13:49:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Fashion & Beauty', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b23d15a-55b0-5476-9bd4-0f8694858a57', 'word_count': 7, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b23d15a-55b0-5476-9bd4-0f8694858a57'}, {'abstract': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: A circus in England is raided for military absentees in September 1916.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/09/13/1916-circus-raided-for-shirkers/', 'snippet': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: A circus in England is raided for military absentees in September 1916.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — A raid for military absentees was made on a travelling circus on Monday [Sept. 11] night by the military authorities, assisted by the police and special constables and a large detachment from a volunteer training corps. The latter surrounded the circus tent while the military and police entered. The names and addresses of seventy men without necessary papers had been taken when all the lights went out, and the audience of between three and four thousand was left in darkness. The proceedings of the military and the remainder of the performance had to be abandoned. — The New York Herald, European Edition, Sept. 14, 1916', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1916: Circus Raided for Shirkers', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-13T13:57:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4601784e-b416-5bef-8d82-5fb88dd3ffc0', 'word_count': 107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4601784e-b416-5bef-8d82-5fb88dd3ffc0'}, {'abstract': 'Through much of American history, presidents and candidates have tried to conceal their maladies, and opponents have done their best to exploit signs of weakness.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/14/us/politics/president-health-history.html', 'snippet': 'Through much of American history, presidents and candidates have tried to conceal their maladies, and opponents have done their best to exploit signs of weakness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hillary Clinton’s bout of pneumonia and the criticism of how little she and her opponent, Donald J. Trump, have made public about their medical histories thrust questions of transparency about health to the center of the presidential campaign this week, with both candidates promising to release more detailed records in the coming days.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/13/us/12presidentialhealth4/12presidentialhealth4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/13/us/12presidentialhealth4/12presidentialhealth4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit':