ian Food? It’s Not Beer', 'kicker': 'The Pour', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pairing Wine With Indian Food', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Asimov, Eric', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beedle, Daniel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dolinski, Michael', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indian Accent (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-13T14:36:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Asimov', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Asimov', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a652d49f-9a3f-507c-b014-ac93282b4cc3', 'word_count': 1532, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a652d49f-9a3f-507c-b014-ac93282b4cc3'}, {'abstract': 'The cool kids gang up on the smart nerd.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/09/13/why-are-the-media-objectively-pro-trump/', 'snippet': 'The cool kids gang up on the smart nerd.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Because they are, at this point. It’s not even false equivalence: compare the amount of attention given to the Clinton Foundation despite absence of any evidence of wrongdoing, and attention given to Trump Foundation, which engaged in more or less open bribery — but barely made a dent in news coverage. Clinton was harassed endlessly over failure to give press conferences, even though she was doing lots of interviews; Trump violated decades of tradition by refusing to release his taxes, amid strong suspicion that he is hiding something; the press simply dropped the subject.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'mult