ppet': 'In Greenwich Village, skillfully updating classic dishes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the hedonist’s view of American immigration patterns, bad times for chefs in China are good times for dumpling chasers and noodle hunters in New York. When experienced cooks couldn’t make a living there for political or economic reasons, they came here. Conversely, over the last decade or so, the hypertrophic Chinese economy has left the kitchens of our Chinatowns somewhat flattened, with fewer high peaks of talent standing out in the landscape.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Spicy Spoils of China’s Boom, at Hao Noodle and Tea', 'kicker': 'Restaurant Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Spicy Spoils of China’s Boom', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greenwich Village (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Hao Noodle and Tea by Madam Zhu's Kitchen (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-13T19:29:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pete Wells', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pete', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wells', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9729ebf-dbc6-5c7c-8cc9-bb95d3cab30f', 'word_count': 981, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9729ebf-dbc6-5c7c-8cc9-bb95d3cab30f'}, {'abstract': 'Spicy and inventive, Hao Noodle and Tea impresses in Greenwich Village.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2016/09/14/dining/hao-noodle-and-tea-by-madam-zhus-kitchen.html', 'snippet': 'Spicy and inventive, Hao Noodle and Tea impresses in Greenwich Village.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Spicy an