fence, a Smilax vine dangled menacingly pointed leaves, like a necklace of shark’s teeth. Beneath it, tiny wild daisies and mint ornamented the grass with pink tassels and purple cornets. Up above, on the sloping branches of oak trees, whiskery bromeliads, Spanish moss and the gray fronds of resurrection fern tangled in a miniature jungle all their own.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '64', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/magazine/18ethnobotany2/18ethnobotany2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/18/magazine/18ethnobotany2/18ethnobotany2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/magazine/18ethnobotany2/18ethnobotany2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/magazine/18ethnobotany2/18ethnobotany2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 799, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/18/magazine/18ethnobotany2/18ethnobotany2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 799}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/magazine/18ethnobotany2/18ethnobotany2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 769, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/magazine/18ethnobotany2/18ethnobotany2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2005, 'width': 1505, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Could Ancient Remedies Hold the Answer to the Looming Antibiotics Crisis?', 'kicker': 'Feature', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Flower Power', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTIBIOTICS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jabr, Ferris', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flowers and Plants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quave, Cassandra L', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bacteria', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chemistry', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Staphylococcus Aureus', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Emory University', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-14T09:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ferris Jabr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ferris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jabr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d981023-ae07-5d65-88ab-48c55ea24ac2', 'word_count': 4481, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d981023-ae07-5d65-88ab-48c55ea24ac2'}, {'abstract': 'It doesn’t actually get the wax out of your ears. But it can still provide a soothing ritual for a circle of friends.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/18/magazine/letter-of-recommendation-ear-candling.html', 'snippet': 'It doesn’t actually get the wax out of your ears. But it can still provide a soothing ritual for a circle of friends.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ear candles are widely and emphatically denounced by doctors as quackery. When burned, the little tubes of waxed gauze are supposed to create a vacuum effect just outside your 