iums are going up, the nonprofit Kaiser Family Foundation said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/15/business/health-insurance-analysis-kaiser.html', 'snippet': 'Although premiums haven’t risen significantly, workers’ deductibles and shares of those premiums are going up, the nonprofit Kaiser Family Foundation said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'State health insurance exchanges created under the new health care law are in turmoil. By contrast, the employer market — where the majority of Americans still get their coverage — seems like a bastion of stability.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Workers Pay More for Health Care as Companies Shift Burden, Survey Finds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Survey Finds Workers Pay a Bigger Share for Health Care', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abelson, Reed', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Employee Fringe Benefits', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kaiser Family Foundation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-14T15:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Reed Abelson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Reed', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abelson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b42b6b00-0268-55ca-9f78-52b5fd5bc8c5', 'word_count': 964, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b42b6b00-0268-55ca-9f78-52b5fd5bc8c5'}, {'abstract': 'Only Bartolo Colon has played as many seasons as the Texas Rangers’ Adrian Beltre and Carl