n the next decade. Officials are marketing the island to developers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/15/nyregion/plum-island-home-to-top-secret-lab-faces-uncertain-future.html', 'snippet': 'Journalists were given a glimpse of the federal Plum Island Animal Disease Center off Long Island, which will be closed within the next decade. Officials are marketing the island to developers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PLUM ISLAND, N.Y. — There have been comparisons to the H.G. Wells novel, “The Island of Dr. Moreau,” a nod from Hannibal Lecter in “The Silence of the Lambs,” and a murder mystery called “Plum Island,” by Nelson DeMille, in 1997. When the carcass of an unidentified animal was found on a Long Island beach a few years ago, it became popularly known as the Montauk Monster, and local residents said it had come from — where else? — Plum Island.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/15/nyregion/15PLUMISLAND1/15PLUMISLAND1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/15/nyregion/15PLUMISLAND1/15PLUMISLAND1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/15/nyregion/15PLUMISLAND1/15PLUMISLAND1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/15/nyregion/15PLUMISLAND1/15PLUMISLAND1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/15/nyregion/15PLUMISLAND1/15PLUMISLAND1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/15/nyregion/15PLUMISLAND1/15PLUMISLAND1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/15/nyregion/15PLUMISLAND1/15PLUMISLAND1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Home to High-Security Lab and Source of Rumors, Plum Island Faces Uncertain Future', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Uncertain Future for an 840-Acre Island of Intrigue', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Plum Island Animal Disease Center', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Livestock Diseases', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Laboratories and Scientific Equipment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Homeland Security Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Plum Island (NY)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Islands', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Land Use Policies', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parks and Other Recreation Areas', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-14T21:17:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline'