omas B. Edsall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/6044c8e3-8b7c-5f01-82ac-4facfaa5acd7', 'word_count': 1945, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6044c8e3-8b7c-5f01-82ac-4facfaa5acd7'}, {'abstract': 'Ending cable’s control over set-top boxes would result in lower costs and more choice for TV consumers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/15/opinion/free-tv-viewers-from-cable-box-fees.html', 'snippet': 'Ending cable’s control over set-top boxes would result in lower costs and more choice for TV consumers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'That little black cable box beside your television is your gateway to dozens of great shows. It’s also a drain, sucking money out of your home. Every month, millions of Americans are forced to pay high fees to rent cable boxes. The only way this can change is if the Federal Communications Commission votes to require cable companies to make programming accessible through other devices, ones you could own outright. A vote is set for Sept. 29.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/15/opinion/15thu2/15thu2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 591, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/15/opinion/15thu2/15thu2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 591}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/15/opinion/15thu2/15thu2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1008, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/15/opinion/15thu2/15thu2-superJumbo.jpg', 'hei