7e773566226a'}, {'abstract': 'Prosecutors and regulators have often struggled to find definitively who is at fault for misdeeds at big banks, while more easily penalizing small lenders.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/16/business/dealbook/wells-fargo-scandal-offers-a-chance-to-punish-big-bank-executives.html', 'snippet': 'Prosecutors and regulators have often struggled to find definitively who is at fault for misdeeds at big banks, while more easily penalizing small lenders.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Wells Fargo scandal puts size to a fresh regulatory test. Despite a settlement, the authorities aren’t finished with the bank’s fake-accounts scandal. Top executives at small lenders have been punished harshly in the past for misdeeds. If Wells Fargo executives escape any such fate, it could escalate tension over the accountability divide.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wells Fargo Scandal Offers a Chance to Punish Big Bank Executives', 'kicker': 'Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fines (Penalties)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Office of the Comptroller of the Currency', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wells Fargo & Company', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-15T19:32:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gina Chon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/720f4dd2-917f-56a0-a121-88a6f159c7ce', 'word_count': 356, 'uri': 'nyt://article/720f4dd2-917f-56a0-a121-88a6f159c7ce'}, {'abstract': 'Carmen Herrera is at last being celebrated at a major museum in New York with a solo show: “Lines of Sight,” a ravishing retrospective of about 50 works.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/16/arts/design/a-101-year-old-artist-finally-gets-her-due-at-the-whitney.html', 'snippet': 'Carmen Herrera is at last being celebrated at a major museum in New York with a solo show: “Lines of Sight,” a ravishing retrospective of about 50 works.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At 101, the artist Carmen Herrera is finally getting the show the art world should have given her 40 or 50 years ago: a solo exhibition at a major museum in New York, where she has been living and working since 1954. The show, “Carmen Herrera: Lines of Sight,” caps off several years of festivities, many of which have focused on the artist’s centenarian status, including a documentary film, “The 100 Years Show, Starring Carmen Herrera”; a spring exhibition of recent paintings at the Lisson Gallery in Chelsea; and numerous profiles hailing Ms. Herrera as a living treasure and praising her acerbic wit.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/16/arts/16CARMEN/16CARMEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 468, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/16/arts/16CARMEN/16CARMEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 468}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/16/arts/16CARMEN/16CARMEN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 798, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'ima