men.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/18/arts/dance/dance-this-fall-indian-mythology-and-ballets-by-women.html', 'snippet': 'Kathakali brings a dash of color to the White Light Festival in “Sounds of India,” and New York ballet companies present works by women.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Indian dance-theater genre Kathakali is exceptionally vivid, its characters often demonstrating a cartoonlike vitality. It’s on the cusp of theater and dance; in some performances, its core essence is music. The brightly colored and ornamented makeup is celebrated (some characters have green faces, some red): It’s like a crust, usually taking performers more than two hours to apply or have applied. The bright and complex costumes, with some characters in apparel like Elizabethan farthingales, are equally picturesque. Stories from Indian mythology are told, often from those central bodies of legend, the Ramayana and Mahabharata. Pictures from Kathakali often serve as cover imagery for guidebooks for India and become poster symbols for all that is most theatrically exotic.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '52', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/arts/18MACAULAY2SUB/18MACAULAY2SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/18/arts/18MACAULAY2SUB/18MACAULAY2SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/arts/18MACAULAY2SUB/18MACAULAY2SUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/arts/18MACAULAY2SUB/18MACAULAY2SUB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1361, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/arts/18MACAULAY2SUB/18MACAULAY2SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/18/arts/18MACAULAY2SUB/18MACAULAY2SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/arts/18MACAULAY2SUB/18MACAULAY2SUB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dance This Fall: Indian Mythology and Ballets by Women', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Indian Mythology and Geometric Movement', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'White Light Festival (Lincoln Center, NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kerala Kalamandalam Kathakali Troupe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN BALLET THEATER', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Ballet', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Theater Ballet', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-15T20:07:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d843ace-19a3-5114-9476-417ef57e732e', 'word_count': 772, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d843ace-19a3-5114-9476-417ef57e732e'}, {'abstract': 'Vail Dance Festival: ReMix NYC comes to City Center in the fall, reflecting the roots of the festival’s artistic director, Damian Woetzel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/18/arts/dance/vail-international-dance-festival-comes-to-new-york-city.html', 'snippet': 'Vail Dance Festival: ReMix NYC comes to City Center in the fall, reflecting the roots of the festival’s artistic director, Damian Woetzel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The notion of bringing the Vail International Dance Festival to New York sounds a little odd. The festival’s most obvious attraction is its alpine setting, and neither the mountain backdrop of its main stage nor the starry nights that frame most performances are exportable.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '52', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/arts/18VAIL/18VAIL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/18/arts/18VAIL/18VAIL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/arts/18VAIL/18VAIL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/arts/18VAIL/18VAIL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/18/arts/18VAIL/18VAIL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/arts/18VAIL/18VAIL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/arts/18VAIL/18VAIL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Rocky Mountain Dance Festival Makes its Way to New York', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Vail Visits New York', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vail International Dance Festival', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woetzel, Damian', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-15T20:07:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seibert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8ecbd23-7135-5a52-8c3f-27989dc66b91', 'word_count': 383, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8ecbd23-7135-5a52-8c3f-27989dc66b91'}, {'abstract': 'The Platform series at Danspace Project addresses the impact of AIDS on future generations of dance artists and the legacy of choreographers lost to that epidemic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/18/arts/dance/honoring-dance-innovators-lost-to-aids.html', 'snippet': 'The Platform series at Danspace Project addresses the impact of AIDS on future generations of dance artists and the legacy of choreographers lost to that epidemic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the past few decades, the veteran choreographer and improviser Ishmael Houston-Jones has become something of a godfather to Downtown dance. He is always on the lookout for new talent; beyond that, he is a guide, showing a younger generation how to grasp the bigger picture of the art form. This fall, Mr. Houston-Jones, 65, along with Will Rawls, a 37-year-old choreographer, performer and writer, will oversee Platform 2016: “Lost and Found” at Danspace Project.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '52', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/arts/18PLATFORM/18PLATFORM-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/18/arts/18PLATFORM/18PLATFORM-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/arts/18PLATFORM/18PLATFORM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 686, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/arts/18PLATFORM/18PLATFORM-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1371, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/arts/18PLATFORM/18PLATFORM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/18/arts/18PLATFORM/18PLATFORM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/arts/18PLATFORM/18PLATFORM-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Honoring Dance Innovators Lost to AIDS', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Finding the Work Lost to the AIDS Epidemic', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub