, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b27d7782-e4d0-5ffd-9886-12db2aabc08d', 'word_count': 3089, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b27d7782-e4d0-5ffd-9886-12db2aabc08d'}, {'abstract': 'A new catalog and an exhibition of paintings by the Texas artist Julian Onderdonk will illuminate the arduous New York phase of his career.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/16/arts/design/shedding-light-on-a-landscape-painters-lost-years-in-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'A new catalog and an exhibition of paintings by the Texas artist Julian Onderdonk will illuminate the arduous New York phase of his career.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The landscape painter Julian Onderdonk spent nearly half his career in New York, but tried to cover up that unprofitable phase of his life. Onderdonk, a San Antonio native who died in 1922 at 40, moved to Manhattan while a teenager, and worked prolifically under pseudonyms to support his family. This fall, a new book and an exhibition in Houston will contrast his largely forgotten scenes of Central Park snowbanks, marshy Bronx riverfronts and Manhattan water towers with his later popular views of sun-bleached dirt roads in Texas.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/16/arts/16ANTIQUES3/16ANTIQUES3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 499, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/16/arts/16ANTIQUES3/16ANTIQUES3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 499}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/16/arts/16ANTIQUES3/16ANTIQUES3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 852, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': N