': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85542339-1ca5-5e89-a431-c6a176f91736', 'word_count': 1203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85542339-1ca5-5e89-a431-c6a176f91736'}, {'abstract': 'Many places outside of Burgundy aspire to make great pinot noir. The Willamette Valley succeeds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/21/dining/wine-school-assignment-oregon-pinot-noir.html', 'snippet': 'Many places outside of Burgundy aspire to make great pinot noir. The Willamette Valley succeeds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a string of summery rosés and whites, it’s time to get back to red wine. Not that I am a seasonal stickler. I drink plenty of whites in cold weather and reds in warm. But the onset of autumn always makes me crave a red, so next up will be pinot noir from Oregon.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/21/dining/21WINE1/21WINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 407, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/21/dining/21WINE1/21WINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 407}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/21/dining/21WINE1/21WINE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 695, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/21/dining/21WINE1/21WINE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1391, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/21/dining/21WINE1/21WINE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail'