illsong — Let Hope Rise,” centered on a concert the Australian Christian band Hillsong United gave at the Forum in Los Angeles in 2014.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/16/arts/26HILLSONG/26HILLSONG-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/16/arts/26HILLSONG/26HILLSONG-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/16/arts/26HILLSONG/26HILLSONG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/16/arts/26HILLSONG/26HILLSONG-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/16/arts/26HILLSONG/26HILLSONG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/16/arts/26HILLSONG/26HILLSONG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/16/arts/26HILLSONG/26HILLSONG-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: In ‘Hillsong — Let Hope Rise,’ a Strumming Ministry Packs in Crowds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Hillsong: Let Hope Rise (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hillsong United (Music Group)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hillsong Church', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Warren, Michael John', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-15T20:48:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Webster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/46e3df5c-5707-5cb3-95c0-a277b87d97e0', 'word_count': 274, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46e3df5c-5707-5cb3-95c0-a277b87d97e0'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Morea, a major figure of the counterculture, is showing some of his works created in the 1960s at White Columns.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/16/arts/design/the-artist-ben-morea-returns-to-the-site-of-the-revolution.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Morea, a major figure of the counterculture, is showing some of his works created in the 1960s at White Columns.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Plenty of New York art world figures have taken umbrage at the Museum of Modern Art, but the painter Ben Morea may be the only one who has managed to shut it down. “They had the entrance of the museum barricaded, with cops behind it,” Mr. Morea, now 75, recalled of the day in 1966 when his manifesto targeting MoMA as one of the objects of a “total revolution, cultural as well as political and social” persuaded nervous museum staff members to bar the doors pre-emptively.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/16/arts/16MOREA/16MOREA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/16/arts/16MOREA/16MOREA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/16/arts/16MOREA/16MOREA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/16/arts/16MOREA/16MOREA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1333, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/16/arts/16MOREA/16MOREA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/16/arts/16MOREA/16MOREA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/16/arts/16MOREA/16MOREA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Artist Ben Morea Returns to the Site of the Revolution', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Returning to the Site of the Revolution', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morea, Ben', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of Modern Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'White Columns (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-15T20:52:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brett Sokol', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brett', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sokol', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/64f9960c-2f01-593a-a062-51df8db50d2d', 'word_count': 1114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64f9960c-2f01-593a-a062-51df8db50d2d'}, {'abstract': 'Hugh Hudson’s drama about the uncovering of cave paintings features Antonio Banderas as the 19th-century Spaniard who fought to prove their authenticity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/16/movies/finding-altamira-review.html', 'snippet': 'Hugh Hudson’s drama about the uncovering of cave paintings features Antonio Banderas as the 19th-century Spaniard who fought to prove their authenticity.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Finding Altamira” — Hugh Hudson’s stately account of events surrounding the discovery of Paleolithic cave paintings in northern Spain in 1879 — addresses a fascinating chapter in archaeology. Marcelino de Sautuola was an amateur scientist who owned the property where the paintings were found. Though the cave itself was known, it was Marcelino’s young daughter, Maria, who first noticed the Stone Age renderings, largely of bison and other animals. Many call the Cave of Altamira, now a Unesco site, the Sistine Chapel of prehistory.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/16/arts/16FINDINGALTAMARA/16FINDINGALTAMARA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/16/arts/16FINDINGALTAMARA/16FINDINGALTAMARA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image',