'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb758e74-41e8-58e1-bd45-2f87c7b05351', 'word_count': 253, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb758e74-41e8-58e1-bd45-2f87c7b05351'}, {'abstract': 'Alice Kaplan’s book about a book — Camus’s “The Stranger” — is part history, part biography and part literary criticism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/16/books/looking-for-the-stranger-alice-kaplan-camus.html', 'snippet': 'Alice Kaplan’s book about a book — Camus’s “The Stranger” — is part history, part biography and part literary criticism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the closing days of World War II, the American publisher Alfred A. Knopf was pursuing English-language rights to Albert Camus’s novel “The Plague,” with its powerful and clear allegorical view of Nazism. With hesitation, he also acquired Camus’s first novel, “The Stranger,” which one reader at the company described as “pleasant, unexciting reading” that seemed “neither very important nor very memorable.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/16/books/16book-1/16book-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 834, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/16/books/16book-1/16book-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 834}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/16/books/16book-1/16book-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 737, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/16/books/16book-1/16book-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1474, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/16/books/16book-1/16book-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/16/books/16book-1/16book-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/16/books/16book-1/16book-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘Looking for “The Stranger,”’ the Making of an Existential Masterpiece', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Making, and Musing On, an Existential Classic', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Camus, Albert', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "Looking for 'The Stranger': Albert Camus and the Life of a Literary Classic (Book)", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaplan, Alice', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Stranger (Book)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-15T20:53:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/6af89242-71ad-546f-81cf-a5446e4f73b0', 'word_count': 919, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6af89242-71ad-546f-81cf-a5446e4f73b0'}, {'abstract': 'Wednesday night included a celebration for Gucci’s newest collaboration, a dinner for Out of Order magazine and closing night for Made.', 'we