acy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/16/arts/16RASHIDJP1/16RASHIDJP1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 374}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/16/arts/16RASHIDJP1/16RASHIDJP1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 638, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/16/arts/16RASHIDJP1/16RASHIDJP1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1276, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/16/arts/16RASHIDJP1/16RASHIDJP1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/16/arts/16RASHIDJP1/16RASHIDJP1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/16/arts/16RASHIDJP1/16RASHIDJP1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In ‘Fly Away,’ Rashid Johnson Keeps the Focus on Race', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Mixed-Media Focus on Race', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Rashid (1977- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hauser & Wirth', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Fly Away (Exhibit)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-15T20:56:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roberta Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roberta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/12096c13-4305-5100-be1f-030203f3fd74', 'word_count': 1093, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12096c13-4305-5100-be1f-030203f3fd74'}, {'abstract': 'The Dutch documentarian Tom Fassaert pursues his own history, beginning with his 95-year-old grandmother in South Africa.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/16/movies/a-family-affair-review.html', 'snippet': 'The Dutch documentarian Tom Fassaert pursues his own history, beginning with his 95-year-old grandmother in South Africa.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Dutch documentarian Tom Fassaert (“An Angel in Doel”) delves into his own painful family history in the peculiar “A Family Affair.” The film begins with Mr. Fassaert’s 95-year-old grandmother, Marianne Cilliers, summoning the filmmaker to her home in South Africa. Marianne, who pursued a modeling career in the 1950s, intermittently relegated her two sons, Rob (Mr. Fassaert’s father) and his older brother, Rene, to orphanages. In later years, she invited Rob, his wife and children to live near her in South Africa, then reneged on certain pledges, and left them more or less stranded. Now, in the new century, she decides to entrust her story to her filmmaker grandson.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘A Family Affair,’ or Airing Dirty Laundry', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'A Family Affair (Movie)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fassaert, Tom (1979- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cilliers, Marianne', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Africa', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-15T20:58:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Glenn Kenny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Glenn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kenny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f184280d-7850-53b7-9c8d-ddeecef10116', 'word_count': 270, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f184280d-7850-53b7-9c8d-ddeecef10116'}, {'abstract': 'Katherine Ramsland has written many books on macabre subjects, but her latest volume takes a startling new form: a collaboration that lets a notorious murderer — Dennis Rader, a.k.a. the ‘B.T.K. Killer’ — tell his own story.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/15/magazine/the-serial-killers-co-author.html', 'snippet': 'Katherine Ramsland has written many books on macabre subjects, but her latest volume takes a startling new form: a collaboration that lets a notorious murderer — Dennis Rader, a.k.a. the ‘B.T.K. Killer’ — tell his own story.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By the time Katherine Ramsland and I stopped at the Copper Oven Cafe and Bakery in the Indian Hills Shopping Center in Wichita, Kan., it was well past lunchtime. It was June 2015, and Ramsland, a professor of forensic psychology and prolific author, was in this sedate city to wind up the last bit of research on “Confession of a Serial Killer,” her book about Dennis Rader, which was published this month by University Press of New England. She wore jean capris and a T-shirt and carried a favorite handbag, made of a soft black cloth and decorated with skulls.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/15/magazine/15radar1/15radar1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/15/magazine/15radar1/15radar1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/15/magazine/15radar1/15radar1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/15/magazine/15radar1/15radar1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/15/magazine/15radar1/15radar1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/15/magazine/15radar1/15radar1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/15/magazine/15radar1/15radar1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Serial Killer’s Co-Author', 'kicker': 'Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Serial Murders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-15T21:03:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Shteir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shteir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc87d3f6-5433-5548-a2df-b65b5685eec4', 'word_count': 2568, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc87d3f6-5433-5548-a2df-b65b5685eec4'}, {'abstract': 'The mother of Tamir, 12, who was fatally shot by the Cleveland police in 2014, has agreed to let the structure be used as part of an arts bank on Chicago’s South Side.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/16/us/tamir-rice-cleveland-chicago.html', 'snippet': 'The mother of Tamir, 12, who was fatally shot by the Cleveland police in 2014, has agreed to let the structure be used as part of an arts bank on Chicago’s South Side.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — At first, Samaria Rice wanted the park gazebo where her son, Tamir, was fatally shot by the Cleveland police in 2014 to simply disappear.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cleveland Gazebo Where Tamir Rice Was Shot Will Be Moved to Chicago', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Turning the Site of a Police Shooting Into ‘a Healing Space’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monuments and Memorials (Structures)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gates, Theaster', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rice, Tamir E (2002-14)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rice, Samaria', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cleveland (Ohio)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-15T21:04:16+0000', 'document_type': 'artic