ff25d', 'word_count': 864, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ccea27a0-8bb8-589c-bd38-ed3dc42ff25d'}, {'abstract': 'High school football players, let me try to persuade you why pulling a Kaepernick is counterproductive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/16/opinion/the-uses-of-patriotism.html', 'snippet': 'High school football players, let me try to persuade you why pulling a Kaepernick is counterproductive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This column is directed at all the high school football players around the country who are pulling a Kaepernick — kneeling during their pregame national anthems to protest systemic racism. I’m going to try to persuade you that what you’re doing is extremely counterproductive.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/16/opinion/16brooksWeb/16brooksWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 348, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/16/opinion/16brooksWeb/16brooksWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 348}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/16/opinion/16brooksWeb/16brooksWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 594, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/16/opinion/16brooksWeb/16brooksWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1187, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/16/opinion/16brooksWeb/16brooksWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/16/opinion/16brooksWeb/16brooksWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/16/opinion/16brooksWeb/16brooksWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Uses of Patriotism', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Uses  of  Patriotism', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Anthems', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaepernick, Colin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interscholastic Athletics', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-16T07:21:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd06e7b9-e9c5-5a6d-b6d7-d0debcf8b999', 'word_count': 813, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd06e7b9-e9c5-5a6d-b6d7-d0debcf8b999'}, {'abstract': 'The move could make the device available to patients with no co-pay. It could allow the company to raise prices while limiting complaints from the public.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/16/business/what-happens-if-epipens-get-the-preventive-label.html', 'snippet': 'The move could make the device available to patients with no co-pay. It could allow the company to raise prices while limiting complaints from the public.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mylan, the maker of EpiPens, an injection device for severe allergy attacks, is trying to persuade the United States Preventive Services Task Force to add the product to the group’s list of preventive medical services. That could make EpiPens available to patients with no insurance co-pay. It could also benefit the company by allowing it to raise prices on the product while limiting complaints from the public. The higher prices would be pushed to the government, insurers or employers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/16/business/16EPIPENLOBBY2/16EPIPENLOBBY2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 445, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/16/business/16EPIPENLOBBY2/16EPIPENLOBBY2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 445}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/16/business/16EPIPENLOBBY2/16EPIPENLOBBY2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 760, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/16/business/16EPIPENLOBBY2/16EPIPENLOBBY2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1519, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/16/business/16EPIPENLOBBY2/16EPIPENLOBBY2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/16/business/16EPIPENLOBBY2/16EPIPENLOBBY2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/16/business/16EPIPENLOBBY2/16EPIPENLOBBY2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Happens if EpiPens Get the ‘Preventive’ Label?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Preventive Medicine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medical Devices', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mylan Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epinephrine (Drug)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-16T07:30:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Abrams and Eric Lipton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abrams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lipton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eff56e1f-790c-53c9-9022-baad87fc7e13', 'word_count': 650, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eff56e1f-790c-53c9-9022-baad87fc7e13'}, {'abstract': 'Inclusion on a federal list would mean Mylan could keep its list price high — or even raise it — without patients’ complaining. But consumers would feel it indirectly.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/16/business/epipen-maker-mylan-preventative-drug-campaign.html', 'snippet': 'Inclusion on a federal list would mean Mylan could keep its list price high — or even raise it — without patients’ complaining. But consumers would feel it indirectly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON 