ds Are Round So Our Thoughts Can Change Direction (Exhibit)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Queens Museum', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Grey Art Gallery', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Museum', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Gallery of Art', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Guggenheim, Solomon R, Museum', 'rank': 18, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Whitney Museum of American Art', 'rank': 19, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hirshhorn Museum and Sculpture Garden', 'rank': 20, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Museum of Contemporary Art', 'rank': 21, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 22, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-16T16:32:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holland Cotter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holland', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cotter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d9f53e2-8769-5255-b67b-f7db82e48b82', 'word_count': 1356, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d9f53e2-8769-5255-b67b-f7db82e48b82'}, {'abstract': 'Many exhibitions devoted to artists who are not white or male will define the coming year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/18/arts/design/museums-embrace-the-unfamiliar.html', 'snippet': 'Many exhibitions devoted to artists who are not white or male will define the coming year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The curator’s job sounds relatively simple: just surprise us. Show us something we haven’t seen before, or lately, or in such depth, or with such clarity. Try to avoid the predictable and familiar, the market-approved or academically sanctioned, or what other curators have already done. Try to step outside your museum’s comfort zone or carefully manicured institutional persona with something eccentric, an intuitive leap. After all, there is plenty of art out there.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '76', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/arts/18SMITH1/18SMITH1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 959, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/18/arts/18SMITH1/18SMITH1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 959}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/arts/18SMITH1/18SMITH1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 641, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/arts/18SMITH1/18SMITH1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1282, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/arts/18SMITH1/18SMITH1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/18/arts/18SMITH1/18SMITH1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/arts/18SMITH1/18SMITH1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Museums Embrace the Unfamiliar', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Embracing the Unfamiliar', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Philadelphia Museum of Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Met Breuer', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MoMA PS1', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jewish Museum (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Dreamlands: Immersive Cinema and Art, 1905-2016 (Exhibit)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of Modern Art', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minorities', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-16T16:34:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roberta Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roberta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f620236-eb27-5cd9-9088-45a0b65dd57f', 'word_count': 988, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f620236-eb27-5cd9-9088-45a0b65dd57f'}, {'abstract': 'Last week’s galas included Cantor Fitzgerald’s annual Charity Day; special dinner and song for Lincoln Center trustees.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/18/fashion/eli-manning-michael-j-fox-sarah-ferguson-jeremy-lin-911-charity.html', 'snippet': 'Last week’s galas included Cantor Fitzgerald’s annual Charity Day; special dinner and song for Lincoln Center trustees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cantor Fitzgerald, which lost 658 employees in the attacks of Sept. 11, 2001, held its annual Charity Day last Monday. A stream of luminaries visited its Midtown offices, including Peyton and Eli Manning, Michael J. Fox and Sarah Ferguson, who joined brokers to complete trading calls, with all revenues donated to the Cantor Fitzgerald Relief Fund and other charities. About $12 million was raised. That night, the Lincoln Center trustees Dan Crown and his wife, Ellen, hosted a performance and dinner in their Park Avenue home. The Broadway star Justin Guarini performed for trustees and donors.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Eli Manning, Michael J. Fox and Sarah Ferguson at 9/11 Charity', 'kicker': 'Scene City', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Helping Hands', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Denny', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cantor Fitzgerald LP', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fox, Michael J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-16T16:36:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Denny Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Denny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bfc83cec-69dd-52fb-85e6-5d06bb94a07b', 'word_count': 96, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bfc83cec-69dd-52fb-85e6-5d06bb94a07b'}, {'abstract': 'Though they are increasingly rare, there are still New York bars where people can (discreetly) drink alongside their four-legged friends.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/18/nyregion/the-speakeasy-underworld-of-the-dog-bar.html', 'snippet': 'Though they are increasingly rare, there a