annual-cicadas-perform-their-final-mating-calls-of-the-season-in-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'The loud little creatures are generally camouflaged in green, black and brown, with none of the demonic, bright red highlights of their periodic cousins.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dog-day cicadas mature into vociferous adulthood during the hottest part of summer, when their steady droning builds in a crescendo and dominates muggy late afternoons. Also known as annual cicadas, these are not the periodic cicadas famous for their 13- or 17-year cycles.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/nyregion/18NATUREsub-1473950307062/18NATUREsub-1473950307062-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 833, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/18/nyregion/18NATUREsub-1473950307062/18NATUREsub-1473950307062-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 833}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/nyregion/18NATUREsub-1473950307062/18NATUREsub-1473950307062-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 738, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/nyregion/18NATUREsub-1473950307062/18NATUREsub-1473950307062-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2032, 'width': 1463, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/nyregion/18NATUREsub-1473950307062/18NATUREsub-1473950307062-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/18/nyregion/18NATUREsub-1473950307062/18NATUREsub-1473950307062-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/nyregion/18NATUREsub-1473950307062/18NATUREsub-1473950307062-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Annual Cicadas Perform Their Final Mating Calls of the Season in New York', 'kicker': 'N.Y.C. Nature', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sound of the Season', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cicadas (Insects)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-16T17:00:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metropolitan', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Taft', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taft', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9d8cb1c-0fb1-5173-9f9b-1144be4cc86c', 'word_count': 497, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9d8cb1c-0fb1-5173-9f9b-1144be4cc86c'}, {'abstract': 'While the years directly following the financial crisis were quiet ones for cultural construction, all that has changed, and not just in this country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/18/arts/design/millions-of-square-feet-billions-of-dollars-an-arts-universe-expands.html', 'snippet': 'While the years directly following the financial crisis were quiet ones for cultural construction, all that has changed, and not just in this country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you need proof of the adage “When the economy sneezes, the arts catch a cold,” consider this: Between 1994 and 2008, the United States added or expanded more than 700 cultural projects, valued at $15.5 billion, according to a University of Chicago study. By 2010, after the housing bubble had burst, “We were happy just to be invited to compete,” said Chris McVoy, senior partner in the New York City-based architecture firm of Steven Holl. “There simply wasn’t any arts-related work out there.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '102', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/arts/18ARCHITECT1/18ARCHITECT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 421, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/18/arts/18ARCHITECT1/18ARCHITECT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 421}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/arts/18ARCHITECT1/18ARCHITECT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 718, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/arts/18ARCHITECT1/18ARCHITECT1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1436, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/arts/18ARCHITECT1/18ARCHITECT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/18/arts/18ARCHITECT1/18ARCHITECT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/arts/18ARCHITECT1/18ARCHITECT1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Millions of Square Feet, Billions of Dollars: An Arts Universe Expands', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Amazing Expanding Arts Universe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Louvre Abu Dhabi', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Gallery of Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tate Modern', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of Contemporary Art (Chicago)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holl, Steven', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nouvel, Jean', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stern, Robert A M', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Herzog & de Meuron', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mecanoo (Architecture)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-16T17:00:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Reed Kroloff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Reed', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kroloff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f7f4bc2-3d73-58de-9a7a-47537b6b0387', 'word_count': 1398, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f7f4bc2-3d73-58de-9a7a-47537b6b0387'}, {'abstract': 'I watched Trump and the celebrity doctor with my patient, wishing health could really be that simple.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/18/opinion/sunday/whats-missing-in-dr-ozs-tv-exam-room.html', 'snippet': 'I watched Trump and the celebrity doctor with my patient, wishing health could really be that simple.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One afternoon during my final year of training to be a doctor, I interviewed to work on “The Dr. Oz Show.” I didn’t get to meet Mehmet Oz himself, but I did explore the back room full of products — weight-loss supplements, anti-aging tinctures, brightly colored workout bands. I joined the team for a lunchtime delivery of Pinkberry frozen yogurt with more toppings than I had ever seen. Later that afternoon, I returned to the sights and smells of sickness in the hospital pleasantly full of tart yogurt and chocolate chips and dreams of celebrity.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/opinion/sunday/18lamas/18lamas-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 598, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/18/opinion/sunday/18lamas/18lamas-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 598}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/opinion/sunday/18lamas/18lamas-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1020, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/opinion/sunday/18lamas/18lamas-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1274, 'width': 1279, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/opinion/sunday/18lamas/18lamas-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/18/opinion/sunday/18lamas/18lamas-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type