 'word_count': 1014, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8c6362e-5588-5317-a8fa-aeea379e082f'}, {'abstract': 'Two books, both by interested parties, examine a 1.3-mile restoration along the East River.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/18/nyregion/brooklyn-bridge-parks-long-path-to-development.html', 'snippet': 'Two books, both by interested parties, examine a 1.3-mile restoration along the East River.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The redevelopment of the World Trade Center site since 2001 has produced a number of tomes. Lynne B. Sagalyn’s “Power at Ground Zero” is already being hailed as a definitive history and a classic in urban studies. Two new books explore a somewhat less visible site across the East River, focusing on the tortured incubation of Brooklyn Bridge Park, which took even longer to develop but produced a 1.3-mile waterfront gem.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/nyregion/18BOOK2/18BOOK2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 542, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/18/nyregion/18BOOK2/18BOOK2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 542}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/nyregion/18BOOK2/18BOOK2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 925, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/nyregion/18BOOK2/18BOOK2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1850, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/nyregion/18BOOK2/18BOOK2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_na