As the Muslim holiday of Eid al-Adha wound down, Syrians squeezed in precious time with family and friends as the sound of explosions signaled a truce may be fraying.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — The weeklong vacation for the Muslim holiday of Eid al-Adha is nearing an end, and the partial cease-fire that began on Monday night is showing signs of fraying.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/17/world/17syria-voices2/17syria-voices2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/17/world/17syria-voices2/17syria-voices2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/17/world/17syria-voices2/17syria-voices2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/17/world/17syria-voices2/17syria-voices2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/17/world/17syria-voices2/17syria-voices2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/17/world/17syria-voices2/17syria-voices2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/17/world/17syria-voices2/17syria-voices2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rags, Tea and Advice as Syrians Fret Over Cease-Fire', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Humanitarian Aid', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-16T22:29:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anne Barnard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0f2bc89-b51c-579c-8235-02c901508e0a', 'word_count': 1071, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0f2bc89-b51c-579c-8235-02c901508e0a'}, {'abstract': 'The survey found that women think that more progress has been made toward ending sexism than racism in society, but they perceive that men still hold advantages.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/17/us/politics/president-poll-women-hillary-clinton.html', 'snippet': 'The survey found that women think that more progress has been made toward ending sexism than racism in society, but they perceive that men still hold advantages.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Nov. 8, American voters for the first time in history will see a woman’s name on the ballot as a major party’s nominee for president. A broad majority of voters — men and women — say they are happy this milestone has been reached, but fully half of them say they would have preferred that that first woman not be Hillary Clinton, according to the latest New York Times/CBS News poll.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/17/us/17womenpoll-web1sub/17womenpoll-web1sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/17/us/17womenpoll-web1sub/17womenpoll-web1sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/17/us/17womenpoll-web1sub/17womenpoll-web1sub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/17/us/17womenpoll-web1sub/17womenpoll-web1sub-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1358, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/17/us/17womenpoll-web1sub/17womenpoll-web1sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/17/us/17womenpoll-web1sub/17womenpoll-web1sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/17/us/17womenpoll-web1sub/17womenpoll-web1sub-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Poll Finds Most Voters Embrace Milestone for Women, if Not Hillary Clinton', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spot on Ballot Is No Cure-All, Women Say in Poll', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thee-Brenan, Megan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murphy, Mary Jo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-16T22:31:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mary Jo Murphy and Megan Thee-Brenan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': 'Jo', 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Megan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thee-Brenan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f3a9fcb-a744-5e2b-be57-52aab367e1a2', 'word_count': 1187, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f3a9fcb-a744-5e2b-be57-52aab367e1a2'}, {'abstract': 'The survey of 1,770 adults from Sept. 9 through 13 used random sampling methods to ensure proper representation in terms of region, sex, race and other factors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/17/us/how-the-new-york-times-cbs-news-poll-was-conducted.html', 'snippet': 'The survey of 1,770 adults from Sept. 9 through 13 used random sampling methods to ensure proper representation in terms of region, sex, race and other factors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The latest New York Times/CBS News Poll is based on telephone interviews conducted from Sept. 9 through 13 with 1,770 adults throughout the United States. Of those, 865 were women and 905 were men.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How the New York Times/CBS