 acrostic from Emily Cox and Henry Rathvon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VARIETY PUZZLE — Leslie Savan’s “The Sponsored Life: Ads, T.V. and American Culture” is a 90s look at the pervasive influence of advertising. I had never heard of this author or book, but fortunately I was able to fill in just enough clues to slowly cobble together the grid. One of my first certain solves, incidentally, was LUFTHANSA based on the advertising line “Nonstop you”; so I guess I’m among the crowd in thrall of the catchy hook.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Variety: The Acrostic', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-17T16:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Games', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Caitlin Lovinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Caitlin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9938210b-9dfe-5635-bbe4-b263a0fbdf6c', 'word_count': 294, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9938210b-9dfe-5635-bbe4-b263a0fbdf6c'}, {'abstract': 'Scenes from the spring/summer 2017 collections which were presented in London on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2016/09/17/t-magazine/fashion/ryan-lo-ashley-williams-london-fashion-week.html', 'snippet': 'Scenes from the spring/summer 2017 collections which were presented in London on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scenes from the spring/summer 2017 collections which were presented in London on Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/17/t-magazine/fashion/ryan-lo-ashley-williams-slide-FF5M/ryan-lo