of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9440af9-301b-531c-ae68-88d1f43afc76', 'word_count': 1186, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9440af9-301b-531c-ae68-88d1f43afc76'}, {'abstract': 'Helping immigrants gain access to health insurance is both sound fiscal policy and good public health policy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/18/opinion/californias-nifty-idea-on-immigrant-health-care.html', 'snippet': 'Helping immigrants gain access to health insurance is both sound fiscal policy and good public health policy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Affordable Care Act has helped 20 million people gain health insurance, but it explicitly excludes one group: undocumented immigrants. Now, lawmakers in California want to help change that by letting all immigrants purchase policies on the state’s insurance marketplace without federal subsidies. This is a good idea that the Obama administration should support.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/opinion/18sun3web/18sun3web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/18/opinion/18sun3web/18sun3web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/opinion/18sun3web/18sun3web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/opinion/18sun3web/18sun3web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/opinion/18sun3web/18sun3web-