t': 'A robust consumer protection bureau is needed to protect the public from unfair, deceptive and abusive practices.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/18/opinion/sunday/bashing-the-hero-in-the-wells-fargo-case.html', 'snippet': 'A robust consumer protection bureau is needed to protect the public from unfair, deceptive and abusive practices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Consumer Financial Protection Bureau has rightly emerged as the hero in the story this month about fraudulent practices at Wells Fargo. The bureau was the lead agency in the investigation of the bank, where some 5,300 employees (now fired) illegally opened millions of unauthorized bank and credit card accounts in customers’ names in order to meet aggressive sales targets.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/opinion/sunday/18sun2/18sun2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 471, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/18/opinion/sunday/18sun2/18sun2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 471}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/opinion/sunday/18sun2/18sun2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 804, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/opinion/sunday/18sun2/18sun2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1547, 'width': 1970, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/opinion/sunday/18sun2/18sun2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/18/opinion/sunday/18sun2/18sun2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/opinion/sunday/18sun2/18sun2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bashing the Hero in the Wells Fargo Case', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bashing the Hero in Wells Fargo Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wells Fargo & Company', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Financial Protection Bureau', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-17T18:30:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/96c214c9-62a1-59db-b4ea-662ab84cf381', 'word_count': 474, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96c214c9-62a1-59db-b4ea-662ab84cf381'}, {'abstract': 'Trump’s paid leave plan is flawed, leaves out fathers — and represents real progress.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/18/opinion/campaign-stops/the-fight-working-moms-won.html', 'snippet': 'Trump’s paid leave plan is flawed, leaves out fathers — and represents real progress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Working mothers, take note: You have won the culture war. Now you are making advances in the policy battle. This presidential race has become, at least in part, a debate over how best to help you balance work and home, not whether you should be working at all.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/opinion/sunday/18bryce/18bryce-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 261, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/18/opinion/sunday/18bryce/18bryce-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 261}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/opinion/sunday/18bryce/18bryce-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 445, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/opinion/sunday/18bryce/18bryce-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 891, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/opinion/sunday/18bryce/18bryce-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/18/opinion/sunday/18bryce/18bryce-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/opinion/sunday/18bryce/18bryce-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Fight Working Moms Won', 'kicker': 'Contributing Op-Ed Writer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Fight Working Moms Won', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Work-Life Balance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Covert, Bryce', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Family Leaves', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-17T18:30:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Campaign Stops', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bryce Covert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bryce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Covert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/c39a3c16-b390-57cc-a3d3-256f71fff27d', 'word_count': 1147, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c39a3c16-b390-57cc-a3d3-256f71fff27d'}, {'abstract': 'The next commander in chief will face no good options in Afghanistan. But we need a plan that is better than the current policy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/18/opinion/sunday/the-afghan-war-quagmire.html', 'snippet': 'The next commander in chief will face no good options in Afghanistan. But we need a plan that is better than the current policy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Eight years ago, President Obama pledged to wind down the war in Iraq and redouble efforts to defeat the Taliban in Afghanistan. “As president, I will make the fight against Al Qaeda and the Taliban the top priority that it should be,” he said during a campaign speech. “This is a war that we have to win.”', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/opinion/18sun1web/18sun1web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/18/opinion/18sun1web/18sun1web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/opinion/18sun1web/18sun1web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/opinion/18sun1web/18sun1web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/opinion/18sun1web/18sun1web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/18/opinion/18sun1web/18sun1web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/18/opinion/18sun1web/18sun1web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Afghan War Quagmire', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Afghan War Quagmire', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001-14)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}