e as to the exact appearance and the construction of the new engine of war. ‘‘The Tank may be roughly described as a dry-land submarine,’’ says ‘‘one who has seen them’’ in an interview with the ‘‘Star.’’ ‘‘The headroom inside the great tortoise is naturally limited, and the crew is selected for its lack of inches.’’ — The New York Herald, European Edition, Sept. 20, 1916', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/20/blogs/20oldiht-1916-tanks/20oldiht-1916-tanks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/20/blogs/20oldiht-1916-tanks/20oldiht-1916-tanks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/20/blogs/20oldiht-1916-tanks/20oldiht-1916-tanks-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/20/blogs/20oldiht-1916-tanks/20oldiht-1916-tanks-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/20/blogs/20oldiht-1916-tanks/20oldiht-1916-tanks-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/20/blogs/20oldiht-1916-tanks/20oldiht-1916-tanks-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/20/blogs/20oldiht-1916-tanks/20oldiht-1916-tanks-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_