nyt://article/92060405-e32d-553f-b640-cb17316277ab', 'word_count': 550, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92060405-e32d-553f-b640-cb17316277ab'}, {'abstract': 'In her first foreign policy speech as prime minister, Mrs. May reassured the United Nations that Britain remained a responsible international player.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/21/world/europe/theresa-may-britain-unga-2016-united-nations.html', 'snippet': 'In her first foreign policy speech as prime minister, Mrs. May reassured the United Nations that Britain remained a responsible international player.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Theresa May, Britain’s new prime minister, in her first speech before the United Nations General Assembly on Tuesday, vowed that Britain would remain an important and responsible international player despite its vote to leave the European Union.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Theresa May Makes Her Debut as the Voice of Britain', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Assembly (UN)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'May, Theresa M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-19T16:12:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Erlanger and Stephen Castle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/266ea057-2d0b-52fc-882a-d57d6ac9b3f3', 'word_count': 407, 'uri': 'nyt://article/266ea057-2d0b-52fc-882a-d57d6ac9b3f3'}, {'abstract': 'In the West Village, lush tarts, cookies and cakes from a former investment banker.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/21/dining/mah-ze-dahr-bakery.html', 'snippet': 'In the West Village, lush tarts, cookies and cakes from a former investment banker.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Umber Ahmad was an investment banker whose specialty was the global expansion of food brands. Tom Colicchio was a client, and they talked food. After Ms. Ahmad treated him to samples of her cakes and cookies she grew up baking with members of her Pakistani family in northern Michigan, he encouraged her to go into the business. Since founding Mah-Ze-Dahr Bakery in 2013, she has been baking in a commercial kitchen with Shelly Barbera, her executive pastry chef and partner, and selling her finely wrought pastries online to consumers as well as to wholesale clients like Jet Blue. And finally, a long year later than expected, she has a spacious West Village shop, opening Thursday, that’s done in pearl gray with a tufted banquette and marble displays for her lush tarts, cookies, cream puffs, bars, cakes, brioche doughnuts and other sweet and savory items. There’s a back room with a communal table that she plans to use for classes, and a big kitchen downstairs. The name of the company is based on the Urdu word mazedar, meaning “the essence”: Mah-Ze-Dahr Bakery, 28 Greenwich Avenue (10th Street), 212-498-9810, mahzedahrbakery.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/21/dining/21BURNER-BAKERY/21BURNER-BAKERY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/21/dining/21BURNER-BAKERY/21BURNER-BAKERY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/21/dining/21BURNER-BAKERY/21BURNER-BAKERY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/21/dining/21BURNER-BAKERY/21BURNER-BAKERY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/21/dining/21BURNER-BAKERY/21BURNER-BAKERY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/21/dining/21BURNER-BAKERY/21BURNER-BAKERY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/21/dining/21BURNER-BAKERY/21BURNER-BAKERY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After a Long Wait, Mah-Ze-Dahr Bakery Gets a Shop', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Indulge: Mah-Ze-Dahr Bakery  Gets a Shop', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bakeries and Baked Products', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Colicchio, Tom', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Village (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mah-Ze-Dahr Bakery (Manhattan, NY, Bakery)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ahmad, Umber', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-19T16:13:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72515f03-0e83-5b0e-b53e-8d5efc4420f0', 'word_count': 188, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72515f03-0e83-5b0e-b53e-8d5efc4420f0'}, {'abstract': '“I can’t see anyone more assimilated than that guy,” a family friend said of the young Somali man who stabbed 10 people in an attack claimed by ISIS.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/20/us/obama-st-cloud-minnesota.html', 'snippet': '“I can’t see anyone more assimilated than that guy,” a family friend said of the young Somali man who stabbed 10 people in an attack claimed by ISIS.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ST. CLOUD, Minn. — The man who the police say stabbed 10 people at a mall here on Saturday seemed like a model of assimilation, not a violent jihadist, people who knew him and his family said. The son of Somali refugees, he lived in the United States most of his life, did well in school, played sports, worked as a security guard and took classes at a local college.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/20/us/20minnesota1/20minnesota-1474326410664-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/20/us/20minnesota1/20minnesota-1474326410664-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/20/us/20minnesota1/20minnesota-1474326410664-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'c