.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mitch Smith and Richard Pérez-Peña', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mitch', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pérez-Peña', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a12cef8-e20e-56e6-9929-83dc6bb5dee9', 'word_count': 1196, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a12cef8-e20e-56e6-9929-83dc6bb5dee9'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Johnson quickly corrected himself on Twitter after misspeaking about terrorist attacks in New York and Minneapolis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/20/us/politics/another-slip-for-the-libertarian-nominee-gary-johnson-nobody-got-hurt.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Johnson quickly corrected himself on Twitter after misspeaking about terrorist attacks in New York and Minneapolis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gary Johnson, the Libertarian Party presidential candidate, who has struggled in recent weeks to recover from a gaffe in which he was unable to identify Aleppo, in war-torn Syria, appeared to fumble once more on Sunday when he said no one had been injured in two violent events in New York City and Minnesota over the weekend.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/20/nyregion/20xp-johnson/20xp-johnson-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/20/nyregion/20xp-johnson/20xp-johnson-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/20/nyregion/20xp-johnson/20xp-johnson-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': '