e Mets’ year-round training complex. They were all there — on the ground, in the air — to watch Tim Tebow play catch.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tim Tebow, Wearing No. 15, Participates in First Mets Workout', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Starting at Bottom, With a Cheering Section', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waldstein, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tebow, Tim', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-19T18:12:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9267fc5f-1136-522b-ab6c-78fb1c0a8a0c', 'word_count': 921, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9267fc5f-1136-522b-ab6c-78fb1c0a8a0c'}, {'abstract': 'A meditation on family and legacy from my teacher and friend, Edward Albee.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/19/opinion/me-and-prof-edward-albee.html', 'snippet': 'A meditation on family and legacy from my teacher and friend, Edward Albee.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We were sitting in his loft in TriBeCa, Edward Albee and I, talking about families. Edward and his partner, the artist Jonathan Thomas, had never had children (“It never occurred to us, never for a second”). They did raise Irish wolfhounds, though. I once asked Edward how many Irish wolfhounds could fit in a king-size bed with two grown men in it, and without hesitation, he provided the answer: seven.', 'sourc