09/19/t-magazine/art/martino-gamper-friends-london-design-festival-no-ordinary-love.html', 'snippet': 'Martino Gamper recruited 13 creative comrades, including Max Lamb and Bethan Laura Wood, to create objects for a new show in London.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With its pristine rows of untouched Victorian villas, Launceston Place is one of the most picturesque corners of the West London district of Kensington. It’s also home to the enterprising art and design upstart Seeds, which is dotted with reminders of the building’s former incarnations as a butcher shop and cheese factory: The intimate gallery and selling space, which opened in January, has meat hooks suspended from the ceiling and ornate ceramic tiling on the walls. “I didn’t want to make it a blank white box,” explains the founder Nathalie Assi, pointing to an antiquated wrought-iron stove where cheese was once made in the redbrick basement kitchen. “We really wanted to preserve its previous life.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/19/t-magazine/art/martino-gamper-slide-VA42/martino-gamper-slide-VA42-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/19/t-magazine/art/martino-gamper-slide-VA42/martino-gamper-slide-VA42-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/19/t-magazine/art/martino-gamper-slide-VA42/martino-gamper-slide-VA42-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/19/t-magazine/art/martino-gamper-slide-VA42/martino-gamper-slide-VA42-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 506, 'width': 600, 'subType':