rical fantasy “Orlando” — which tells the tale of a young Elizabethan nobleman — gave rise to what the makeup artist Wendy Rowe called “beautiful statuesque skin” backstage at Burberry today. The collection was renamed September 2016 (as opposed to spring/summer 2017), because everything, including the makeup used for the look, is shoppable straight after the show. The matte finish of the skin mirrored the many antique statues that filled Burberry’s labyrinth “Maker’s House” venue on the edges of London’s Soho.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/19/t-magazine/fashion/19tmag-bbr-01/19tmag-bbr-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 928, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/19/t-magazine/fashion/19tmag-bbr-01/19tmag-bbr-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 928}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/19/t-magazine/fashion/19tmag-bbr-01/19tmag-bbr-01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 662, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/19/t-magazine/fashion/19tmag-bbr-01/19tmag-bbr-01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1324, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/19/t-magazine/fashion/19tmag-bbr-01/19tmag-bbr-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/19/t-magazine/fashion/19tmag-bbr-01/19tmag-bbr-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image'