diq Khan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'de Blasio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hidalgo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Sadiq', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Khan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/765e7635-2d55-58a9-9710-62059456ea45', 'word_count': 764, 'uri': 'nyt://article/765e7635-2d55-58a9-9710-62059456ea45'}, {'abstract': 'He didn’t win the nomination. Can he help get other people elected?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/20/opinion/campaign-stops/the-bernie-bump.html', 'snippet': 'He didn’t win the nomination. Can he help get other people elected?', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW PALTZ, N.Y. — This crunchy college town, between the Hudson River and the Catskill Mountains, feels like an ideal place for a Woodstock attendee to retire. Amble down Main Street, and you’ll see a yoga studio, a gluten-free bakery and a clothing store called the Groovy Blueberry. “I’m already against the NEXT war,” a passing bumper sticker reads.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/20/opinion/20rollerWeb/20rollerWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/20/opinion/20rollerWeb/20rollerWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/20/opinion/20rollerWeb/20rollerWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', '