t money.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Great partnerships are often forged when each party enjoys a surplus of something the other needs, and there’s little conflict in their ambitions. By that logic, two of Silicon Valley’s best-known firms, Apple and Tesla Motors, really need each other right now. An investment in Tesla by Apple in return for some of the carmaker’s innovation dust might be just the ticket.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Tesla and Apple Could Be Good for Each Other', 'kicker': 'Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Driverless and Semiautonomous Vehicles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Innovation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tesla Motors Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Musk, Elon', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cook, Timothy D', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-20T20:25:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Cox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5fd64809-f047-577c-a82a-90679a63ce95', 'word_count': 1125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5fd64809-f047-577c-a82a-90679a63ce95'}, {'abstract': 'Our reporter Julia Moskin spent a week cooking in Julia Child’s kitchen in the South of France.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2016/09/21/dining/julia-child-kitchen-la-pitchoune.html', 'snippet': 'Our reporter Julia Moskin spent a week cooking in Julia Child’s kitchen in the South of France.', 'lead_par