ion. They were perfecting the marigold hue that features prominently in the spring/summer 2017 collection for their brand, Olderbrother. “Turmeric is a known natural dye, but making it stable, so that a garment can see sunlight or go in the washing machine, takes a while,” Kingery says. He likens the process to cooking (although not all their ingredients are edible), another inexact science. For example, they created a black indigo because Kingery made a mathematical error. “We really stumbled into that one,” he says.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Brand to Know: Basics That Champion an Eco-Friendly Agenda', 'kicker': 'On the Verge', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Almost Edible', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sustainable Living', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dyes and Dyestuffs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Textiles', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-20T20:35:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Fashion & Beauty', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hilary Moss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hilary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f868d868-8907-5b99-8301-166715012f5c', 'word_count': 531, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f868d868-8907-5b99-8301-166715012f5c'}, {'abstract': 'The Tulsa Police Department released video on Monday of a white police officer fatally shooting an unarmed black man in Tulsa, Okla.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/us/100000004660026/shooting-of-terence-crutcher-by-tulsa-police.html', 'snippet': 'The Tulsa Police Department re