mon Wayans and Clayne Crawford; and CBS’s “MacGyver,” with Lucas Till, is to debut.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/21/arts/television/review-lethal-weapon-and-macgyver-2-80s-reboots-1-with-chemistry.html', 'snippet': 'Fox’s “Lethal Weapon” TV series may develop some intrigue with Damon Wayans and Clayne Crawford; and CBS’s “MacGyver,” with Lucas Till, is to debut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s chemistry versus cleverness in this week’s battle of the 1980s reboots. And the winner is — well, neither of them is mandatory viewing, but if you have to watch one, go with chemistry.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/21/arts/21LETHAL1/21LETHAL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 416, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/21/arts/21LETHAL1/21LETHAL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 416}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/21/arts/21LETHAL1/21LETHAL1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 709, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/21/arts/21LETHAL1/21LETHAL1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1418, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/21/arts/21LETHAL1/21LETHAL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/21/arts/21LETHAL1/21LETHAL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/21/arts/21LETHAL1/21LETHAL1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘Lethal Weapon’ and ‘MacGyver,’ 2 ’80s Reboots, 1 With Chemistry', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Two 1980s Reboots, One With Chemistry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Lethal Weapon (TV Program)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'MacGyver (TV Program)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wayans, Damon', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crawford, Clayne', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Till, Lucas', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corporation', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-20T21:12:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/997f2486-277b-5a70-97f3-398bfc86165a', 'word_count': 530, 'uri': 'nyt://article/997f2486-277b-5a70-97f3-398bfc86165a'}, {'abstract': 'Twice a year, when the “mangoes are really good,” Lily and Hopie Stockman of Block Shop return to Rajasthan to oversee production of scarves, quilts and rugs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/20/t-magazine/design/block-shop-travel-diary-india.html', 'snippet': 'Twice a year, when the “mangoes are really good,” Lily and Hopie Stockman of Block Shop return to Rajasthan to oversee production of scarves, quilts and rugs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Twice a year for a month at a time, when the tourists melt away in the heat and the “mangoes are really good,” the sisters Lily and Hopie Stockman return to Rajasthan, India, where they have been traveling for the last five years to oversee the production of their textiles line, Block Shop. Beloved for its wood-printed scarves — which are conveyed along the international style route by such retailers as Playmountain in Tokyo and the Hammer Museum shop in Los Angeles — the label recently grew to include topstitched quilts and flat rugs known as dhurries that reflect, as Hopie explains, the subcontinent’s “mashed-up” confluence of overland influences: including “pre-partition” cotton weaving techniques, the dusky desert palette and the visual principles of jaali, stacked geometric forms found in Mughal and Islamic architecture.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '66', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Trip to India With the Sisters Behind a Cult-Favorite Textile Label', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Textiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carpets and Rugs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Block Shop', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jaipur (India)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-20T21:12:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Design & Interiors', 'byline': {'original': 'By Su Wu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Su', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aedf6f97-09a8-5152-afec-2b5e7f3ebc0e', 'word_count': 415, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aedf6f97-09a8-5152-afec-2b5e7f3ebc0e'}, {'abstract': 'This choreographer’s new work, part of the Next Wave Festival at the Brooklyn Academy of Music, is his latest effort to leave audiences with feelings that linger.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/21/arts/dance/john-jasperse-hopes-remains-lasts-after-the-dancing-stops.html', 'snippet': 'This choreographer’s new work, part of the Next Wave Festival at the Brooklyn Academy of Music, is his latest effort to leave audiences with feelings that linger.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s one thing, on an intellectual level, to grasp how ephemeral dance is. Coming to grips with it emotionally is something else. There’s plenty of excitement in fleetingness, but that can also lead to heartbreak. No, dance may not leave any tangible remains, but the choreographer John Jasperse sees another possibility.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/21/arts/21JASPERSE2/21JASPERSE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/21/arts/21JASPERSE2/21JASPERSE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/21/arts/21JASPERSE2/21JASPERSE2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/21/arts/21JASPERSE2/21JASPERSE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/21/arts/21JASPERSE2/21JASPERSE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth