f_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc935d66-da75-583d-94f9-c719d3ba0fb7', 'word_count': 1202, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc935d66-da75-583d-94f9-c719d3ba0fb7'}, {'abstract': 'The corrections officers, who worked in Fishkill, were accused of severely injuring Kevin Moore, tearing out his dreadlocks and lying about the encounter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/22/nyregion/new-york-officers-downstate-correctional-facility-inmate-beating.html', 'snippet': 'The corrections officers, who worked in Fishkill, were accused of severely injuring Kevin Moore, tearing out his dreadlocks and lying about the encounter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the night three years ago when Kevin Moore’s dreadlocks were ripped out and his ribs and facial bones were broken, a group of New York State corrections officers involved in a confrontation with him said that they were the victims, that Mr. Moore, a 56-year-old inmate, had attacked them.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Five New York Prison Guards Charged in ’13 Beating of Inmate', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Prison Guards Are Charged in ’13 Beating of an Inmate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prison Guards and Corrections Officers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winerip, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moore, Kevin (1960- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Downstate Correctional Facility (Fishkill, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assaults', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morris, Carson (Fishkill, NY, Corrections Officer)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santiago, George Jr', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scott, Kathy L', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fishkill (NY)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-21T13:16:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Winerip and Michael Schwirtz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Winerip', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwirtz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7644289b-598a-5886-a9e7-d2c1eba0b8d5', 'word_count': 962, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7644289b-598a-5886-a9e7-d2c1eba0b8d5'}, {'abstract': 'A Texas man found a collection of old baseball cards and entered a 1957 contest sponsored by Bazooka that omitted the year of the deadline. The company delivered.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/22/us/a-baseball-card-contest-pays-off-6-decades-after-the-fact.html', 'snippet': 'A Texas man found a collection of old baseball cards and entered a 1957 contest sponsored by Bazooka that omitted the year of the deadline. The company delivered.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the years, Darwin Day, a 70-year-old resident of Grand Prairie, Tex., had given away so many baseball cards from his childhood that he didn’t think he had any left. But one that he found recently paid off when he entered a contest from 1957: He won a new baseball glove.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/15/sports/15xp-glove_web1/15xp-glove_web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/15/sports/15xp-glove_web1/15xp-glove_web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xla