erseas territories, warned that an independence vote would mean that France will wash its hands of its last African colony and cut off most aid to it. Information Minister Yvon Bourges said after a cabinet meeting presided over by President Charles de Gaulle that a bill authorizing the referendum would be introduced in parliament. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Sept. 22, 1966', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/22/blogs/22oldiht-1966-somalia/22oldiht-1966-somalia-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/22/blogs/22oldiht-1966-somalia/22oldiht-1966-somalia-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/22/blogs/22oldiht-1966-somalia/22oldiht-1966-somalia-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/22/blogs/22oldiht-1966-somalia/22oldiht-1966-somalia-jumbo.png', 'height': 336, 'width': 274, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/22/blogs/22oldiht-1966-somalia/22oldiht-1966-somalia-superJumbo.png', 'height': 336, 'width': 274, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1966: Paris Plans Somali Plebiscite', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Somaliland', 'rank': 2, 'major': '