s to live-action ones: a staggering masterpiece that can never be seen in its ideal form. “Ambersons,” directed by Orson Welles, was completed but then mutilated by its studio, its original version lost; “Cobbler,” a dream project the animator Richard Williams had been working on since the 1960s, was wrested from him by financiers in 1993, incomplete by about 15 minutes.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/22/arts/22THIEF/22THIEF-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 237, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/22/arts/22THIEF/22THIEF-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 237}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/22/arts/22THIEF/22THIEF-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 404, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/22/arts/22THIEF/22THIEF-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 808, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/22/arts/22THIEF/22THIEF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/22/arts/22THIEF/22THIEF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/22/arts/22THIEF/22THIEF-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: A Rough Cut of ‘The Thief and the Cobbler’ Makes It to MoMA', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rough Magic: A Lost Classic  Makes It to the Museum', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Richard (1933-2019)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Thief and the Cobbler: A Moment in Time (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Thief and the Cobbler (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMATED FILMS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of Modern Art', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-21T22:04:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Glenn Kenny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Glenn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kenny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/53676388-fa58-54da-811d-b71403538eac', 'word_count': 312, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53676388-fa58-54da-811d-b71403538eac'}, {'abstract': 'Our critic Charles Isherwood prizes epic theater. Here’s his take on two inspired long-form works coming to an end in New York at roughly the same time.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/22/theater/forget-twitter-id-rather-binge-theater.html', 'snippet': 'Our critic Charles Isherwood prizes epic theater. Here’s his take on two inspired long-form works coming to an end in New York at roughly the same time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s often said that we live in an era that prizes speed and brevity above all else. There’s long been fast food, but now there’s fast fashion, too. Why take the time to phone someone when an email will take less of your time? Why send an email when a text message would be quicker?', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1',