': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/45e40881-ca3f-5845-bb07-1e133a813d86', 'word_count': 665, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45e40881-ca3f-5845-bb07-1e133a813d86'}, {'abstract': 'The federal government argued that the fraught relationship between the companies ran counter to their defense in the case.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/22/business/dealbook/anthem-and-cigna-accuse-each-other-of-breaching-merger-deal.html', 'snippet': 'The federal government argued that the fraught relationship between the companies ran counter to their defense in the case.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Justice Department, which is suing Anthem and Cigna to block their $48 billion deal, revealed on Wednesday in court documents that the two health insurers have been accusing each other of breaching their merger agreement.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Anthem and Cigna Accuse Each Other of Breaching Merger Deal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'While Battling U.S., Anthem and Cigna Are Also Sniping at Each Other', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Picker, Leslie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ANTHEM INC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CIGNA Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-21T22:19:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leslie Picker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leslie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Picker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2711a6b-249e-5033-9a1a-6a41ca735361', 'word_count': 493, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2711a6b-249e-5033-9a1a-6a41ca735361'}, {'abstract': 'On the moody “I Had a Dream That You Were Mine,” Mr. Leithauser and Rostam shamble through styles and approaches without fretting over how all the pieces will fit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/22/arts/music/hamilton-leithauser-rostam-review.html', 'snippet': 'On the moody “I Had a Dream That You Were Mine,” Mr. Leithauser and Rostam shamble through styles and approaches without fretting over how all the pieces will fit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hamilton Leithauser has one of the most tactile voices in rock: a coarse yet viscous instrument, like wet concrete. So it’s striking that he keeps returning to the intangible, the realm of phantasm and reverie, on “I Had a Dream That You Were Mine,” his persuasively moody new collaboration with the producer and multi-instrumentalist known as Rostam.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/22/arts/22ALBUMREVIEW/22ALBUMREVIEW-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/22/arts/22ALBUMREVIEW/22ALBUMREVIEW-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/22/arts/22ALBUMREVIEW/22ALBUMREVIEW-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subTyp