'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-22T10:50:20+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By THE NEW YORK TIMES MAGAZINE', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/9947a924-cebc-52fc-add4-0173d892068a', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/9947a924-cebc-52fc-add4-0173d892068a'}, {'abstract': 'On the visual — and psychological — contradictions of pictures from the road.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/25/magazine/what-we-see-when-we-look-at-travel-photography.html', 'snippet': 'On the visual — and psychological — contradictions of pictures from the road.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is a vast gulf between how people tend to think of “tourism,” an agreeable pursuit for themselves and a great benefit to their local economy, and how people tend to think of other tourists, as interlopers, beholden to oafish appetites for packaged experience. Those of us who travel professionally, with a view to record for those at home our encounters on the road, try to bridge that perceptual divide. This can be uncomfortable. Tourists in bad faith, we are paid to elevate our naïve consumption (of city, museum, vista, ruin, breakfast) to the level of a vocation. The internal anxiety that this contradiction inspires in us often gets displaced, in an amusing way, onto others on the same circuit. Professional travelers like nothing better than the opportunity to point out the crumminess of other professional travelers.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '41', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/25/magazine/25essay1/25mag-25essay-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 406, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/25/magazine/25essay1/25mag-25essay-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 406}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/25/magazine/25essay1/25mag-25essay-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 693, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/25/magazine/25essay1/25mag-25essay-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1385, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/25/magazine/25essay1/25mag-25essay-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/25/magazine/25essay1/25mag-25essay-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/25/magazine/25essay1/25mag-25essay-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What We See When We Look at Travel Photography', 'kicker': 'The Voyages Issue', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On the Road', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lewis-Kraus, Gideon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Road Trips', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Instagram Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Levi-Strauss, Claude', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {