retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/09/22/1966-peace-move-would-end-assault/', 'snippet': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: The United States offer to stop bombing North Vietnam if Hanoi takes similar action towards the U.S. forces, during the Vietnam War in September 1966.', 'lead_paragraph': 'United Nations — The United States offered today [Sept. 22] to stop bombing North Vietnam and begin pulling out its troops if Hanoi would take corresponding action to de-escalate the fighting. U.S. Ambassador Arthur J. Goldberg, making a major policy declaration, told the 118-member General Assembly that the United States was willing to undertake first steps provided North Vietnam showed through public or private response it was ready to reciprocate. The United States, Mr. Goldberg said, does not seek to make South Vietnam a permanent U.S. ally. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Sept. 23, 1966', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/blogs/23oldiht-1966-vietnam/23oldiht-1966-vietnam-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/23/blogs/23oldiht-1966-vietnam/23oldiht-1966-vietnam-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/blogs/23oldiht-1966-vietnam/23oldiht-1966-vietnam-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/blogs/23oldiht-1966-vietnam/23oldiht-1966-vietnam-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 526, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/23/blogs/23oldiht-1966-vietnam/23oldiht-1966-vietnam-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 526}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/blogs/23oldiht-1966-vietnam/23oldiht-1966-vietnam-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 805, 'width': 919, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/blogs/23oldiht-1966-vietnam/23oldiht-1966-vietnam-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 805, 'width': 919, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1966: Peace Move Would End Assault', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'UNITED STATES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hanoi (Vietnam)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vietnam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'VIETNAM WAR', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-22T10:55:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9985f83-35df-537e-a1e8-32e852899ac1', 'word_count': 100, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9985f83-35df-537e-a1e8-32e852899ac1'}, {'abstract': 'The soprano is playing Isolde in this Wagner opera at the Met. Here, she discusses a passing moment in the first act.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/25/arts/music/my-favorite-page-nina-stemme-on-a-love-and-loss-in-tristan-und-isolde-wagner.html', 'snippet': 'The soprano is playing Isolde in this Wagner opera at the Met. Here, she discusses a passing moment in the first act.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nina Stemme’s favorite page from the score of Wagner’s “Tristan und Isolde” is a surprising one: not Isolde’s closing “Liebestod” or the great love scene, but a passing moment in the first act. Isolde, eyeing Tristan but addressing herself and her maid, Brangäne, laments that Tristan is destined for her but has been taken from her. She reveals her love for him by tracing the yearning theme that dominates the opera but resolves that such love must end in death. Hers are a “Todgeweihtes Haupt” and a “Todgeweihtes Herz” — a head and heart fated for the grave. Here are edited excerpts from a conversation with Ms. Stemme about the sequence.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nina Stemme on a Love and Loss in ‘Tristan und Isolde’', 'kicker': 'My Favorite Page', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Love and Lose', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Allen, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stemme, Nina', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wagner, Richard', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Tristan und Isolde (Opera)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-22T10:59:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Allen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Allen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c93d6bd0-3753-5b63-879d-a01f4f1ecbb2', 'word_count': 502, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c93d6bd0-3753-5b63-879d-a01f4f1ecbb2'}, {'abstract': 'His effort to halt the government’s plan to transfer oversight of the internet’s master directory of website addresses seems set to find purchase in a congressional measure.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/23/us/politics/ted-cruz-internet.html', 'snippet': 'His effort to halt the government’s plan to transfer oversight of the internet’s master directory of website addresses seems set to find purchase in a congressional measure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A plan to help revive the Export-Import Bank seems to be headed for the legislative cutting-room floor. A Republican dream of weakening pesticide regulations has been scotched. But the short-term spending bill that Congress is set to pass next week, one that both parties tried to use to promote various policies, will most likely include a provision championed by Senator Ted Cruz, Republican of Texas, a frequent troublemaker on all matters fiscal.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/22/us/22fdnl-cruz/22fdnl-cruz-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/22/us/22fdnl-cruz/22fdnl-cruz-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/22/us/22fdnl-cruz/22fdnl-cruz-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/22/us/22fdnl-cruz/22fdnl-cruz-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit':