 years of rightward drift in their party.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/23/opinion/jeremy-corbyn-and-the-problem-with-electability.html', 'snippet': 'If Labour members re-elect a left-wing firebrand as their leader, they’ll undo years of rightward drift in their party.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Jeremy Corbyn’s tenure since last September as leader of the Labour Party has been bumpy, to say the least: The party now has the worst poll ratings in its history. Labour’s parliamentary members have complained that Mr. Corbyn cannot manage them. And his tenure has been troubled by poor decisions — he chose, for example, to go to a Cuba solidarity event on the same day that Theresa May, the new prime minister, announced the formation of her cabinet, leaving the opposition with no public response. Mr. Corbyn was widely considered a lackluster campaigner in the effort to persuade British voters that their country should remain in the European Union.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/opinion/23ohagan-inytA/23ohagan-inytA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/23/opinion/23ohagan-inytA/23ohagan-inytA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/opinion/23ohagan-inytA/23ohagan-inytA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/opinion/23ohagan-inytA/23ohagan-inytA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/opinion/23ohagan-inytA/23ohagan-inytA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/23/opinion/23ohagan-inytA/23ohagan-inytA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/opinion/23ohagan-inytA/23ohagan-inytA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jeremy Corbyn and the Problem With ‘Electability’', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Corbyn corrective', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Labour Party (Great Britain)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blair, Tony', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Corbyn, Jeremy (1949- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miliband, Edward S', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-22T12:56:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': "By Ellie Mae O'Hagan", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ellie', 'middlename': 'Mae', 'lastname': "O'Hagan", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc4501e2-2a71-5232-993c-b067ca816539', 'word_count': 1032, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc4501e2-2a71-5232-993c-b067ca816539'}, {'abstract': 'Instead of continuing aid for security forces that have a dire human rights record, America should back calls for an independent investigation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/23/opinion/end-us-support-for-the-thugs-of-honduras.html', 'snippet': 'Instead of continuing aid for security forces that have a dire human rights record, America should back calls for an independent investigation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Santa Cruz, Calif. — Around midnight on March 2, the indigenous peoples’ rights and environmental activist Berta Cáceres was shot dead by gunmen who entered her residence in La Esperanza, Honduras. A longtime campaigner against illegal logging operations, Ms. Cáceres had been repeatedly threatened because of her opposition to the Agua Zarca hydroelectric project, one of the largest of its kind in Central America.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/opinion/23Frank-inyt/23Frank-inyt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/23/opinion/23Frank-inyt/23Frank-inyt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/opinion/23Frank-inyt/23Frank-inyt-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/opinion/23Frank-inyt/23Frank-inyt-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/23/opinion/23Frank-inyt/23Frank-inyt-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/opinion/23Frank-inyt/23Frank-inyt-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/opinion/23Frank-inyt/23Frank-inyt-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'End U.S. Support for the Thugs of Honduras', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. aids thugs of Honduras', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Honduras', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Caceres, Berta', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-22T13:20:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dana Frank', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Frank', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b619707-8555-524e-8e2f-8d773dd6c0a0', 'word_count': 952, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b619707-8555-524e-8e2f-8d773dd6c0a0'}, {'abstract': 'The Met will welcome visitors to the front of the opera house for free self-guided tours on weekdays, from 10 a.m.-2 p.m., starting Oct. 4.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/23/arts/music/metropolitan-opera-tour-front-house.html', 'snippet': 'The Met will welcome visitors to the front of the opera house for free self-guided tours on weekdays, from 10 a.m.-2 p.m., starting Oct. 4.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As opera companies around the world try to remove the barriers that can inhibit newcomers, the Metropolitan Opera is experimenting with a literal approach. The Met plans to throw open its gates and welcome visitors to the front of the opera house for free on weekdays beginning next month, the company announced Thursday.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_pag