cent next year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/23/world/africa/fees-must-fall-anatomy-of-the-student-protests-in-south-africa.html', 'snippet': 'Protests by university students flared up after a government proposal that university fees could increase as much as 8 percent next year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'University students protested in South Africa for at least a second day this week over plans to increase fees at the country’s colleges in 2017. The protests, which erupted in September, have turned violent as students have clashed with the police.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Fees Must Fall’: Anatomy of the Student Protests in South Africa', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ITT Technical Institute', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Cape Town', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rhodes, Cecil', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Johannesburg (South Africa)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Stellenbosch (South Africa)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Africa', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of the Witwatersrand', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-22T17:58:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 