d the New York premiere of John Corigliano’s “STOMP” and an animated performance by the pianist Aaron Diehl.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/23/arts/music/review-a-safe-start-to-alan-gilberts-final-season-with-the-philharmonic.html', 'snippet': 'The season-opening gala concert included the New York premiere of John Corigliano’s “STOMP” and an animated performance by the pianist Aaron Diehl.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alan Gilbert began his tenure as music director of the New York Philharmonic in September  2009 by turning the traditional season-opening gala concert into a strong statement of artistic purpose. Conductors at orchestras everywhere are under institutional pressure to make these gala programs, which also function as fund-raisers for patrons, light and festive. Mr. Gilbert’s inaugural challenged this notion.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/arts/23NYPHIL/23NYPHIL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/23/arts/23NYPHIL/23NYPHIL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/arts/23NYPHIL/23NYPHIL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/arts/23NYPHIL/23NYPHIL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/23/arts/23NYPHIL/23NYPHIL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/arts/23NYPHIL/23NYPHIL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/arts/23NYPHIL/23NYPHIL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: A Safe Start to Alan Gilbert’s Final Season With the Philharmonic', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Celebrating a New York Institution', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gilbert, Alan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tommasini, Anthony', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Philharmonic', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-22T21:13:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Tommasini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tommasini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c80a7257-cf3d-5c11-b871-185a1acf26f7', 'word_count': 788, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c80a7257-cf3d-5c11-b871-185a1acf26f7'}, {'abstract': 'This documentary by Menachem Daum and Oren Rudavsky focuses on the fate of an old Arab village on the outskirts of Jerusalem.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/23/movies/the-ruins-of-lifta-review.html', 'snippet': 'This documentary by Menachem Daum and Oren Rudavsky focuses on the fate of an old Arab village on the outskirts of Jerusalem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Among the hills on the western outskirts of Jerusalem stands an abandoned group of stone buildings, the remains of Lifta, an Arab village whose residents were driven out in 1948, during what Israelis know as the War of Independence and what Palestinians call the Nakba (Catastrophe). Plans to demolish the homes and build a new development have drawn opposition from an Israeli-Palestinian coalition seeking to preserve the site.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: In ‘The Ruins of Lifta,’ a Dispute Amid the Rubble', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Daum, Menachem', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Arab-Israeli War (1948)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rudavsky, Oren', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jerusalem (Israel)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-22T21:13:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel M. Gold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ae31a8c-cc30-55d7-88a7-81290945388f', 'word_count': 289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ae31a8c-cc30-55d7-88a7-81290945388f'}, {'abstract': 'Times Opinion columnist Andrew Rosenthal on the Chelsea bombing, racial profiling, Lewis Black, and Times Op-Docs. Susan Lehman is host.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2016/09/22/insider/22-insider-andy-AUDIO.html', 'snippet': 'Times Opinion columnist Andrew Rosenthal on the Chelsea bombing, racial profiling, Lewis Black, and Times Op-Docs. Susan Lehman is host.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Times Opinion columnist Andrew Rosenthal on the Chelsea bombing, racial profiling, Lewis Black, and Times Op-Docs. Susan Lehman is host.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Good, Bad and Mad: Times Opinion Columnist Andrew Rosenthal on the News', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-09-22T21:13:36+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Times Insider', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/a6777d67-a1b8-5c60-9ee5-24568be23220', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/a6777d67-a1b8-5c60-9ee5-24568be23220'}, {'abstract': 'Kai Althoff’s major exhibition at MoMA features more than 200 works folded into a confusing installation of found materials.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/23/arts/design/the-paintings-are-delicate-the-shows-a-shambles.html', 'snippet': 'Kai Althoff’s major exhibition at MoMA features more than 200 works folded into a confusing installation of found materials.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some artists may be at odds with their own talents and wish they could be something more than they are. A spectacular example of such a conflicted creative sensibility is “Kai Althoff: and then leave me to the common swifts (und dann überlasst mich den Mauerseglern)” at the Museum of Modern Art, which has more than 200 of Mr. Althoff’s poetically allusive, delicately made paintings, drawings and sculptures folded into an unfortunately messy and confusing installation of found materials.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/arts/23KAI1/23KAI1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'c