(Exhibit)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-22T22:09:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holland Cotter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holland', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cotter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/48187cbd-fad9-5a51-a5fa-d9022e90664e', 'word_count': 1435, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48187cbd-fad9-5a51-a5fa-d9022e90664e'}, {'abstract': 'Inspired by the memorably scary 1973 movie, a new Fox series starring Geena Davis, Ben Daniels and Alfonso Herrera enlists two contrasting priests.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/23/arts/television/review-the-exorcist-reboots-a-battle-against-a-demonic-presence.html', 'snippet': 'Inspired by the memorably scary 1973 movie, a new Fox series starring Geena Davis, Ben Daniels and Alfonso Herrera enlists two contrasting priests.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The Exorcist,” a horror series that begins Friday on Fox, has two demons to fight. Some viewers will be measuring it against what they consider to be one of the scariest movies the genre has ever produced, the 1973 film directed by William Friedkin. Others, schooled on decades’ worth of parodies of that same movie (especially its projectile-vomiting and 360-degree-head-spinning scenes), will be on the lookout for anything in the TV show that might be laughably ineffective or pretentious.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/arts/23EXORCIST/23EXORCIST-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/23/arts/23EXORCIST/23EXORCIST-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/arts/23EXORCIST/23EXORCIST-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/arts/23EXORCIST/23EXORCIST-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 376, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/23/arts/23EXORCIST/23EXORCIST-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 376}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/arts/23EXORCIST/23EXORCIST-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 642, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/arts/23EXORCIST/23EXORCIST-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1283, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘The Exorcist’ Reboots a Battle Against a Demonic Presence', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Daughter’s Acting Oddly? Call a Can-Do Priest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Exorcist (TV Program)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Geena', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-22T22:12:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger