: 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/us/23CHARLOTTE-sub3/23CHARLOTTE-sub3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Questions for: ‘Charlotte Police Are Urged to Release Video of Shooting’', 'kicker': 'Article of the Day', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-09-23T11:47:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Learning', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d0c66d3-95c9-5e6a-9837-20dda15d4754', 'word_count': 281, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d0c66d3-95c9-5e6a-9837-20dda15d4754'}, {'abstract': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: Collaboration between France’s Vichy government and Germany’s Nazi regime are evident in September 1941.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/09/23/1941-signs-of-vichy-collaboration/', 'snippet': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: Collaboration between France’s Vichy government and Germany’s Nazi regime are evident in September 1941.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VICHY — Signs of a renewal of political activity, probably along the lines of Franco-German collaboration, were evident in Vichy today, after the summer lull. Marshal Henri Pétain is back in the provisional capital after a visit to the Alpine province of Savoy, and Jacques Benoist-Mechin, Under Secretary of State, is on his way here from Paris. Benoist-Mechin, one of the most ardent collaborationists, has his office in Paris, where he is in fact, if not titularly, the most important representative of the Pétain government. His return to Vichy follows discussions with Otto Abetz, the German Ambassador at Paris. Informed quarters here say they expect no important developments in Franco-German relations soon, but it is cautiously admitted that Benoist-Mechin’s visit here signifies a ‘‘resumption of contacts’’ with the Nazis. — New York Herald Tribune, Sept. 24, 1941', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/24/blogs/24oldiht-1941-nazi/24oldiht-1941-nazi-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 792, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/24/blogs/24oldiht-1941-nazi/24oldiht-1941-nazi-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 792}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/24/blogs/24oldiht-1941-nazi/24oldiht-1941-nazi-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 777, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/24/blogs/24oldiht-1941-nazi/24oldiht-1941-nazi-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1194, 'width': 905, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/24/blogs/24oldiht-1941-nazi/24oldiht-1941-nazi-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/24/blogs/24oldiht-1941-nazi/24oldiht-1941-nazi-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/24/blogs/24oldiht-1941-nazi/24oldiht-1941-nazi-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name':