nyt://article/efb737bd-91bf-57e0-ae29-39b97002c4da'}, {'abstract': 'Amanda Chantal Bacon, who founded the L.A.-based wellness brand, is releasing recipes, and life tips, in print.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/23/t-magazine/food/moon-juice-cookbook-recipes-amanda-chantal-bacon.html', 'snippet': 'Amanda Chantal Bacon, who founded the L.A.-based wellness brand, is releasing recipes, and life tips, in print.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Amanda Chantal Bacon, the founder of the L.A.-based wellness brand Moon Juice, owns countless cookbooks but can’t remember ever having followed a recipe, preferring to page through them for inspiration, often in bed. To that end, she sees her own first book, out next month, as more guide than manual, for anyone who wants to rethink their entire food philosophy\xad — though it does contain recipes, 75 of them, for things like green-juice-and-kelp gazpacho, almond milk kefir and chia sesame dough.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '64', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/21/t-magazine/21tmag-moonjuice/21tmag-moonjuice-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/21/t-magazine/21tmag-moonjuice/21tmag-moonjuice-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/21/t-magazine/21tmag-moonjuice/21tmag-moonjuice-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/21/t-magazine/21tmag-moonjuice/21tmag-moonjuice-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'ima