 J (1954- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Muir-Wood, Robert', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schwartz, Judith D', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Olson, Steve (1956- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Thirty-Eight: The Hurricane That Transformed New England (Book)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Cure for Catastrophe: How We Can Stop Manufacturing Natural Disasters (Book)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Water in Plain Sight: Hope for a Thirsty World (Book)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Eruption: The Untold Story of Mount St Helens (Book)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-23T14:47:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kim Tingley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tingley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0c1f89e-1b39-53ea-b266-1cf9b07b476b', 'word_count': 976, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0c1f89e-1b39-53ea-b266-1cf9b07b476b'}, {'abstract': 'The notion that life, including intelligent life, exists beyond Earth seems more persuasive than ever. Four new books take a look at the search, and the searchers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/25/books/review/search-for-extraterrestrial-intelligence.html', 'snippet': 'The notion that life, including intelligent life, exists beyond Earth seems more persuasive than ever. Four new books take a look at the search, and the searchers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In October of 1995, two Swiss astronomers announced a major discovery: They had detected, about 50 light-years from Earth, a planet orbiting a sun-like star. Scientists had long imagined there were such planets outside our solar system, but never before had one been confirmed. This extrasolar planet, or “exoplanet,” appeared to be a Jupiter-like ball of gas and liquid with a blistering atmospheric temperature of 1,700 degrees Fahrenheit. In the two decades since, astronomers have detected more than 3,000 exoplanets. No one has yet found a replica of Earth, although Proxima b, an Earth-size planet in a temperate orbit a mere 4.2 light-years away, whose discovery was announced last month, sounds as if it could be a decent place to live.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/25/books/review/0925-BKS-IvoryTower/0925-BKS-IvoryTower-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/25/books/review/0925-BKS-IvoryTower/0925-BKS-IvoryTower-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/25/books/review/0925-BKS-IvoryTower/0925-BKS-IvoryTower-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/25/books/review/0925-BKS-IvoryTower/0925-BKS-IvoryTower-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 984, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/25/books/review/0925-BKS-IvoryTower/0925-BKS-IvoryTower-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 984}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/25/books/review/0925-BKS-IvoryTower/0925-BKS-IvoryTower-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 625, 'subType': 'j