739da839', 'word_count': 1334, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21634fcf-cd62-5007-a7a8-7a05739da839'}, {'abstract': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: A Russian minister emphases the possibility of a war in Europe during the Vietnam war in September 1966.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/09/23/1966-war-threat-in-europe/', 'snippet': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: A Russian minister emphases the possibility of a war in Europe during the Vietnam war in September 1966.', 'lead_paragraph': 'UNITED NATIONS — Soviet Foreign Minister Andrei A. Gromyko pulled a surprise in his speech today [Sept. 23] to the General Assembly by placing more emphasis on the potential for war in Europe than on the actual conflict in Vietnam. Mr. Gromyko did castigate the United States for its ‘‘barbaric bombing’’ of North Vietnam and for ‘‘military interference in the affairs of Cambodia and Laos.’’ ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1966: War Threat in Europe', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vietnam War', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'USSR (Former Soviet Union)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-23T14:50:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/769db757-9a07-5a77-90af-81b33e240383', 'word_count': 171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/769db757-9a07-5a77-90af-81b33e240383'}, {'abstract': 'The nomination of Donald J. T