ct': 'Hey, at the new National Museum of African American History and Culture in Washington, one four-word line from the poem gets a whole wall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/23/insider/3-questions-langston-hughes-poem-anchors-entire-page.html', 'snippet': 'Hey, at the new National Museum of African American History and Culture in Washington, one four-word line from the poem gets a whole wall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Times Insider delivers behind-the-scenes insights into how news, features and opinion come together at The New York Times. Below, Alicia DeSantis and Wayne Kamidoi, the graphics editor and art director behind The Times’s stand-alone print section on the Smithsonian’s new National Museum of African American History and Culture in Washington, share their rationale for devoting the section’s whole back page to “I, Too.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/arts/22INSIDERHUGHES/22INSIDERHUGHES-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/23/arts/22INSIDERHUGHES/22INSIDERHUGHES-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/arts/22INSIDERHUGHES/22INSIDERHUGHES-thumbLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/arts/22INSIDERHUGHES/22INSIDERHUGHES-articleLarge-v5.jpg', 'height': 620, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/23/arts/22INSIDERHUGHES/22INSIDERHUGHES-articleLarge-v5.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 620}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'capti