cs and Pottery', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collectors and Collections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Christie's", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Sotheby's", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Far East, South and Southeast Asia and Pacific Areas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-23T16:01:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Reyburn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reyburn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7033e68f-499e-5671-8294-8b32558d1551', 'word_count': 1013, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7033e68f-499e-5671-8294-8b32558d1551'}, {'abstract': 'For this issue, we decided to take a closer look at the meaning of design and why we make certain choices.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/23/t-magazine/ts-new-design-luxury-issue-editors-letter.html', 'snippet': 'For this issue, we decided to take a closer look at the meaning of design and why we make certain choices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Design is so pervasive, argues Michael Rock in his Sign of the Times essay, that it often appears as fact rather than the result of subjective decision-making. After a period of time, an idea that originally evolved from mores, habits or customs becomes so codified and ingrained that it takes on the air of inevitability. For this issue, we decided to take a closer look at the meaning of design and why we make certain choices, from the wild natural beauty of Isabel and Julian Bannerman’s garden to the fine attention to detail in the rising designer Billy Cotton’s interiors. We considered the psychological effects of design, from the standpoint of a mad collector, the young fashion designer Jonathan Anderson, to what happens when it all goes terribly wrong. Of course, we also celebrate the vast range of the designed world: teapots, interesting hairdos, clever companies, artists’ communities, fabric, paint and rugs, jewels, clothing, even plumbing. Added up, these stories are a call to see design more clearly, to appreciate what is all around us, but also to realize the delicacy of ingenuity — that none of it had to be quite this way, and yet it is. And, to recognize that if something isn’t working, we can try to design its change.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '54', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/t-magazine/23tmag-edletter/23tmag-edletter-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 327, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/23/t-magazine/23tmag-edletter/23tmag-edletter-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 327}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/t-magazine/23tmag-edletter/23tmag-edletter-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 558, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/t-magazine/23tmag-edletter/23tmag-edletter-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1116, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/t-magazine/23tmag-edletter/23tmag-edletter-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/23/t-magazine/23tmag-edletter/23tmag-edletter-thumbStandard.jpg', 