, 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Suliman, Adela', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslim Americans', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jerrahi, Fariha al-', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-23T16:49:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metropolitan', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adela Suliman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adela', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Suliman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0b00861-267a-58af-852c-626a2bad4c38', 'word_count': 2035, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0b00861-267a-58af-852c-626a2bad4c38'}, {'abstract': 'Her appearance with Zack Galifianakis showed her as bemused and withering. Will she show that side on Monday night’s debate?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/23/magazine/hillary-clinton-between-two-ferns.html', 'snippet': 'Her appearance with Zack Galifianakis showed her as bemused and withering. Will she show that side on Monday night’s debate?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yesterday, Hillary Clinton arguably had one of her most effective public appearances in months, and it happened on the website Funny or Die. Clinton appeared as a guest on “Between Two Ferns” with Zach Galifianakis, a semi-aggressive, extremely rumpled comedian and sort-of talk show host who makes David Letterman look painfully earnest by comparison. The show has a glaringly low-rent aesthetic, like something made in an office park, circa 1981, by a bunch of interns with time on their hands. That sensibility — self-mocking, on-the-fly and D.I.Y. — is very 2016.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'c