a musical impresario ever closer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/25/fashion/weddings/drawn-to-a-jazzwoman-and-her-trumpets-clarion-call.html', 'snippet': 'A fateful ride around and around Manhattan brings a jazz musician and a musical impresario ever closer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On their first official date, Bria Skonberg, the jazz trumpeter and vocalist, and Matthew Papper, who would later become the artistic director of Town Hall, circumnavigated Manhattan in a yellow cab. More than twice.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Drawn to a Jazzwoman and Her Trumpet’s Clarion Call', 'kicker': 'Vows', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Drawn to a Jazzwoman and Her Trumpet’s Clarion Call', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ellin, Abby', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Town Hall (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vows (Times Column)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-23T18:03:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Society', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': 'Weddings', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abby Ellin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ellin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/495d711a-75f3-5c7d-8fec-e6a9bed33a73', 'word_count': 2015, 'uri': 'nyt://article/495d711a-75f3-5c7d-8fec-e6a9bed33a73'}, {'abstract': 'Share your concerns, and hopes, for the future.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/23/education/if-i-were-president-of-my-club-my-class-my-college-my-country.html', 'snippet': 'Share your concerns, and hopes, for the future.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Students, send us — in words, drawings or pictures — what you would do if you were in charge. We want to know your concerns, and hopes, for the future. Would you make college free? Ban drinking? Build a safe space, or a wall around campus? Why, and what would that look like? Written entries should be no more than 150 words. Provide the name of your school, class and a photo credit. Please email your submissions to edlife@nytimes.com. Selections are being posted here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/education/edlife/23callout/23callout-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/23/education/edlife/23callout/23callout-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/education/edlife/23callout/23callout-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/education/edlife/23callout/23callout-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/education/edlife/23callout/23callout-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/23/education/edlife/23callout/23callout-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/education/edlife/23callout/23callout-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'If I Were President … of My Club, My Class, My College, My Country', 'kicker': 'Photo Booth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-09-23T18:05:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'EdLife', 'section_name': 'Education', 'subsection_name': 'Education Life', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8f3a1ac-a7cf-5396-8bb8-978252271bae', 'word_count': 84, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8f3a1ac-a7cf-5396-8bb8-978252271bae'}, {'abstract': 'A by-no-means exhaustive list of items we like.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/23/t-magazine/some-things-t-editors-are-really-into-right-now.html', 'snippet': 'A by-no-means exhaustive list of items we like.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The designer and DwellStudio founder Christiane Lemieux’s new book is chock-full of inspiring interiors — and mini-guides to understanding the most fundamental elements of a great room. From the history of wallpaper to the evolution of a frame, “The Finer Things” breaks down furniture, textiles and details — and how to incorporate them — to show how good design is truly the sum of its parts. It’s probably a perfect housewarming gift, if such a thing exists. $60, amazon.com. — ALAINNA LEXIE BEDDIE', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/t-magazine/fashion/23tmag-editorspicks-slide-N4NE/23tmag-editorspicks-slide-N4NE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/23/t-magazine/fashion/23tmag-editorspicks-slide-N4NE/23tmag-editorspicks-slide-N4NE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnai