', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In California, Grenache Packs More Than Power', 'kicker': 'Wines of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In California, Grenache Packs More Than Power', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Asimov, Eric', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grapes', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-23T18:11:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Asimov', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Asimov', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2614ad55-fa1e-5d15-bdb0-ef50e1fcd54d', 'word_count': 1625, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2614ad55-fa1e-5d15-bdb0-ef50e1fcd54d'}, {'abstract': 'The pileup of prejudices in the premiere’s final scene bodes well for how the show will handle its newfound interest in intersectionality.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/23/arts/television/transparent-season-3-premiere-recap.html', 'snippet': 'The pileup of prejudices in the premiere’s final scene bodes well for how the show will handle its newfound interest in intersectionality.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After seven decades on Earth, Maura Pfefferman finally has everything she ever wanted. In an early scene from the Season 3 premiere, she lists her blessings: a loving girlfriend (Anjelica Huston is back as Vicki), supportive kids, meaningful volunteer work at an L.G.B.T. hotline. It goes without saying that she left the trappings of Mort behind some time ago to live as Maura.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank':