ason, rather than show an overtly sexy collection akin to the Versace designs of yore, Donatella Versace said that her mission was to elevate sportswear to luxury levels — so women could look good while feeling comfortable and powerful. To that end, she asked the makeup artist Pat McGrath to create a look that emphasized a natural glow. Which she did, with just a bit of cream blush and mascara, and her namesake line’s Skin Fetish highlighter. McGrath also groomed the models’ eyebrows and, finally, added a touch of silver pigment to the inside corner of the eyes — “a little futuristic but at the same time pretty,” she said. “The look is sporty, but not sporty as in sweaty and undone and disheveled … it’s more of a refined sport look.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/t-magazine/fashion/23tmag-versacebbr/23tmag-versacebbr-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/23/t-magazine/fashion/23tmag-versacebbr/23tmag-versacebbr-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/t-magazine/fashion/23tmag-versacebbr/23tmag-versacebbr-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/t-magazine/fashion/23tmag-versacebbr/23tmag-versacebbr-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/23/t-magazine/fashion/23tmag-versacebbr/23tmag-versacebbr-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': '