2-year-old billionaire who not only manages but is instantly identifiable with the brands he owns. Unlike his closest peers, François-Henri Pinault of Kering, or Bernard Arnault of LVMH, Della Valle has an unexpected, dandyish flair: He habitually sports upturned shirt collars and a wide-spread scarf in place of a tie, and employs not one but two tailors (Lattini for his sport jackets, Caraceni for his suits) though I’ve most often seen him combine his Caraceni jackets with Levis. His gray hair is swept back from his high forehead, his horn-rimmed spectacles seem well-considered. He is a man who likes fashion, wears it, buys some — and sells lots.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/t-magazine/fashion/tods-slide-P8X4/tods-slide-P8X4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/23/t-magazine/fashion/tods-slide-P8X4/tods-slide-P8X4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/t-magazine/fashion/tods-slide-P8X4/tods-slide-P8X4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/t-magazine/fashion/tods-slide-P8X4/tods-slide-P8X4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/t-magazine/fashion/tods-slide-P8X4/tods-slide-P8X4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/23/t-magazine/fashion/tods-slide-P8X4/tods-slide-P8X4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/23/t-magazine/fashion/tods-slide-P8X4/tods-slide-P8X4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Diego Della Valle of Tod’s on Design, Politics — and Tattoos', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Tod's Group", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Milan (Italy)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Milan Fashion Week', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-23T19:41:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Fashion & Beauty', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexander Fury', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexander', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fury', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9857a772-6979-5ecd-b9b2-9dd1c8517b9f', 'word_count': 887, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9857a772-6979-5ecd-b9b2-9dd1c8517b9f'}, {'abstract': 'Over the last few months, Harvard’s endowment has fallen short of its own goals, and that of its rival, Yale.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/24/business/dealbook/harvard-needs-a-steady-endowment-manager.html', 'snippet': 'Over the last few months, Harvard’s endowment has fallen short of its own goals, and that of its rival, Yale.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Harvard University is struggling with postgraduate life. Its giant endowment lost 2 percent in the year to June, falling short of its own yardsticks and the 3.4 percent gain generated by David Swensen at its rival, Yale. More than a decade after the departure of its architect, Jack Meyer, the Harvard Management Company is finding it hard to get past being the sort-of hedge fund it once was.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Harvard Needs a Steady Endowment Manager', 'kicker': 'Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endowments', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harvard University', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yale University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-23T19:44:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Beales', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beales', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8da7989-5570-5328-a021-08f1aa83bd15', 'word_count': 375, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8da7989-5570-5328-a021-08f1aa83bd15'}, {'abstract': 'Chemists in Italy offer up a solution for all that smelly espresso and coffee waste.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/24/science/coffee-grounds-filter-heavy-metals-water.html', 'snippet': 'Chemists in Italy offer up a solution for all that smelly espresso and coffee waste.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Inside an old gas tank, pink and white mold grows atop crispy cakes of spent espresso.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/24/science/23COFFEE/23COFFEE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 427, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/24/science/23COFFEE/23COFFEE-articl