reunion that ended by headlining Riot Fest in Chicago.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/24/arts/music/glenn-danzig-misfits-interview.html', 'snippet': 'Glenn Danzig, the Misfits’ co-founder, who had not fronted it since 1983, discussed the short reunion that ended by headlining Riot Fest in Chicago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Sunday night, Glenn Danzig fronted the Misfits — the band in which he sang lead for six years in his 20s but hadn’t joined onstage since 1983 — for the headlining slot of Chicago’s Riot Fest. The second and, he said, final performance of a two-show reunion run, the set was a comprehensive, ecstatic summary of his time with the group, which is credited with developing and popularizing horror punk.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/24/arts/24DANZIG/24DANZIG-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/24/arts/24DANZIG/24DANZIG-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/24/arts/24DANZIG/24DANZIG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/24/arts/24DANZIG/24DANZIG-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1362, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/24/arts/24DANZIG/24DANZIG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/24/arts/24DANZIG/24DANZIG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/24/arts/24DANZIG/24DANZIG-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Danzig on Getting the Band (the Misfits) Back Together. Briefly.', 'kicker': 'A Word With', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Getting  the Band  Back Together', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pop and Rock Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Danzig, Glenn (1955- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Misfits (Music Group)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-23T22:07:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Grayson Haver Currin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Grayson', 'middlename': 'Haver', 'lastname': 'Currin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ad227f9-826d-5f2b-8ab1-cff158992b9a', 'word_count': 898, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ad227f9-826d-5f2b-8ab1-cff158992b9a'}, {'abstract': 'In her stunning new show at Joe’s Pub, Ms. Buckley gave everything she sang the shape and depth of a personal confession.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/24/arts/music/betty-buckley-story-songs-review.html', 'snippet': 'In her stunning new show at Joe’s Pub, Ms. Buckley gave everything she sang the shape and depth of a personal confession.', 'lead_paragraph': '“September! November!” To hear Betty Buckley cry out the names of the remaining months as the year wanes in “September Song” at Joe’s Pub on Thursday evening was to hear a great dramatic singer dig out the underlying anguish in a standard that is typically treated as a slice of senior nostalgia. Yes, the days may be dwindling down, but there is consolation. The words, “These few precious days I’ll spend with you” give you an image of grandma and grandpa snuggling under a comforter by the hearth, not of a dazed oldster struggling with Alzheimer’s. Without overstating things, Ms. Buckley found alarm and impending grief in the song.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: Betty Buckley Digs Deep for the Autumn in Her Soul', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Digging Deep for the Autumn in Her Soul', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Joe's Pub", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Buckley, Betty', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-23T22:11:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca11e610-485f-5e81-9d23-c9189fbdb067', 'word_count': 363, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca11e610-485f-5e81-9d23-c9189fbdb067'}, {'abstract': 'Bill Cosby’s fate may rest on whether a judge in his sexual assault trial lets jurors hear from a group of women with details that prosecutors say echo his accuser’s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/24/arts/television/13-women-bill-cosby-sexual-assault-trial.html', 'snippet': 'Bill Cosby’s fate may rest on whether a judge in his sexual assault trial lets jurors hear from a group of women with details that prosecutors say echo his accuser’s.', 'lead_paragr