T00:05:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Today’s Paper', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ef4525d-19c8-5481-8de0-8ad40a435370', 'word_count': 41, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ef4525d-19c8-5481-8de0-8ad40a435370'}, {'abstract': 'David Wildstein, who has confessed to coming up with the George Washington Bridge lane-closing scheme, said the Christie administration used the agency to spread money, jobs and gifts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/24/nyregion/bridge-case-culprit-says-christie-and-ex-aides-used-port-authority-as-goody-bag.html', 'snippet': 'David Wildstein, who has confessed to coming up with the George Washington Bridge lane-closing scheme, said the Christie administration used the agency to spread money, jobs and gifts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEWARK — The admitted mastermind of the mysterious George Washington Bridge lane closings broke a three-year silence on Friday, testifying in federal court here that everything he did in his job was at the direction and for the benefit of Gov. Chris Christie of New Jersey.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/24/nyregion/24BRIDGEGATE1/24BRIDGEGATE1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 817, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/24/nyregion/24BRIDGEGATE1/24BRIDGEGATE1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 817}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/24/nyregion/24BRIDGEGATE1/24BRIDGEGATE1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 752, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images