esk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Zernike', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zernike', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1864db0-21f2-561a-926e-d4ed00317aaf', 'word_count': 1060, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1864db0-21f2-561a-926e-d4ed00317aaf'}, {'abstract': 'Some intellectuals once believed that blacks lacked humanity because they had no written history. The new museum demolishes that idea.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/24/opinion/henry-louis-gates-jr-restoring-black-history.html', 'snippet': 'Some intellectuals once believed that blacks lacked humanity because they had no written history. The new museum demolishes that idea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the ringing of a bell and a speech from President Obama, the National Museum of African American History and Culture in Washington is to officially open its extraordinary collection to the public on Saturday. But the museum can claim another, equally important achievement: helping resolve the protracted debate about the contributions of black people to American history and, indeed, about whether they had a history worth preserving at all. Those questions were at the heart of the nation’s original debate about whether, and how, black lives matter.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/24/opinion/24gates/24gates-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/24/opinion/24gates/24gates-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/24/opinion/24gates/24gates-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/24/opinion/24gates/24gates-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 893, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/24/opinion/24gates/24gates-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 893}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/24/opinion/24gates/24gates-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 688, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/24/opinion/24gates/24gates-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1376, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Henry Louis Gates Jr.: Restoring Black History', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Proving Black History Matters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gates, Henry Louis Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Museum of African American History and Culture', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Mall (Washington, DC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Slavery (Historical)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jefferson, Thomas', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-24T00:16:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Henry Louis Gates Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Henry', 'middlename': 'Louis', 'lastname': 'Gates', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/e59c12f9-f361-5a84-904b-3370d0c5f160', 'word_count': 938, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e59c12f9-f361-5a84-904b-3370d0c5f160'}, {'abstract': 'In another marathon game, the Mets thumped the Phillies, but the loss of Syndergaard to illness was a blow to their chase for a wild-card berth.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/24/sports/baseball/new-york-mets-philadelphia-phillies.html', 'snippet': 'In another marathon game, the Mets thumped the Phillies, but the loss of Syndergaard to illness was a blow to their chase for a wild-card berth.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the Mets near the final week of the regular season chasing a playoff spot, they have come to resemble a triage unit housing a baseball team. Every day seems to bring a new injury and a new conundrum. Their September roster, bloated to 39 players, is not carrying unnecessary baggage but much-needed pieces to paper over new holes and to leverage in crucial moments.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/24/sports/24METS2/24METS2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/24/sports/24METS2/24METS2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/24/sports/24METS2/24METS2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 