 history of do-overs at The New York Times, there is one example that may seem of no large consequence but nonetheless infuriated readers. It involved an obituary about a rocket scientist named Yvonne Brill. In its first incarnation, the obit referred to 88-year-old Brill in the first paragraph as a woman who “made a mean beef stroganoff, followed her husband around from job to job and took eight years off to raise three children.” In secondary fashion, it mentioned that Brill was a pioneering scientist who invented a propulsion system that kept communications satellites in orbit.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/25/sunday-review/25Pubed/25Pubed-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/25/sunday-review/25Pubed/25Pubed-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/25/sunday-review/25Pubed/25Pubed-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/25/sunday-review/25Pubed/25Pubed-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 339, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/25/sunday-review/25Pubed/25Pubed-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 339}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/25/sunday-review/25Pubed/25Pubed-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 578, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/25/sunday-review/25Pubed/25Pubed-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1156, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Taking the Stealth Out of Editing', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Taking the Stealth Out of Editing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spayd, Liz', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Editor (Times Column)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-24T18:30:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Public Editor', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Spayd', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spayd', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b1843bd-8338-5a7d-9ff2-7093a0f979d5', 'word_count': 1099, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b1843bd-8338-5a7d-9ff2-7093a0f979d5'}, {'abstract': 'The drug appears to increase the risk of asthma or developmental problems in children.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/25/opinion/sunday/the-trouble-with-tylenol-and-pregnancy.html', 'snippet': 'The drug appears to increase the risk of asthma or developmental problems in children.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you’re a pregnant woman and have a backache or headache, or a fever, your options for over-the-counter treatment basically boil down to one medication: the pain reliever acetaminophen, better known as Tylenol. Doctors advise against using nonsteroidal anti-inflammatories, like ibuprofen and aspirin, during late pregnancy because they can compromise fetal circulation and have other adverse consequences.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/25/opinion/sunday/25velasquez/25velasquez-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 595, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/25/opinion/sunday/25velasquez/25velasquez-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 595}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/25/opinion/sunday/25velasquez/25velasquez-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 999, 'width': 1008, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/25/opinion/sunday/25velasquez/25velasquez-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 999, 'width': 1008, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/25/opinion/sunday/25velasquez/25velasquez-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/25/opinion/sunday/25velasquez/25velasquez-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/25/opinion/sunday/25velasquez/25velasquez-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Trouble With Tylenol and Pregnancy', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Trouble With Tylenol', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Velasquez-Manoff, Moises', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Childbirth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asthma', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tylenol (Drug)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Attention Deficit Hyperactivity Disorder', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-24T18:30:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Moises Velasquez-Manoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Moises', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Velasquez-Manoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/da2e339d-f7a3-5817-895f-df57769fd4ca', 'word_count': 1135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da2e339d-f7a3-5817-895f-df57769fd4ca'}, {'abstract': 'As a kid with diabetes, I learned to find substitutes for what I loved.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/25/opinion/sunday/the-sweet-relief-of-splenda-in-my-purse.html', 'snippet': 'As a kid with diabetes, I learned to find substitutes for what I loved.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I feel a special kind of relief when I walk into a fancy coffee shop and see Splenda alongside the simple syrup and almond milk. Nowadays it’s trendy to eat all-natural, organic, clean. We’re told it’s healthy and morally superior, even. But all I want in my iced coffee is the contents of those little yellow packets, or the blue ones, or pink.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/25/opinion/sunday/25kreizman/25kreizman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/25/opinion/sunday/25kreizman/25kreizman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/25/opinion/sunday/25kreizman/25kreizman-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/25/opinion/sunday/25kreizman/25kreizman-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 415, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/25/opinion/sunday/25kreizman/25kreizman-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 415}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/25/opinion/sunday/25kreizman/25kreizman-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 708, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/25/opinion/sunday/25kreizman/25kreizman-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 870, 'width': 1258, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Sweet Relief of Splenda in My Purse', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Sweet Relief of Splenda', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diabetes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Artificial Sweeteners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sugar', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-24T18:30:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maris Kreizman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kreizman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a1c1c66-3a35-5d1d-a76c-007ec7590cbb', 'word_count': 952, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a1c1c66-3a35-5d1d-a76c-007ec7590cbb'}, {'abstract': 'I said no to parties, ducked out of school events, and excused it as “self-care.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/25/opinion/sunday/am-i-introverted-or-just-rude.html', 'snippet': 'I said no to parties, ducked out of school events, and excused it as “self-care.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'A good friend and colleague, a real extrovert, sent me a link to a shirt recently that she knew I’d appreciate. “Sorry I’m late,” the T-shirt reads. “I didn’t want to be here.”', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/25/opinion/sunday/25dellantonia/25dellantonia-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 354, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/25/opinion/sunday/25dellantonia/25dellantonia-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 354}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/25/opinion/sunday/25dellantonia/25dellantonia-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 604, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/25/opinion/sunday/25dellantonia/25dellantonia-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 798, 'width': 1352, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/25/opinion/sunday/25dellantonia/25dellantonia-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/25/opinion/sunday/25dellantonia/25dellantonia-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/25/opinion/sunday/25dellantonia/25dellantonia-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Am I Introverted, or Just Rude?', 'kicker': 'Dispatch', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Am I Introverted or Just Rude?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-24T18:30:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': "By KJ Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9c0ba9e-a41a-5fc5-baeb-6efd1d2a28e5', 'word_count': 1262, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9c0ba9e-a41a-5fc5-baeb-6efd1d2a28e5'}, {'abstract': 'An Asian man can write a lynching scene if it’s good enough. So could Lionel Shriver.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/25/opinion/sunday/who-gets-to-write-what.html', 'snippet': 'An Asian man can write a lynching scene if it’s good enough. So could Lionel Shriver.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I was in graduate school, I remember a fellow writer bringing to a workshop a lynching scene. The writer was not black. He was, in fact, a Chinese-American man named Bill Cheng, who would go on to write a novel of the blues called “Southern Cross the Dog.”', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/25/opinion/sunday/25greenidge/25greenidge-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 779, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/25/opinion/sunday/25greenidge/25greenidge-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 779}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/25/opinion/sunday/25greenidge/25greenidge-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 790, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/25/opinion/sunday/25greenidge/25greenidge-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1413, 'width': 1089, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/25/opinion/sunday/25greenidge/25greenidge-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/25/opinion/sunday/25greenidge/25greenidge-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/25/opinion/sunday/25greenidge/25greenidge-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Gets to Write What?', 'kicker': 'Contributing Op-Ed Writer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Who Gets to Write What Story?', 'name': None, 's