ract': 'Sol Calero brings T to Gloria’s Unisex Salon, a source of inspiration and reminder of home, for a haircut.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/26/t-magazine/art/sol-calero-hair-solo-pintura.html', 'snippet': 'Sol Calero brings T to Gloria’s Unisex Salon, a source of inspiration and reminder of home, for a haircut.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Coming here reminds me of home,” says the Venezuelan artist Sol Calero as she relaxes into her chair. It’s days before the opening of her sophomore show at Laura Bartlett Gallery in London, and Calero is at Gloria’s Unisex Salon, a local’s haunt that’s situated under the railway arches in Elephant and Castle. “I realized I needed a change,” she says, showing off her Rapunzel length jet-black hair. “It has got so long that cycling around Berlin, where I live, has become kind of dangerous.” It’s not the first time the artist has visited Gloria Dominguez’s salon. After spotting an advertisement for the hairdresser in a copy of the local Latin News (Dominguez hails from Ecuador), Calero enlisted her help for her debut display at Laura Bartlett — a reconstructed Latin beauty salon, where visitors could get their hair and nails done.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/26/t-magazine/art/26tmag-sol-01/26tmag-sol-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/26/t-magazine/art/26tmag-sol-01/26tmag-sol-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/26/t-magazine/art/26tmag-sol-01/26tmag-sol-01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/26/t-magazine/art/26tmag-sol-01/26tmag-sol-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 453, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/26/t-magazine/art/26tmag-sol-01/26tmag-sol-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 453}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/26/t-magazine/art/26tmag-sol-01/26tmag-sol-01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 774, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/26/t-magazine/art/26tmag-sol-01/26tmag-sol-01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1548, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Artist’s New Look — at the Hairdresser, and on Show', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beauty Salons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-26T17:37:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Art', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aimee Farrell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aimee', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Farrell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d51b2f16-1e0c-5e85-bc24-78dbac54e54c', 'word_count': 502, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d51b2f16-1e0c-5e85-bc24-78dbac54e54c'}, {'abstract': 'A look at the line’s fall/winter 2016 collection.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2016/09/29/t-magazine/fashion/meet-quetsche-a-new-brand-inspired-by-fantasy.html', 'snippet': 'A look at the line’s fall/winter 2016 collection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A loo