 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-26T22:23:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Fashion & Beauty', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexander Fury', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexander', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fury', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bbb67527-0321-5503-913d-57296a260b59', 'word_count': 1263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbb67527-0321-5503-913d-57296a260b59'}, {'abstract': 'A longtime defender of fossil fuels and critic of regulations limiting greenhouse gases appears to be Trump’s pick to handle the transition at the Environmental Protection Agency should he prevail.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/09/26/no-debate-trump-picks-a-perfect-transition-man-for-the-e-p-a/', 'snippet': 'A longtime defender of fossil fuels and critic of regulations limiting greenhouse gases appears to be Trump’s pick to handle the transition at the Environmental Protection Agency should he prevail.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Late this afternoon, I sent an email query to Myron Ebell, the longtime director of energy and environmental policy at the Competitive Enterprise Institute, to check on reports that he’d been tapped by Donald J. Trump’s campaign to run the evisceration transition team for the Environmental Protection Agency should Trump prevail in November. Robin Bravender at E&E’s Climate Wire appeared to lead the pack this morning. (Read more about Trump’s environmental game plan in a detailed E&E feature\xa0by Kevin Bogardus.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/26/blogs/dotebell/dotebell-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 360, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'captio