n accused of carrying out recent bombings in Manhattan and on the Jersey Shore, took a new turn on Monday when the American Civil Liberties Union of New Jersey said that it had been retained by his father and his wife to defend him on federal charges, at least until he was given a federal public defender or other lawyer.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ahmad Khan Rahami’s Father and Wife Retain A.C.L.U. to Defend Him', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Two Relatives Get A.C.L.U.  to Represent Bomb Suspect', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rahimi, Ahmad Khan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosenberg, Eli', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chelsea, Manhattan Bombing (2016)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Civil Liberties Union', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-27T02:03:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Weiser and Eli Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weiser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Eli', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b6d7fec-b62e-5388-8d4e-32767181d577', 'word_count': 401, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b6d7fec-b62e-5388-8d4e-32767181d577'}, {'abstract': 'The initiative, which applies to New York City public school students, is part of an effort by the city to encourage more young people to go to college.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/27/nyregion/cuny-application-fee-to-be-waived-for-low-income-students.html', 'sni