e worried that the searing heat would lead to too much drinking. It was 3 p.m. on June 11, and the gates to the Ravinia outdoor theater in Highland Park, Ill., had just opened. People streamed in carrying coolers and lawn chairs, checkered blankets and wineglasses, plasticware full of crackers, melons and deviled eggs. They politely competed for swatches of grass in the shade of oak trees mounted with thank you for not smoking signs.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/02/magazine/02thile1/02thile1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/02/magazine/02thile1/02thile1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/02/magazine/02thile1/02thile1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/02/magazine/02thile1/02thile1-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 639, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/02/magazine/02thile1/02thile1-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 639}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/02/magazine/02thile1/02thile1-jumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 963, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/02/magazine/02thile1/02thile1-superJumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 2000, 'width': 1879, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s ‘A Prairie Home Companion’ Without Garrison Keillor?', 'kicker': 'Feature', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘The Beauty of It Is That It Could Fail.’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Streep, Abe', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thile, Chris', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'A Prairie Home Companion (Radio Program)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keillor, Garrison', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nickel Creek', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radio', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-27T09:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abe Streep', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Streep', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/993cdea2-fc9d-50b4-8e94-8c922f4a71b4', 'word_count': 3549, 'uri': 'nyt://article/993cdea2-fc9d-50b4-8e94-8c922f4a71b4'}, {'abstract': 'How paranoia moved from the margins of American politics to its center.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/02/magazine/the-conspiracy-theorists-election.html', 'snippet': 'How paranoia moved from the margins of American politics to its center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s possible to gaze back almost wistfully on all the moments in recent American politics that seemed, at the time, to constitute Peak Crazy, but look from today’s vantage point like false summits. Consider, for instance, the remarks Barack Obama gave at the 2011 White House Correspondents Dinner, three days after releasing the long-form birth certificate Donald Trump had spent weeks demanding. “Now, I know that he’s taken some flak lately,” Obama said, with Trump in the audience, “but no one is happier, no one is prouder to put this birth-certificate matter to rest than the Donald. And that’s because he can finally get back to focusing on issues that matter — like, did we fake the moon landing? What really happened in Roswell? And where are Biggie and Tupac?”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/02/magazine/02firstwords-promo/02mag-02firstwords-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/02/magazine/02firstwords-promo/02mag-02firstwords-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/02/magazine/02firstwords-promo/02mag-02firstwords-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/02/magazine/02firstwords-promo/02mag-02firstwords-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/02/magazine/02firstwords-promo/02mag-02firstwords-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/02/magazine/02firstwords-promo/02mag-02firstwords-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/02/magazine/02firstwords-pr