ead_paragraph': 'Across Western Europe, marriage equality is fast becoming the norm: From Scandinavia through the Netherlands and Denmark; even the Catholic countries of Ireland, France and Spain. But there’s one glaring exception: Germany. It stands out not only because it is the largest country in Western Europe, but also because on many measures, it is among the most progressive.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Germany’s Retrograde Record on Gay Rights', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merkel, Angela', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-27T13:54:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexander Görlach', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexander', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Görlach', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c2eedb9-00e0-5bc6-9a6e-f13fc7bf98bd', 'word_count': 798, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c2eedb9-00e0-5bc6-9a6e-f13fc7bf98bd'}, {'abstract': 'It wasn’t the usual post-show bash that kept some in the French capital up until the wee hours.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/28/fashion/debates-paris-fashion-week.html', 'snippet': 'It wasn’t the usual post-show bash that kept some in the French capital up until the wee hours.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — At 3 a.m. on Tuesday, the streets near the Champs-Élysées were eerily silent, the stillness punctuated only by the rolling shutters of brasseries being drawn down by weary waiters, the occasional moped engine or faraway siren, and the click-clack of a policeman’s boots on the sidewalk as he stood on duty, rifle firmly in hand.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/28/fashion/28FASHDEBATE/28FASHDEBATE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/28/fashion/28FASHDEBATE/28FASHDEBATE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/28/fashion/28FASHDEBATE/28FASHDEBATE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/28/fashion/28FASHDEBATE/28FASHDEBATE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/28/fashion/28FASHDEBATE/28FASHDEBATE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/28/fashion/28FASHDEBATE/28FASHDEBATE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/28/fashion/28FASHDEBATE/28FASHDEBATE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'During the Presidential Debate, a Fashionable Pajama Party in Paris', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wearing Pajamas to a Presidential Debate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paton, Elizabeth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paris Fashion Week', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pajamas', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-27T13:58:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth Paton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Paton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ef242a8-9df7-5a30-99ed-e64e2e6f528c', 'word_count': 699, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ef242a8-9df7-5a30-99ed-e64e2e6f528c'}, {'abstract': 'Monday night, Mrs. Clinton displayed her preparedness and her quick wit, her affection for granular policy detail and her eagerness to throw flames and flip the script on Donald J. Trump.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/28/us/politics/hillary-clinton-debate.html', 'snippet': 'Monday night, Mrs. Clinton displayed her preparedness and her quick wit, her affection for granular policy detail and her eagerness to throw flames and flip the script on Donald J. Trump.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HEMPSTEAD, N.Y. — I’ve heard Hillary Clinton tell the story about her father and his drapery business so many times now that I can mouth the word “squeegee” at the exact second it comes out of her mouth.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/28/us/28CLINTONassess/