e}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/579adeb9-a5e8-5324-ad07-2ef1c28859ea', 'word_count': 747, 'uri': 'nyt://article/579adeb9-a5e8-5324-ad07-2ef1c28859ea'}, {'abstract': 'Naomi Duguid’s latest cookbook follows a trail through Iran, Georgia, Kurdistan, Azerbaijan and Armenia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/28/dining/taste-of-persia-cookbook-review-naomi-duguid.html', 'snippet': 'Naomi Duguid’s latest cookbook follows a trail through Iran, Georgia, Kurdistan, Azerbaijan and Armenia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new book from Naomi Duguid is a reason to celebrate, as each promises a fascinating culinary excursion. Her previous books focused on Southeast Asia, and like them, this newest, “Taste of Persia,” opens with a map, which illustrates Ms. Duguid’s wise observation that regional cooking doesn’t respect borders. So the search for Persian cuisine includes stops in Armenia, Azerbaijan, Georgia, Iran and Kurdistan.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/28/dining/28PERSIAN2/28PERSIAN2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/28/dining/28PERSIAN2/28PERSIAN2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/28/dining/28PERSIAN2/28PERSIAN2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/28/dining/28PERSIAN2/28PERSIAN2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 538, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/28/dining/28PERSIAN2/28PERSIAN2-articleLarge.jpg