n-design.html', 'snippet': 'Ahead of his first retrospective, the designer and UFO Collective co-founder delves into his archive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ahead of his first retrospective, the designer and UFO Collective co-founder delves into his archive.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/27/t-magazine/art/lapo-bonazzi-slide-5RKR/lapo-bonazzi-slide-5RKR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/27/t-magazine/art/lapo-bonazzi-slide-5RKR/lapo-bonazzi-slide-5RKR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/27/t-magazine/art/lapo-bonazzi-slide-5RKR/lapo-bonazzi-slide-5RKR-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/27/t-magazine/art/lapo-bonazzi-slide-5RKR/lapo-bonazzi-slide-5RKR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 421, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/27/t-magazine/art/lapo-bonazzi-slide-5RKR/lapo-bonazzi-slide-5RKR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 421}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/27/t-magazine/art/lapo-bonazzi-slide-5RKR/lapo-bonazzi-slide-5RKR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/27/t-magazine/art/lapo-bonazzi-slide-5RKR/lapo-bonazzi-slide-5RKR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1438, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lapo Binazzi’s Radical Italian Design', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-09-27T20:49:33+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'T Magazine', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Art', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/2eaf7879-03d7-5210-92bb-3fd3d8f9351c', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/2eaf7879-03d7-5210-92bb-3fd3d8f9351c'}, {'abstract': 'Lapo Binazzi shares thoughts on his own loopy work: dollar-sign table lamps, satirical discos and more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/27/t-magazine/art/lapo-binazzi-ufo-r-and-company.html', 'snippet': 'Lapo Binazzi shares thoughts on his own loopy work: dollar-sign table lamps, satirical discos and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lapo Binazzi is a lover of the absurd. UFO, the design collective he co-founded, played an integral role in the rise of Radical Design in Italy, alongside groups like Gruppo 9999 and Superstudio, all of which pushed forward utopian agendas using a practice that wed art, architecture and technology. The supergroups used humor and free association to topple the existing hierarchies of quality as a reaction to Italy’s political and economic strife — often in undeniably fun ways. (For evidence, look no further than UFO’s “Discoteque Bamba Issa,” a shapeshifting discothèque variously dotted with seating inspired by camels’ humps, and décor that satirized Italian infrastructural bureaucracy.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Artist-Architect Who Revolutionized Italian Design — With Humor', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'R & Company', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-27T20:49:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Art', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kat Herriman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kat', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Herriman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3fdb0102-b362-5973-90ff-c4b7d1802c4b', 'word_count': 241, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3fdb0102-b362-5973-90ff-c4b7d1802c4b'}, {'abstract': 'Undecided women in Philadelphia’s suburbs, a crucial voting bloc, said Mr. Trump had not only failed to win them over but in many cases had repelled them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/28/us/politics/women-voters-reaction.html', 'snippet': 'Undecided women in Philadelphia’s suburbs, a crucial voting bloc, said Mr. Trump had not only failed to win them over but in many cases had repelled them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WEST CHESTER, Pa. — Donald J. Trump badly needed to make an impression on women like Nancy Groux in Monday’s presidential debate. She is an undecided Republican who hungers for change in Washington and thinks business experience would be an asset in the Oval Office.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/28/us/28voices3/28voices3-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/28/us/28voices3/28voices3-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/28/us/28voices3/28voices3-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', '