ay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d269c55b-4909-57ab-9a57-828bc03a0146', 'word_count': 449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d269c55b-4909-57ab-9a57-828bc03a0146'}, {'abstract': 'Simon Porte Jacquemus drew on his youth as inspiration, while at Courrèges, Sébastien Meyer and Arnaud Vaillant showed their first full collection.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/29/fashion/the-jacquemus-girl-courreges-slim-and-short.html', 'snippet': 'Simon Porte Jacquemus drew on his youth as inspiration, while at Courrèges, Sébastien Meyer and Arnaud Vaillant showed their first full collection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — “It’s a French one, eh?” said Simon Porte Jacquemus, accepting French cheek kisses and French congratulations backstage after his Jacquemus show. The tent had been pitched in the heart of the Tuileries garden, but the scene was set in the south of France, his home turf. His models wore giant straw hats and, leg-of-mutton sleeves, and came down the runway to the schmaltzy orchestral theme from “Jean de Florette,” the Gérard Depardieu period piece from the 1980s — French cheese at its ripest.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/29/fashion/29PARIS-WEB1/29PARIS-WEB1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/29/fashion/29PARIS-WEB1/29PARIS-WEB1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/29/fashion/29PARIS-WEB1/29PARIS-WEB1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': 