White Christmas.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/02/theater/holiday-inn-arrives-and-so-does-an-early-white-christmas.html', 'snippet': 'Roundabout presents a stage adaptation of the 1942 movie starring Bing Crosby. The film is best known for Irving Berlin’s “White Christmas.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Roundabout Theater Company enters the seasonal-treats sweepstakes with “Holiday Inn,” a stage adaptation of the 1942 movie starring Bing Crosby as an entertainer who decides to call it quits, buy a farm and turn the place into a novelty act: a venue open only on holidays.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/02/arts/1002WEEKAHEAD3/1002WEEKAHEAD3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/02/arts/1002WEEKAHEAD3/1002WEEKAHEAD3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/02/arts/1002WEEKAHEAD3/1002WEEKAHEAD3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/02/arts/1002WEEKAHEAD3/1002WEEKAHEAD3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/02/arts/1002WEEKAHEAD3/1002WEEKAHEAD3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/02/arts/1002WEEKAHEAD3/1002WEEKAHEAD3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/02/arts/1002WEEKAHEAD3/1002WEEKAHEAD3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Holiday Inn’ Arrives, and so Does an Early ‘White Christmas’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Theater; ‘White Christmas’ Comes Early', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roundabout Theater Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Studio 54', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berlin, Irving', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greenberg, Gordon', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Holiday Inn (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Holiday Inn (Play)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-28T16:46:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Isherwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isherwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc1d9b5d-b98c-51af-9ddd-b42b421d6091', 'word_count': 156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc1d9b5d-b98c-51af-9ddd-b42b421d6091'}, {'abstract': 'Michael Cimino’s costly, 216-minute western about class conflict in Wyoming, based on the Johnson County War, helped sink the studio behind it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/02/movies/heavens-gate-comes-to-bamcinematek.html', 'snippet': 'Michael Cimino’s costly, 216-minute western about class conflict in Wyoming, based on the Johnson County War, helped sink the studio behind it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Michael Cimino’s costly, 216-minute western “Heaven’s Gate” (1980) — coming to BAMcinématek on Sunday, Oct. 2, as part of “Desperate Hours: The Films of Michael Cimino” — helped sink United Artists, the studio behind it. But Mr. Cimino (who died in July) had made his masterpiece, with granular attention to period detail that at times evokes the Italian director Luchino Visconti at his most lavish. The brilliant cinematographer Vilmos Zsigmond is at his atmospheric apex, with a cast including Isabelle Huppert, Christopher Walken (from Mr. Cimino’s “The Deer Hunter”), Jeff Bridges (from his “Thunderbolt and Lightfoot”) and Kris Kristofferson as the archetypal taciturn lawman.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/02/arts/1002WEEKAHEAD4/1002WEEKAHEAD4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/02/arts/1002WEEKAHEAD4/1002WEEKAHEAD4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/02/arts/1002WEEKAHEAD4/1002WEEKAHEAD4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/02/arts/1002WEEKAHEAD4/1002WEEKAHEAD4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/02/arts/1002WEEKAHEAD4/1002WEEKAHEAD4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/02/arts/1002WEEKAHEAD4/1002WEEKAHEAD4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 676, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/02/arts/1002WEEKAHEAD4/1002WEEKAHEAD4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1353, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Heaven’s Gate’ Comes to BAMcinématek', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Film; Class Conflict, in Lavish Detail', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "Heaven's Gate (Movie)", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cimino, Michael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bridges, Jeff', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kristofferson, Kris', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zsigmond, Vilmos (1930-2016)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Academy of Music', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-28T16:47:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Webster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/577af8b9-58cd-5607-806e-57f52a9eaf37', 'word_count': 164, 'uri': 'nyt://article/577af8b9-58cd-5607-806e-57f52a9eaf37'}, {'abstract': 'This film revisits the trials and tribulations of an Irish force in Central Africa in 1961.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/02/movies/the-siege-of-jadotville-on-netflix-rediscovers-a-faded-footnote.html', 'snippet': 'This film revisits the trials and tribulations of an Irish force in Central Africa in 1961.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Congo crisis, as it was generally known, is a historical footnote to many people now, but “The Siege of Jadotville,” a Netflix film that becomes available Friday, Oct. 7, makes a gripping drama out of one particular moment in the yearslong struggle for control in Central Africa. Jamie Dornan (“Fifty Shades of Grey”) plays the commandant leading a small Irish force of United Nations peacekeepers that was besieged in 1961 in the Democratic Republic of Congo by several thousand local troops from Katanga Province, which was seeking to secede. “By the fourth day, the Irish were down to their last biscuit,” The New York Times reported at the time. “They had gone for four days without sleep and two days without water.” Early in the film, before the Irish force deploys, someone asks the commandant if he thinks his men will see any action. “Who knows?” he responds. “I don’t think anyone’s clear what’s going on out there.” Those words prove to be quite accurate.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/02/arts/1002WEEKAHEAD6/1002WEEKAHEAD6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/02/arts/1002WEEKAHEAD6/1002WEEKAHEAD6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/02/arts/1002WEEKAHEAD6/1002WEEKAHEAD6-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/02/arts/1002WEEKAHEAD6/1002WEEKAHEAD6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/02/arts/1002WEEKAHEAD6/1002WEEKAHEAD6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 6