g intricate sets, much like the director of a film.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/28/t-magazine/fashion/alessandro-michele-gucci-set-design-fashion-week.html', 'snippet': 'In his tenure at the house, Alessandro Michele has become known for creating intricate sets, much like the director of a film.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I have the soul of a director,” says the designer Alessandro Michele, a couple of days after his spring/summer 2017 Gucci show. He’s speaking over the phone from Rome, which is fitting, given that Rome is the home of la Cinecittà, the hub of Italian cinema. Michele isn’t hankering after a feature film production like his predecessor Tom Ford. (The former Gucci creative director’s second movie, “Nocturnal Animals,” is out this November.) Rather, he’s talking about the scenography of his tenure at Gucci, which has scrolled through multiple iterations over the past 18 months, like sequels in an ever-unfolding cinematic franchise.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside the Elaborate World of Gucci’s Shows', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Michele, Alessandro', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gucci', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-28T19:27:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Fashion & Beauty', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexander Fury', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexander', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fury', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c57c220a-18bf-5a21-a8ce-467c89c2adfd', 'word_count': 1182, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c57c220a-18bf-5a21-a8ce-467c89c2adfd'}, {'abstract': 'What exactly did the Republican candidate say about the Iraq war in 2003?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/28/magazine/donald-trump-sean-hannity-and-a-still-elusive-tape.html', 'snippet': 'What exactly did the Republican candidate say about the Iraq war in 2003?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Near the end of Monday’s presidential debate between Donald Trump and Hillary Clinton, Trump stood by his oft-contested claim that he opposed invading Iraq in 2003, despite a tape-recorded interview with Howard Stern in 2002 to the contrary. This time, however, he suggested a new source to back up his assertion. “I had numerous conversations with Sean Hannity at Fox,” he told the audience. “He and I used to have arguments about the war. I said it’s a terrible, stupid thing; it’s going to destabilize the Middle East. And that’s exactly what it’s done.” He added: “Nobody wants to call him. Nobody calls Sean Hannity.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/28/magazine/28mag-trump-1/28mag-trump-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/28/magazine/28mag-trump-1/28mag-trump-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/28/magazine/28mag-trump-1/28mag-trump-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/28/magazine/28mag-trump-1/28mag-trump-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/28/magazine/28mag-trump-1/28mag-trump-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600,