le': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/508da67b-3b24-54bc-9a1d-074b4127a4d7', 'word_count': 177, 'uri': 'nyt://article/508da67b-3b24-54bc-9a1d-074b4127a4d7'}, {'abstract': 'Time and home cooking have stripped away many of the dish’s Continental flourishes. That might be for the better.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/02/magazine/chicken-tetrazzini-the-casserole-even-snobs-love.html', 'snippet': 'Time and home cooking have stripped away many of the dish’s Continental flourishes. That might be for the better.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the early years of the 20th century, when the Italian opera star Luisa Tetrazzini was singing to adoring crowds in San Francisco and New York, some enterprising chef got the idea of making an insanely rich pasta dish and naming it for her. Chicken tetrazzini was spaghetti, heavy cream, chicken, mushrooms and Parmesan, served with two classic French sauces, chicken velouté and hollandaise, on top. This was fancy food, if hardly Italian, and within just a few years you could find tetrazzini in the dining rooms of the nation’s swankier hotels. In the 1930s, the actor Vincent Price used to eat it at Sardi’s in Manhattan, where he was a thrice-weekly regular during a run of “Victoria Regina” at the Broadhurst Theater across the street. He liked tetrazzini so much that he included a recipe for it in “A Treasury of Great Recipes,” the cookbook he wrote with his wife, Mary, in 1965.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/02/magazine/02eat/02mag-02eat-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/02/magazine/02eat/02mag-02eat-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/02/magazine/02eat/02mag-02eat-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/02/magazine/02eat/02mag-02eat-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/02/magazine/02eat/02mag-02eat-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/02/magazine/02eat/02mag-02eat-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/02/magazine/02eat/02mag-02eat-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chicken Tetrazzini, the Casserole Even Snobs Love', 'kicker': 'Eat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sing for Your Supper', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sifton, Sam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pasta', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-29T09:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Sifton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sifton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_