ot heed the standard warnings, acts in a way that seems to invite danger, and ends up dead.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/30/us/30Troubled-web2/30Troubled-web2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/30/us/30Troubled-web2/30Troubled-web2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/30/us/30Troubled-web2/30Troubled-web2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/30/us/30Troubled-web2/30Troubled-web2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/30/us/30Troubled-web2/30Troubled-web2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/30/us/30Troubled-web2/30Troubled-web2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/30/us/30Troubled-web2/30Troubled-web2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When ‘Yelling Commands’ Is the Wrong Police Response', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When ‘Yelling Commands’ Is the Wrong Police Response', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Abuse of the Disabled', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disabilities', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Intellectual Disabilities', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-29T09:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Pérez-Peña', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pérez-Peña', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/11fcd76f-f624-5a40-9269-dcfa391e518f', 'word_count': 1174, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11fcd76f-f624-5a40-9269-dcfa391e518f'}, {'abstract': 'Fashion — and fans — paid court to the pop star and the look she described as Marie Antoinette “if she was going to the gym.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/30/fashion/rihannas-fenty-line-debuts-in-paris-and-receives-a-pop-star-welcome.html', 'snippet': 'Fashion — and fans — paid court to the pop star and the look she described as Marie Antoinette “if she was going to the gym.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — On an upper floor of the Hôtel Salomon de Rothschild, the 19th-century manse formerly occupied by the banking Rothschilds, a line of sweating models fiddled with the rings in their lips and the septums of their perfect noses, and waited to have their lip gloss reapplied. They chatted among themselves, fanning one another with torn bits of cardboard in the close, sticky corridor and examining their nails, which had been sharpened to talons and encrusted with miniature gems. They received compliments with the languorous equanimity of court ladies, which for a night they were.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rihanna’s Fenty Line Debuts in Paris and Receives a Pop Star Welcome', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'RihannaHolds Court', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schneier, Matthew', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paris Fashion Week', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rihanna', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Puma AG', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-29T09:04:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew Schneier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schneier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a4082b3-ab8b-56d6-a20b-163bdda992be', 'word_count': 426, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a4082b3-ab8b-56d6-a20b-163bdda992be'}, {'abstract': 'How diverse are the sources in your social media feed, and why does it matter?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/29/learning/is-your-online-world-just-a-filter-bubble-of-people-with-the-same-opinions.html', 'snippet': 'How diverse are the sources in your social media feed, and why does it matter?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Where and how do you get your news? How much comes via a social media feed? How diverse is that feed in terms of demographic details like the ages, races, religions, geographical locations, interests and political affiliations of the people you follow?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/22/opinion/sunday/22b