rint_headline': 'Microsoft  Reorganizes  Its Research  Into A.I.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corp', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Artificial Intelligence', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nadella, Satya', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shum, Harry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lu, Qi', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-29T21:28:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Wingfield', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wingfield', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8336148a-25de-5834-aa33-32336f96362c', 'word_count': 377, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8336148a-25de-5834-aa33-32336f96362c'}, {'abstract': 'More details on the scope and scale of the militarization of American police forces would help bolster this documentary.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/30/movies/review-do-not-resist.html', 'snippet': 'More details on the scope and scale of the militarization of American police forces would help bolster this documentary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s easy to fault the one-sidedness of “Do Not Resist,” Craig Atkinson’s documentary about the militarization of the police in the United States, but that’s missing the point. Sure, plenty of local police officers — a majority, even — have more in common with Andy Taylor (Andy Griffith), the genial television sheriff of the 1960s than they do with a storm trooper. But this unsettling film is about the planting and nurturing of a mind-set, one grounded in hostility and fear.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘Do Not Resist,’ or When a Police Force Becomes an Army', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Do Not Resist (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Atkinson, Craig (Filmmaker)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-29T21:31:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/26c9b197-b47d-5b14-8de0-6c17c8962973', 'word_count': 229, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26c9b197-b47d-5b14-8de0-6c17c8962973'}, {'abstract': 'A woman and a man conjure ever-morphing, wildly different ideas in this show from Forced Entertainment, part of the Crossing the Line Festival.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/30/theater/review-in-tomorrows-parties-visions-of-the-planets-future.html', 'snippet': 'A woman and a man conjure ever-morphing, wildly different ideas in this show from Forced Entertainment, part of the Crossing the Line Festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was a deep-sleep snore with a snort at the end. Rising out of the darkened auditorium at Florence Gould Hall on Wednesday night, near the end of “Tomorrow’s Parties” by the British company Forced Entertainment, the sound was too loud to ignore. An infectious case of the giggles rippled through the audience, and kept rippling.', 'print_section': 'C', 'pr