d_paragraph': 'Tired of tracking the presidential election through the soporific data analyses of political pundits? Try the Mexican peso instead. The currency\xa0turns out to be inversely tied to the fortunes of Donald Trump as he makes a daily punching bag of Mexico in his campaign. Experts who saw the peso reach an all-time low against the dollar just before the presidential debate Monday reported that it rose immediately after the debate, going up 2.3 percent in tandem with opinion polls in which viewers pronounced Mr. Trump the loser.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/29/opinion/30clinesWEB2/30clinesWEB2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/29/opinion/30clinesWEB2/30clinesWEB2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/29/opinion/30clinesWEB2/30clinesWEB2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/29/opinion/30clinesWEB2/30clinesWEB2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/29/opinion/30clinesWEB2/30clinesWEB2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/29/opinion/30clinesWEB2/30clinesWEB2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/29/opinion/30clinesWEB2/30