section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kaya Laterman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kaya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Laterman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f3e62615-c31a-591b-b28b-a9727f729b4a', 'word_count': 1700, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f3e62615-c31a-591b-b28b-a9727f729b4a'}, {'abstract': 'Shop in brick-and-mortar stores. Don’t obsess over mechanics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/02/magazine/how-to-walk-in-high-heels.html', 'snippet': 'Shop in brick-and-mortar stores. Don’t obsess over mechanics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Start with the right shoes. Finding them should be not unlike finding a lover. “Go toward the thing that excites you the most,” says Alexandra Billings, a transgender actress and theater-arts professor at California State University, Long Beach, who plays the role of mentor to Jeffrey Tambor’s character on “Transparent.” Billings does all her shoe shopping in brick-and-mortar stores, never online. “You’ve got to walk around in them, touch them, spend some time,” she says. Feel even the hint of a pinched toe or wobble? Take them off. You cannot be your true self if you’re in pain. Plus, Billings says, “nobody wants to see you fall.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/02/magazine/02tip/02mag-02tip-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 974, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/02/magazine/02tip/02mag-02tip-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 974}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/02/magazine/02tip/02mag-02tip-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 631, 'subType': 'jumbo