the hardcover fiction list.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/09/books/review/the-story-behind-this-weeks-best-sellers.html', 'snippet': 'Witchcraft is suspected in Alan Bradley’s latest book about the 12-year-old chemist-sleuth Flavia de Luce, No. 6 on the hardcover fiction list.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Caldron Bubble: The Canadian crime writer Alan Bradley continues his best-selling Flavia de Luce series with the novel “Thrice the Brinded Cat Hath Mew’d,” new at No.\u202f6 on the hardcover fiction list, and I know what you’re thinking: “Hey, isn’t that the line the first witch utters in Act IV, Scene 1 of ‘Macbeth,’ just before the ‘toil and trouble’ witches’ song?” It is! You guys are so smart. This is the eighth book in Bradley’s series about a precocious adolescent chemist-slash-sleuth, and here’s how Booklist describes the story:', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/09/books/review/09list-image/09list-image-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/09/books/review/09list-image/09list-image-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/09/books/review/09list-image/09list-image-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/09/books/review/09list-image/09list-image-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 271, 'width': 257, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/09/books/review/09