sports/baseball/baltimore-orioles-woody-guthrie-this-land-is-your-land.html', 'snippet': 'The regular playing of “This Land Is Your Land” is a subtle reminder from Orioles management that at the intersection of sports and patriotism, one size does not have to fit all.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BALTIMORE — In the middle of the seventh inning of the Baltimore Orioles’ game against the Arizona Diamondbacks two Friday nights ago, the public-address announcer asked the crowd at Camden Yards to stand and celebrate America’s diversity. Three singers then stood on the first-base dugout and did a rendition of “This Land Is Your Land,” the famous folk song written by Woody Guthrie.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/02/sports/02GUTHRIEweb2/02GUTHRIEweb2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/02/sports/02GUTHRIEweb2/02GUTHRIEweb2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/02/sports/02GUTHRIEweb2/02GUTHRIEweb2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/02/sports/02GUTHRIEweb2/02GUTHRIEweb2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 472, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/02/sports/02GUTHRIEweb2/02GUTHRIEweb2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 472}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/02/sports/02GUTHRIEweb2/02GUTHRIEweb2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 805, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/02/sports/02GUTHRIEweb2/02GUTHRIEweb2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1610, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Orioles Deliver a Seventh-Inning Message: This Song Is Their Song', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Baltimore, This Song Is Their Song', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strauss, Ben', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baltimore Orioles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Guthrie, Woody', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaepernick, Colin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berlin, Irving', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Angelos, John P', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'This Land Is Your Land (Song)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-09-30T21:04:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Strauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe82bb7d-738f-52f4-bf0f-e6086bf37ba8', 'word_count': 1203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe82bb7d-738f-52f4-bf0f-e6086bf37ba8'}, {'abstract': 'The company’s fall season has been bounteous with repertory by its founder-choreographer, George Balanchine, and features exciting performances.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/01/arts/dance/women-fill-new-york-city-ballets-season-with-splendor.html', 'snippet': 'The company’s fall season has been bounteous with repertory by its founder-choreographer, George Balanchine, and features exciting performances.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s hard to tear yourself away from New York City Ballet just now, in particular from its many excellent ballerinas. The company, almost halfway through its four-week fall season, is being characteristically bounteous with repertory by its founder-choreographer, George Balanchine, which in turn is bounteous with ballerina roles. A few of the women cast in Balanchine parts are too tame, too weak, too passive; but all the troupe’s three ranks (principal, soloist, corps) contain women whose vivid individuality excites. Two in particular — Tiler Peck and Sara Mearns — set peak standards of musicality that enrich the entire art, showing the mysterious connection between space and music at its most fascinating.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/01/arts/01NYCB/01NYCB-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/01/arts/01NYCB/01NYCB-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/01/arts/01NYCB/01NYCB-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/01/arts/01NYCB/01NYCB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 598, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/01/arts/01NYCB/01NYCB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 598}}, {'ran